1
00:00:01,102 --> 00:00:03,237
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:03,270 --> 00:00:06,473
♪ NEXT SUNDAY, A.D. ♪

3
00:00:06,507 --> 00:00:09,310
♪ THERE WAS A GUY
NAMED JOEL ♪

4
00:00:09,343 --> 00:00:12,813
♪ NOT TOO DIFFERENT
FROM YOU OR ME ♪

5
00:00:12,847 --> 00:00:15,683
♪ HE WORKED
AT GIZMONIC INSTITUTE ♪

6
00:00:15,717 --> 00:00:19,120
♪ JUST ANOTHER FACE
IN A RED JUMPSUIT ♪

7
00:00:19,153 --> 00:00:21,655
♪ HE DID A GOOD JOB
CLEANING UP THE PLACE ♪

8
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,458
♪ BUT HIS BOSSES
DIDN'T LIKE HIM ♪

9
00:00:23,492 --> 00:00:25,893
♪ SO THEY SHOT HIM
INTO SPACE ♪

10
00:00:28,195 --> 00:00:31,332
♪ WE'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

11
00:00:31,365 --> 00:00:34,535
- ♪ THE WORST WE CAN FIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

12
00:00:34,568 --> 00:00:37,405
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

13
00:00:37,438 --> 00:00:40,675
- ♪ AND WE'LL MONITOR HIS MIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

14
00:00:40,708 --> 00:00:43,712
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND
JOEL CAN'T CONTROL ♪

15
00:00:43,745 --> 00:00:46,915
- ♪ WHERE THE MOVIES
BEGIN OR END ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

16
00:00:46,948 --> 00:00:50,118
♪ BECAUSE HE USED
THOSE SPECIAL PARTS ♪

17
00:00:50,152 --> 00:00:53,087
♪ TO MAKE HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

18
00:00:54,755 --> 00:00:56,623
LET'S GO.

19
00:00:56,657 --> 00:00:57,925
- CAMBOT.
- PAN LEFT.

20
00:00:57,958 --> 00:00:59,227
HI, GIRL.

21
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:01,095
WHAT A COOL GUY.

22
00:01:01,128 --> 00:01:02,663
A WISECRACKER.

23
00:01:02,697 --> 00:01:05,667
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING HOW
HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

24
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:08,503
- ♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

25
00:01:08,537 --> 00:01:11,538
♪ THEN REPEAT TO YOURSELF
"IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

26
00:01:11,572 --> 00:01:14,908
♪ "I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX ♪

27
00:01:14,942 --> 00:01:17,778
♪ FOR..." ♪

28
00:01:30,725 --> 00:01:33,427
♪ MAD ABOUT THE BOY ♪

29
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:35,330
♪ DAH-DIN DA-DA-DEE ♪

30
00:01:35,363 --> 00:01:37,165
♪ MAD ABOUT THE BOY ♪

31
00:01:37,198 --> 00:01:38,933
HA-HA,
WHAT A CUTE SHAPE ON ME.

32
00:01:38,967 --> 00:01:40,768
HUH? CHECK ME OUT, EH? WHOO.

33
00:01:40,802 --> 00:01:42,703
THERE YOU GO, ALL DONE.

34
00:01:42,737 --> 00:01:46,007
AH, TODAY I AM
A REAL LIVE BOY. MAZEL TOV!

35
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:47,742
HEY, HI, CROW.
HI TOM.

36
00:01:47,775 --> 00:01:50,077
HI, EVERYBODY, WELCOME
TO THE SATELLITE OF LOVE.

37
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,812
I'M JOEL ROBINSON.
YOU MIGHT REMEMBER ME

38
00:01:51,845 --> 00:01:54,382
AS THE GUY WHO WAS
ACCIDENTALLY SHOT INTO SPACE

39
00:01:54,415 --> 00:01:56,250
AND THEN F-- THE HELL?

40
00:01:56,283 --> 00:01:57,785
TOM SERVO, YOU'RE NAKED.

41
00:01:57,818 --> 00:01:59,320
NAKED AND BEAUTIFUL, JOEL.

42
00:01:59,353 --> 00:02:01,622
THE HUMAN BODY IN ALL
ITS MANY SHAPES AND SIZES

43
00:02:01,655 --> 00:02:02,890
IS A WONDER TO BEHOLD.

44
00:02:02,923 --> 00:02:04,392
TODAY I BEGIN ANEW.

45
00:02:04,425 --> 00:02:06,293
NO LONGER TOM SERVO,
MERE ROBOT.

46
00:02:06,327 --> 00:02:08,362
I EMERGE FROM
MY METAL CHRYSALIS.

47
00:02:08,395 --> 00:02:10,832
TOM SERVO, REAL LIVE BOY.

48
00:02:10,865 --> 00:02:13,033
SNIPS AND SNAILS
AND PUPPY DOG'S TAILS.

49
00:02:13,067 --> 00:02:14,768
THAT'S WHAT TOMMY'S MADE OF.

50
00:02:14,802 --> 00:02:16,570
- YEAH, REALLY.
- UH, NO, PAINT ACTUALLY.

51
00:02:16,603 --> 00:02:18,907
YEAH, TOM, YOU KNOW, I KNEW
THIS WAS GONNA HAPPEN SOMETIME.

52
00:02:18,940 --> 00:02:20,942
YOU'RE EXPERIENCING
THE PINOCCHIO SYNDROME.

53
00:02:20,975 --> 00:02:22,577
OH, NONSENSE, BROTHER.

54
00:02:22,610 --> 00:02:25,012
IT HAS ALWAYS BEEN MY DREAM
TO BE A REAL LIVE BOY.

55
00:02:25,045 --> 00:02:27,148
AND NOW I AM THAT THING.

56
00:02:27,182 --> 00:02:29,283
BUT, TOM, WHY DO YOU WANT
TO BE A REAL LIVE BOY?

57
00:02:29,317 --> 00:02:31,152
THERE ARE BILLIONS
OF REAL LIVE BOYS ON EARTH.

58
00:02:31,185 --> 00:02:32,953
THERE'S ONLY ONE TOM SERVO.

59
00:02:32,987 --> 00:02:35,390
I WANT TO RUN AND JUMP
AND SKIN MY KNEES.

60
00:02:35,423 --> 00:02:36,723
UH, YOU DON'T HAVE ANY LEGS.

61
00:02:36,757 --> 00:02:39,160
I WANT TO CATCH FROGS DOWN
AT THE OLD SWIMMING HOLE.

62
00:02:39,193 --> 00:02:41,262
- YOUR ARMS DON'T WORK.
- I WANT TO EXPERIENCE

63
00:02:41,295 --> 00:02:42,663
A WORLD OF EMOTIONS
AND FEELINGS.

64
00:02:42,697 --> 00:02:44,198
YOU'LL GET BEAT UP
BECAUSE YOU'RE A FREAK.

65
00:02:44,232 --> 00:02:46,733
- [SERVO SOBS]
- FIVE SECONDS
TO COMMERCIAL SIGN.

66
00:02:46,767 --> 00:02:48,402
NOW I KNOW I'M A REAL BOY.

67
00:02:48,435 --> 00:02:50,137
I CAN HEAR
MY HEART BREAKING.

68
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:52,707
- IT'S OKAY. IT'S OKAY.
- COMMERCIAL SIGN NOW.

69
00:02:52,740 --> 00:02:55,577
SITTING HERE, SMILING,
WATCHING TOMMY GROW.

70
00:02:55,610 --> 00:02:56,710
UH, I'M STILL WET, YOU KNOW.

71
00:02:56,743 --> 00:02:58,345
- OH. OOH.
- I THINK YOU'RE STUCK.

72
00:03:05,753 --> 00:03:07,255
GEE, UH, SERVO, YOU'RE GONNA
HAVE TO TOUCH UP YOUR SKIN.

73
00:03:07,288 --> 00:03:08,823
I CAN SEE THAT, DON'T YOU
THINK I CAN SEE THAT?

74
00:03:08,857 --> 00:03:10,392
HERE, SPIT.

75
00:03:10,425 --> 00:03:11,658
THAT'S REALLY PINK,
ISN'T IT?

76
00:03:11,692 --> 00:03:14,495
YEAH-- OH, BUFFY
AND HILDEGARD ARE CALLING.

77
00:03:14,528 --> 00:03:18,365
OH, JOEL, THE STORIES
I COULD TELL OF...

78
00:03:18,398 --> 00:03:20,835
FRENZIED BACHELOR PARTIES
AND EXOTIC DANCERS

79
00:03:20,868 --> 00:03:23,570
JUMPING OUT OF CAKES.
SOUNDS EXCITING?

80
00:03:23,603 --> 00:03:24,838
SURE.

81
00:03:24,872 --> 00:03:26,740
BUT AROUND MIDNIGHT,
THERE YOU ARE.

82
00:03:26,773 --> 00:03:28,208
FRUSTRATED
AND DISAPPOINTED

83
00:03:28,242 --> 00:03:29,877
WITH A FAKE CAKE
YOU CAN'T EAT

84
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:31,947
AND A DANCER NAMED CANDY
WHO HAS TO LEAVE

85
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:33,347
TO DRIVE HER
BABY-SITTER HOME.

86
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:35,283
- WHAT'VE YOU GOT?
- NOTHING.

87
00:03:35,317 --> 00:03:37,218
THAT'S WHY WE'VE
COMBINED DESSERT

88
00:03:37,252 --> 00:03:39,320
AND OBJECTIFYING
THE HUMAN BODY

89
00:03:39,353 --> 00:03:41,388
IN ONE EASY CAKE MIX.

90
00:03:41,422 --> 00:03:42,590
CAKE AND SHAKE.

91
00:03:42,623 --> 00:03:45,258
A REAL EXOTIC DANCER
INCLUDED.

92
00:03:45,292 --> 00:03:46,660
THAT'S RIGHT, CLAY.

93
00:03:46,693 --> 00:03:49,663
NOW GLUTTONY AND EXPLOITATION
SERVES EIGHT.

94
00:03:49,697 --> 00:03:52,500
AND JUST THINK, NOW EVEN MOM,
DAD, AND THE KIDS

95
00:03:52,533 --> 00:03:54,168
CAN ENJOY
A CHIPPENDALE DANCER

96
00:03:54,202 --> 00:03:56,337
AT LITTLE JIMMY'S
SEVENTH BIRTHDAY PARTY.

97
00:03:56,370 --> 00:03:59,840
- OH, CLAY?
- HMM?

98
00:03:59,873 --> 00:04:01,708
CAN I TEMPT YOU
WITH SOME DESSERT?

99
00:04:01,742 --> 00:04:03,945
OH, FRANK,
THIS LOOKS WONDERFUL.

100
00:04:03,978 --> 00:04:05,547
YOU'VE OUTDONE YOURSELF.

101
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:06,780
JUST A SLIVER.

102
00:04:06,813 --> 00:04:08,382
OH, IT WAS NOTHING.

103
00:04:08,415 --> 00:04:10,885
I MERELY FOLLOWED
THE EASY-TO-READ INSTRUCTIONS

104
00:04:10,918 --> 00:04:12,053
RIGHT ON THE BOX.

105
00:04:12,087 --> 00:04:13,553
AND, HEY, HERE'S A TIP.

106
00:04:13,587 --> 00:04:16,957
JUST FOLD THE EXOTIC DANCER
RIGHT INTO THE CAKE.

107
00:04:16,990 --> 00:04:18,358
THAT WAY, YOU SAVE A STEP.

108
00:04:18,392 --> 00:04:20,762
YOU DON'T HAVE TO WAIT
FOR THE CAKE TO FINISH BAKING.

109
00:04:20,795 --> 00:04:22,263
I'LL REMEMBER THAT
FOR MY CAKE

110
00:04:22,297 --> 00:04:24,432
FOR THE NEXT BAKE S--
YOU WHAT?!

111
00:04:24,465 --> 00:04:26,100
YOU BAKED A PERSON IN IT?

112
00:04:26,133 --> 00:04:27,668
AN HOUR AT 350?

113
00:04:27,702 --> 00:04:29,470
D'OH, START DIGGING, FRANK!

114
00:04:29,503 --> 00:04:30,705
I GET THE ROSE--

115
00:04:30,738 --> 00:04:32,673
JUST DIG, DUNCAN-HINEDER!

116
00:04:32,707 --> 00:04:34,175
[ALL GASP]

117
00:04:34,208 --> 00:04:35,343
OH, IT'S BEEFCAKE.

118
00:04:35,377 --> 00:04:36,910
- HEY.
- SEE, 'CAUSE HE'S--

119
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:39,113
HUSH. ANYWAY, SIRS,

120
00:04:39,147 --> 00:04:40,782
OUR INVENTION THIS WEEK
IS BASED

121
00:04:40,815 --> 00:04:42,750
ON THE OLD AMERICAN
TRADITION--

122
00:04:42,783 --> 00:04:43,985
THE JUNK DRAWER.

123
00:04:44,018 --> 00:04:46,487
YEAH, HEY, DID YOU KNOW
THAT BENJAMIN FRANKLIN

124
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:47,688
INVENTED THE JUNK DRAWER?

125
00:04:47,722 --> 00:04:49,390
AND WERE HE ALIVE TODAY,

126
00:04:49,423 --> 00:04:51,858
HE MIGHT'VE INVENTED
THE NEW AMERICAN TRADITION,

127
00:04:51,892 --> 00:04:53,327
THE JUNK DRAWER ORGANIZER.

128
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:55,262
- AAH.
- FINALLY, THERE'S
A PLACE IN THIS WORLD

129
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:57,698
FOR THOSE STRANGE KEYS,
KETCHUP PACKETS,

130
00:04:57,732 --> 00:04:59,967
THAT LINOLEUM KNIFE WITH
THE POINT BROKEN OFF.

131
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,902
ALL THOSE THINGS THAT,
UNTIL NOW,

132
00:05:01,935 --> 00:05:03,938
HAVE DEFIED THE LAWS
OF SEQUENTIAL OCCURRENCE

133
00:05:03,972 --> 00:05:05,440
IN SPACE AND TIME.

134
00:05:05,473 --> 00:05:06,840
YEAH, AND HOW MANY TIMES

135
00:05:06,873 --> 00:05:08,710
HAVE YOU GONE ROOTING
THROUGH YOUR JUNK DRAWER

136
00:05:08,743 --> 00:05:11,245
MUTTERING TO YOURSELF,
"WHERE'D I PUT THAT GUN?"

137
00:05:11,278 --> 00:05:13,447
WELL, NOW THERE'S
A PLACE FOR IT.

138
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:16,217
AND-- AND THERE'S A PLACE
FOR ROUND BAND-AIDS,

139
00:05:16,250 --> 00:05:19,353
AND FOR THAT HANDFUL OF GRAVEL
THAT MIGHT BE AGATE,

140
00:05:19,387 --> 00:05:20,588
AND YOUR SHOEHORN,

141
00:05:20,622 --> 00:05:22,157
AND THOSE TWO-INCH
PIECES OF STRING

142
00:05:22,190 --> 00:05:23,490
THAT MIGHT
COME IN HANDY SOMEDAY.

143
00:05:23,523 --> 00:05:25,993
MM-HMM, HEY, THERE'S EVEN
A SEPARATE COMPARTMENT

144
00:05:26,027 --> 00:05:28,362
FOR MISCELLANEOUS
GRIT AND LINT.

145
00:05:28,395 --> 00:05:29,730
ALREADY BUILT-IN.

146
00:05:29,763 --> 00:05:31,098
SO YOU DON'T HAVE TO!

147
00:05:31,132 --> 00:05:32,267
- HUH?
- HUH?

148
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:33,533
WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

149
00:05:33,567 --> 00:05:36,370
WE COULD GET INTO A LOT
OF TROUBLE FOR THIS, FRANK.

150
00:05:36,403 --> 00:05:38,305
OH, JOEL, UM.

151
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:41,375
UH, EVERYTHING'S FINE.
NOTHING TO SEE HERE.

152
00:05:41,408 --> 00:05:43,745
YOUR FEATURE PRESENTATION

153
00:05:43,778 --> 00:05:46,680
IS A FILM CALLED
I ACCUSE MY PARENTS.

154
00:05:46,713 --> 00:05:48,315
UH, YOU FIGURE IT OUT.

155
00:05:48,348 --> 00:05:51,718
ENJOY IT WITH THE SHORT
ABOUT TRUCK FARMING.

156
00:05:51,752 --> 00:05:53,620
WE'RE HAVE TO ANSWER TO THE
CHIPPENDALE CORPORATION

157
00:05:53,653 --> 00:05:55,523
- FOR THIS, FRANK!
- OH, HEY.

158
00:05:55,557 --> 00:05:57,825
THE JAWS OF LIFE, MAN!
GET THE JAWS OF LIFE!

159
00:05:57,858 --> 00:06:00,462
- CAKE?
- [ALL GASP]

160
00:06:00,495 --> 00:06:01,595
- I'M BETTER.
- [ALARM BLARES]

161
00:06:01,628 --> 00:06:03,630
[ALL] MOVIE SIGN!

162
00:06:15,643 --> 00:06:17,912
EASTER BUNNY FILMS PRESENTS.

163
00:06:20,413 --> 00:06:22,317
TRUCK FARMER--
THE SPECIAL EDITION.

164
00:06:22,350 --> 00:06:24,152
INCLUDES SCENES THE STUDIO
ORIGINALLY THOUGHT

165
00:06:24,185 --> 00:06:27,622
TOO GRAPHIC FOR AUDIENCES.

166
00:06:27,655 --> 00:06:29,857
WONDER IF THEY SOLD THIS FILM
DOOR TO DOOR.

167
00:06:29,890 --> 00:06:32,360
[MIMIC HORSE HOOFS]

168
00:06:35,395 --> 00:06:37,565
- OH, THE DONNER PARTY.
- [NARRATOR] LESS THAN
A CENTURY AGO,

169
00:06:37,598 --> 00:06:39,333
OUR FOREFATHERS MOVED WEST

170
00:06:39,367 --> 00:06:41,468
ACROSS THE VAST
AND FERTILE PLAINS

171
00:06:41,502 --> 00:06:42,537
OF OUR GROWING NATION.

172
00:06:42,570 --> 00:06:45,438
HUNTING FOR GOOD LAND.

173
00:06:45,472 --> 00:06:48,008
SEARCHING FOR
A PLACE TO FARM.

174
00:06:48,042 --> 00:06:49,710
[ALL] HELP US!

175
00:06:49,743 --> 00:06:52,713
--TIME AS ROMANTIC AND
EXCITING.

176
00:06:52,747 --> 00:06:55,550
MOST OF US THINK THAT THESE
PEOPLE WERE REALLY FREE.

177
00:06:55,583 --> 00:06:56,783
BUT THEY WERE JUST STUPID.

178
00:06:56,817 --> 00:06:59,687
--THEY WERE RESTRICTED
IN MANY WAYS.

179
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:01,488
TODAY WE TAKE A NUMBER
OF FOODS FOR GRANTED--

180
00:07:01,522 --> 00:07:04,325
♪ SURREY,
CROSS THE GUERNSEY ♪

181
00:07:04,358 --> 00:07:06,993
--THEY ATE LITTLE
BUT MEAT AND STAPLES.

182
00:07:07,027 --> 00:07:09,530
HERE'S A FIVE-INCH NAIL
FOR DESSERT. GO NUTS.

183
00:07:09,563 --> 00:07:12,667
--MEANT THE END OF MOST
FRESH VEGETABLES.

184
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:15,235
THEIR OPPORTUNITIES
FOR A BALANCED DIET

185
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:17,103
DISAPPEARED.

186
00:07:17,137 --> 00:07:18,873
INSTEAD THEY ATE
THE YELLOW SNOW.

187
00:07:18,907 --> 00:07:21,542
--SNOW COVERS THE NORTHERN
PART OF OUR COUNTRY.

188
00:07:21,575 --> 00:07:24,178
- PEOPLE DIE.
- --GREAT TRUCK
FARMING AREAS

189
00:07:24,212 --> 00:07:25,980
SUPPLY THE CONSTANT DEMAND

190
00:07:26,013 --> 00:07:28,815
FOR FRESH VEGETABLES.

191
00:07:28,848 --> 00:07:31,552
FLORIDA IS ONE
OF THE AREAS.

192
00:07:31,585 --> 00:07:34,355
EVEN DURING BITTER
NORTHERN WINTER,

193
00:07:34,388 --> 00:07:37,192
HARVESTING
GOES ON IN FLORIDA.

194
00:07:37,225 --> 00:07:40,393
THESE SELECT FEW ARE MAKING
THREE CENTS A DAY.

195
00:07:40,427 --> 00:07:43,330
LET'S TAKE YOU BACK TO
THE DAYS WHEN DDT WAS SAFE.

196
00:07:46,667 --> 00:07:48,302
AND IN CALIFORNIA,

197
00:07:48,335 --> 00:07:50,638
IN THE SALINAS VALLEY
AND OTHER AREAS,

198
00:07:50,672 --> 00:07:53,773
LETTUCE FOR THE SALADS
AND SANDWICHES OF A NATION

199
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:55,977
IS HARVESTED FRESH
IN WINTERTIME.

200
00:07:56,010 --> 00:07:58,345
OH, YOU KNOW,
EVERYTHING LOOKS SO GOOD

201
00:07:58,378 --> 00:07:59,780
ON THIS SALAD BAR.

202
00:07:59,813 --> 00:08:02,217
OH HEAVENS YES, EVERYTHING
LOOKS SO FRESH AND DELIGHTFUL.

203
00:08:02,250 --> 00:08:03,783
I'M JUST GONNA HAVE
A SMALL SALAD,

204
00:08:03,817 --> 00:08:07,053
MAYBE SOME SOUP, AND THEN
TREAT MYSELF TO SOME FRO-YO.

205
00:08:09,157 --> 00:08:11,192
OH, WHERE ELSE
ARE PEOPLE EXPLOITED?

206
00:08:11,225 --> 00:08:13,093
WHY-- DOWN ON
THE SOUTHERN BORDER.

207
00:08:13,127 --> 00:08:14,595
--SKILLED HANDS
SHAKE BUNDLES

208
00:08:14,628 --> 00:08:17,332
OF FRESH CARROTS
IN JANUARY.

209
00:08:17,365 --> 00:08:19,300
IN RECENT DECADES,
TRUCK FARMING

210
00:08:19,333 --> 00:08:20,902
HAS BECOME BIG BUSINESS.

211
00:08:20,935 --> 00:08:22,903
BUT NOT FOR THESE PEOPLE.

212
00:08:22,937 --> 00:08:24,905
A LOT OF FACTORS HELP.

213
00:08:24,938 --> 00:08:26,240
BUT NO ONE CAN DENY

214
00:08:26,273 --> 00:08:29,410
THE IMPORTANT ROLE
OF POWER MACHINERY.

215
00:08:29,443 --> 00:08:33,080
AAH! IT'S KILLDOZER!
CLINT WALKER, NO!

216
00:08:33,113 --> 00:08:36,517
HERE, THOUSANDS OF ACRES
OF RAINFOREST ARE CLEARED AWAY.

217
00:08:36,550 --> 00:08:37,652
WHO CARES?

218
00:08:37,685 --> 00:08:41,388
STUPID TREES.
GOD, I HATE 'EM.

219
00:08:41,422 --> 00:08:44,092
EARLY TRACTOR PULLS.
NOT THAT MUCH FUN.

220
00:08:44,125 --> 00:08:47,027
THIS IS THE FREESTYLE
COMPETITION.

221
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:48,828
DON'T SEE MANY
OF THESE TREES ANYMORE.

222
00:08:48,862 --> 00:08:50,430
WELL, DOWN IT GOES.

223
00:08:50,463 --> 00:08:52,567
THE SAD THING IS THIS GUY
DOESN'T EVEN WORK FOR ANYBODY.

224
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,335
HE'S JUST DOING THIS
FOR KICKS.

225
00:08:56,937 --> 00:08:59,807
WELL, HERE AS
ANOINTED BY GOD,

226
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:03,410
MAN HOLDS DOMINION
OVER HIS EARTH.

227
00:09:03,443 --> 00:09:05,713
BY HAND,
THE LAND WOULD'VE TAKEN

228
00:09:05,747 --> 00:09:07,815
WEEKS OF HARD LABOR
TO CLEAR.

229
00:09:07,848 --> 00:09:10,283
- STICK FARMERS.
- BUT NOW TREES AND BRUSH

230
00:09:10,317 --> 00:09:12,820
CAN BE CLEARED
AND BURNED IN DAYS.

231
00:09:12,853 --> 00:09:14,455
- WELL, THAT'S CHEERFUL.
- AND THE LAND

232
00:09:14,488 --> 00:09:15,657
READIED FOR THE PLOW.

233
00:09:15,690 --> 00:09:18,225
SPEED THE PLOW.

234
00:09:18,258 --> 00:09:20,593
I'M THINKING OF TELLING
MY WIFE I LOVE HER.

235
00:09:20,627 --> 00:09:23,030
NAH, FORGET IT.
NOT WORTH IT.

236
00:09:23,063 --> 00:09:25,432
- ♪ GO SPEED FARMER ♪
- [ALL] ♪ GO SPEED FARMER ♪

237
00:09:25,465 --> 00:09:28,102
[ALL]
♪ GO SPEED FARMER GO ♪

238
00:09:28,135 --> 00:09:30,603
AFTER PLOWING,
A SEED BED IS PREPARED

239
00:09:30,637 --> 00:09:32,607
BY A MODERN DISK HARROW.

240
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:35,275
BREAKING UP
THE CLODS OF EARTH.

241
00:09:35,308 --> 00:09:36,577
THERE'S SOMETHING
YOU DON'T SEE EVERY DAY.

242
00:09:36,610 --> 00:09:38,645
- WHAT'S THAT?
- A FARMER WITH ALL HIS LIMBS.

243
00:09:38,678 --> 00:09:40,648
SORRY.

244
00:09:40,682 --> 00:09:43,683
[BOTS MIMIC QUACK-LIKE MUSIC]

245
00:09:43,717 --> 00:09:46,853
NOW, DUCK NEWS.
HERE'S HUGH McQUACKEN.

246
00:09:46,887 --> 00:09:48,522
- HARROWING, ISN'T IT?
- D'OH.

247
00:09:48,555 --> 00:09:50,190
HARROWING CAUSE--
FARMER JOKE.

248
00:09:50,223 --> 00:09:54,028
AND THEN PLANTING
AND FERTILIZING.

249
00:09:54,062 --> 00:09:57,230
FERTILIZER, WHICH NOT ONLY
INCREASES THE YIELD

250
00:09:57,263 --> 00:09:59,967
BUT ADDS TO THE FOOD VALUE
OF THE VEGETABLE,

251
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,103
IS ADDED TO THE SOIL
THROUGH ONE SET OF HOPPERS.

252
00:10:03,137 --> 00:10:06,040
WHILE THE OTHER SET OF HOPPERS
PLANTS THE SEED.

253
00:10:06,073 --> 00:10:07,375
AND REMEMBER, BE SURE TO USE

254
00:10:07,408 --> 00:10:09,977
LOTS AND LOTS OF CHEMICALS
FOR A GOOD CROP.

255
00:10:11,378 --> 00:10:12,647
EVEN CULTIVATING IS DONE

256
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:15,048
WITH THE HELP
OF MODERN MACHINERY.

257
00:10:15,082 --> 00:10:16,550
IN SOME PLACES,

258
00:10:16,583 --> 00:10:19,687
A ROTARY HOE IS USED
TO DESTROY WEEDS.

259
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:22,088
YOU KNOW, I SAW THAT
ON CHILDREN OF THE CORN.

260
00:10:25,927 --> 00:10:27,327
MOST FARMERS
LIKE TO LISTEN

261
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:29,797
TO IGOR STRAVINSKY
WHEN THEY FARM.

262
00:10:29,830 --> 00:10:32,433
BUT WHERE MECHANICAL MEANS
ARE DANGEROUS,

263
00:10:32,467 --> 00:10:35,235
CHEMICAL CULTIVATION
IS OFTEN USED.

264
00:10:35,268 --> 00:10:37,203
ESPECIALLY
SELECTED CHEMICALS

265
00:10:37,237 --> 00:10:38,572
THAT DESTROY WEEDS
WITHOUT--

266
00:10:38,605 --> 00:10:40,207
- [ALL COUGH]
- --INJURING VEGETABLES,

267
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:44,045
- --ARE SPRAYED IN THE FIELDS.
- ♪ HOORAY FOR CHEMICALS ♪

268
00:10:44,078 --> 00:10:45,747
HERE IN SOUTHERN TEXAS,

269
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:47,382
THERE IS AN
ADDITIONAL PROBLEM.

270
00:10:47,415 --> 00:10:50,583
- TEXANS.
- ADEQUATE SUPPLIES
OF WATER.

271
00:10:50,617 --> 00:10:53,287
THE RIO GRANDE, WITH
THE HELP OF THE TRUCK FARMER,

272
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:55,322
MAKES UP FOR
THE SCANTY AMOUNT OF RAIN.

273
00:10:55,355 --> 00:10:57,257
YEAH, LET ME HARNESS
THIS THING HERE--

274
00:10:57,290 --> 00:10:59,660
WELL, I'LL BE DAMNED!
I'M IN MEXICO.

275
00:10:59,693 --> 00:11:01,362
[SERVO HUMS]

276
00:11:01,395 --> 00:11:03,130
- UP RIVER, A HUGE DAM
- [CROW SPITS]

277
00:11:03,163 --> 00:11:05,733
ENSURES A CONSTANT SUPPLY
OF WATER THE YEAR ROUND.

278
00:11:05,767 --> 00:11:07,402
THE TY-D-BOL MAN.

279
00:11:07,435 --> 00:11:09,470
A COMPLICATED SYSTEM
OF IRRIGATION IS USED.

280
00:11:09,503 --> 00:11:11,138
OH, REAL COMPLICATED.

281
00:11:11,172 --> 00:11:13,040
GREAT CARE IS TAKEN
TO SEE THAT

282
00:11:13,073 --> 00:11:15,275
NONE OF THE PRECIOUS WATER
IS WASTED.

283
00:11:15,308 --> 00:11:19,012
I WANTED TO BE
A CHOREOGRAPHER.

284
00:11:19,045 --> 00:11:22,817
OH, THIS IS AN ARTISTIC VIEW
OF FARMING.

285
00:11:22,850 --> 00:11:24,585
[CROW COUGHS]

286
00:11:24,618 --> 00:11:26,887
- I LOVE YOU, EARL.
- UH, NOT HERE, TOM.

287
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:29,623
- I LOVE YOU.
- NO. OH.

288
00:11:29,657 --> 00:11:32,927
CHARLEY VARRICK IS EMPLOYED.

289
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:34,262
- ON LARGE FARMS,
- [SERVO COUGHS]

290
00:11:34,295 --> 00:11:36,397
THE SPEED AND VERSATILITY
OF THE AIRPLANE

291
00:11:36,430 --> 00:11:39,167
IS OFTEN USED
TO CONTROL INSECT PESTS

292
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:42,537
BY QUICKLY DUSTING
WIDE AREAS.

293
00:11:42,570 --> 00:11:45,973
SOME FARMS USE MECHANICAL
SPRAYERS IN THE FIELDS.

294
00:11:46,007 --> 00:11:47,475
THERE'S NOTHING
WE CAN'T SPRAY.

295
00:11:47,508 --> 00:11:49,777
FINALLY, PLANTS RIPEN.

296
00:11:52,613 --> 00:11:54,282
NOW, THIS TOMATO
IS HIGHLY DEFORMED,

297
00:11:54,315 --> 00:11:56,550
BUT CUT OFF THE EYES,
AND IT'S GOOD EATING.

298
00:11:59,153 --> 00:12:00,855
THE LAST FEW DAYS OF GROWTH

299
00:12:00,888 --> 00:12:02,557
BRING THE VEGETABLES
TO THEIR PEAK.

300
00:12:02,590 --> 00:12:05,960
I'M PEAKIN', MAN.

301
00:12:05,993 --> 00:12:08,162
THE FIELDS
FILL WITH PEOPLE,

302
00:12:08,195 --> 00:12:09,930
AND A COMPLEX SYSTEM
OF HARVESTING

303
00:12:09,963 --> 00:12:11,498
GOES INTO HIGH GEAR.

304
00:12:11,532 --> 00:12:13,900
LYNDON JOHNSON.

305
00:12:13,933 --> 00:12:15,468
- HERE.
- RIPENING TOMATOES--

306
00:12:15,502 --> 00:12:17,170
- PUT 'EM IN THE BASKET.
- --ARE CAREFULLY PICKED--

307
00:12:17,203 --> 00:12:18,905
- I GIVE UP.
- --BY EXPERIENCED HANDS.

308
00:12:22,275 --> 00:12:23,777
UH, ONE.

309
00:12:23,810 --> 00:12:25,178
TWO.

310
00:12:25,212 --> 00:12:26,513
THREE.

311
00:12:26,547 --> 00:12:27,982
FOUR.

312
00:12:28,015 --> 00:12:30,117
- FIVE.
- --INCOME FROM THE SALE OF--

313
00:12:30,150 --> 00:12:31,985
- FIVE.
- --PEAS AND OTHER VEGETABLES

314
00:12:32,018 --> 00:12:35,222
AVERAGES MORE THAN A BILLION
AND A HALF DOLLARS A YEAR.

315
00:12:35,255 --> 00:12:36,757
BUT HE'LL SEE NONE OF IT!

316
00:12:36,790 --> 00:12:38,325
-- GOES TO TRUCK FARMERS

317
00:12:38,358 --> 00:12:41,528
- WHO RAISE
WINTER VEGETABLES.
- I'M SO HAPPY.

318
00:12:41,562 --> 00:12:44,698
ANNUAL FARM INCOME PRODUCED
BY VEGETABLES ALONE

319
00:12:44,732 --> 00:12:46,233
IS NEARLY AS GREAT AS

320
00:12:46,267 --> 00:12:47,935
YEARLY FARM INCOME PRODUCED

321
00:12:47,968 --> 00:12:49,903
BY THE SALE
OF BREAD GRAINS.

322
00:12:49,937 --> 00:12:51,772
COME ON, WORK,
DAMN IT, WORK.

323
00:12:51,805 --> 00:12:55,275
YOU GOT A BEAN
IN YOUR POCKET, I KNOW IT.

324
00:12:55,308 --> 00:12:58,678
OH, TAKE YOUR TIME, AL.

325
00:12:58,712 --> 00:13:01,515
MANY TRUCK CROPS,
LIKE CARROTS,

326
00:13:01,548 --> 00:13:03,950
ARE HARVESTED
BY HAND LABOR.

327
00:13:03,983 --> 00:13:07,788
CHEAP, ABUSED HAND LABOR.

328
00:13:07,822 --> 00:13:09,890
HERE IN THE
RIO GRANDE DELTA,

329
00:13:09,923 --> 00:13:12,258
MEXICAN CITIZENS
WHO CROSS THE BORDER

330
00:13:12,292 --> 00:13:14,495
ON TEMPORARY
WORK PERMITS HELP.

331
00:13:14,528 --> 00:13:16,730
THEY MAKE IT SOUND SO NICE.

332
00:13:16,763 --> 00:13:20,733
I'M FROM CANADA--
WHAT AM I DOING HERE?

333
00:13:20,767 --> 00:13:22,368
A PRE-TEEN IS PUT TO WORK.

334
00:13:22,402 --> 00:13:25,405
HER BEAUTY WILL SOON FADE.

335
00:13:25,438 --> 00:13:27,908
WHILE SOME CARROTS ARE
TOPPED IN THE FIELD

336
00:13:27,942 --> 00:13:30,177
AND SENT TO MARKET
IN PLIOFILM BAGS.

337
00:13:30,210 --> 00:13:32,847
MANY ARE HARVESTED
AND PROCESSED INTACT.

338
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:35,082
OH, THE GREAT HANK
GETS TO WORK ON THE TRUCK.

339
00:13:35,115 --> 00:13:36,483
HEY, LAY OFF,
I'M SICK TODAY.

340
00:13:36,517 --> 00:13:37,752
[SERVO COUGHS]

341
00:13:37,785 --> 00:13:39,018
OH, LET'S SEE,
WHAT AM I GONNA HAVE

342
00:13:39,052 --> 00:13:40,420
OR DINNER TONIGHT? CAR--

343
00:13:40,453 --> 00:13:42,522
NO, NOT CARROTS.

344
00:13:42,555 --> 00:13:44,190
A RACE AGAINST TIME.

345
00:13:44,223 --> 00:13:47,327
WELL, HEY, I'M STACKING 'EM
AS FAST AS I CAN.

346
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:49,263
CARROTS ARE TAKEN
TO A PACKING PLANT

347
00:13:49,297 --> 00:13:51,098
WHERE A HIGHLY
MECHANIZED PROCESS

348
00:13:51,132 --> 00:13:53,167
OF PREPARATION
FOR MARKET BEGINS.

349
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:55,135
HERE, THEY ARE INTERROGATED.

350
00:13:55,168 --> 00:13:58,105
--ORGANIZED
ALONG FACTORY LINES.

351
00:13:58,138 --> 00:14:00,007
THE CARROTS
ARE WASHED FIRST.

352
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:03,443
THEY'RE MADE FLAVORLESS,
SO PEOPLE WILL BUY STEAK.

353
00:14:03,477 --> 00:14:05,478
WHEN THEY ARE TOPPED
IN THE FIELD,

354
00:14:05,512 --> 00:14:07,080
THE PROCESS IS RAPID.

355
00:14:07,113 --> 00:14:08,315
RABBIT?

356
00:14:08,348 --> 00:14:09,650
SOME, OF COURSE,
ARE CANNED.

357
00:14:09,683 --> 00:14:11,452
AND TURNED INTO
CARROT PAINT.

358
00:14:14,488 --> 00:14:16,690
SOME CARROTS ARE FROZEN.

359
00:14:16,723 --> 00:14:19,260
SOME CARROTS ARE
HUMILIATED PUBLICLY.

360
00:14:19,293 --> 00:14:21,962
UNTOPPED CARROTS ARE
PACKED WITH CHIPPED ICE

361
00:14:21,995 --> 00:14:23,497
TO ENSURE FRESHNESS.

362
00:14:23,530 --> 00:14:27,100
HIGH-ENERGY CARROT TOP'S
ALSO PACKED IN ICE.

363
00:14:27,133 --> 00:14:30,003
SOYLENT GREEN
IS MADE FROM PEOPLE!

364
00:14:33,673 --> 00:14:37,310
HMM. HEY, CAN I BORROW
YOUR FINGER A SECOND, LEN?

365
00:14:37,343 --> 00:14:39,580
- GOOD.
- DESPITE THE SPEED
AND EFFICIENCY

366
00:14:39,613 --> 00:14:40,847
OF THE PROCESS,

367
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:43,617
GREAT CARE IS TAKEN
WITH THE VEGETABLES.

368
00:14:43,650 --> 00:14:45,152
VARIED SKILLS ARE APPLIED

369
00:14:45,185 --> 00:14:47,087
AT ALL STAGES
OF THE PROCESS.

370
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:49,055
I LOVE MY RUBBER APRON.

371
00:14:49,088 --> 00:14:50,523
AN AUTOMATIC MACHINE

372
00:14:50,557 --> 00:14:52,225
- PUTS A TOP--
- [SERVO GROANS]

373
00:14:52,258 --> 00:14:54,595
AND THE FINISHED BOX
IS PASSED ALONG

374
00:14:54,628 --> 00:14:56,063
ON A SERIES OF ROLLERS

375
00:14:56,097 --> 00:14:59,467
DIRECTLY TO A REFRIGERATED
RAILROAD CAR.

376
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:01,435
WHERE IT IS LOADED
IMMEDIATELY.

377
00:15:01,468 --> 00:15:02,737
THEN SENT BACK TO THE FARM

378
00:15:02,770 --> 00:15:03,970
AND PUT BACK
INTO THE GROUND.

379
00:15:04,003 --> 00:15:06,007
IT ACTUALLY MAKES
NO SENSE WHATSOEVER.

380
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:08,475
MORE ICE IS POURED INTO
THE REFRIGERATOR CAR

381
00:15:08,508 --> 00:15:09,877
TO MAKE SURE THAT
THE CARROTS

382
00:15:09,910 --> 00:15:12,478
- ARE KEPT FRESH.
- NEAT.

383
00:15:12,512 --> 00:15:13,947
REFRIGERATION,

384
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:16,783
LIKE THE DEVELOPMENT
OF POWERED FARM MACHINERY,

385
00:15:16,817 --> 00:15:19,887
IS VITAL FOR LARGE-SCALE
TRUCK FARMING.

386
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:22,857
LATER, THIS DEVICE IS USED
TO BEAT BACK THE WORKERS.

387
00:15:22,890 --> 00:15:24,758
--IS RAPID TRANSPORTATION.

388
00:15:24,792 --> 00:15:26,693
- [SERVO LAUGHS]
- THE RACE TO MARKET

389
00:15:26,727 --> 00:15:28,262
ENTERS THE FINAL STAGES.

390
00:15:28,295 --> 00:15:30,397
UH, WE HAVEN'T WORKED OUT
ALL THE KINKS YET.

391
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:32,667
ALL OVER THE NORTHERN PART
OF THE NATION,

392
00:15:32,700 --> 00:15:34,668
IN THE CITIES AND TOWNS,

393
00:15:34,702 --> 00:15:36,103
THE DELIVERY
OF THESE PRODUCTS

394
00:15:36,137 --> 00:15:37,570
IS NOW
TAKEN FOR GRANTED.

395
00:15:37,603 --> 00:15:39,072
YES, THE SOUTH STARVES,

396
00:15:39,105 --> 00:15:40,507
WHILE THE NORTH
EATS HEALTHILY.

397
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:42,977
--TRUCK FARMING
IS A BIG BUSINESS.

398
00:15:43,010 --> 00:15:44,612
VITAL TO THE HEALTH
OF OUR NATION.

399
00:15:44,645 --> 00:15:46,080
WAIT A MINUTE-- HAS ANYBODY

400
00:15:46,113 --> 00:15:47,982
- SEEN A TRUCK YET?
- WITHOUT IT,

401
00:15:48,015 --> 00:15:50,083
THE BALANCED DIET
SO NECESSARY

402
00:15:50,117 --> 00:15:51,485
FOR OUR WELL-BEING

403
00:15:51,518 --> 00:15:53,453
WOULD BE DIFFICULT INDEED
TO ACHIEVE

404
00:15:53,487 --> 00:15:54,922
DURING THE WINTER MONTHS.

405
00:15:57,590 --> 00:16:00,427
AH, J. EDGAR HOOVER
GOES SHOPPING.

406
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:02,797
HMM, LET'S SEE.

407
00:16:02,830 --> 00:16:04,932
WELL, IT ISN'T MEAT,
BUT I SUPPOSE I'D BETTER

408
00:16:04,965 --> 00:16:06,733
BUY SOME OF THESE
JUST FOR APPEARANCES.

409
00:16:06,767 --> 00:16:09,268
[GASPS] CUCUMBERS.

410
00:16:09,302 --> 00:16:11,105
BECAUSE OF OUR
TRUCK FARMERS,

411
00:16:11,138 --> 00:16:12,605
THE VITAMINS AND MINERALS

412
00:16:12,638 --> 00:16:14,207
TO BE FOUND
IN FRESH VEGETABLES--

413
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:16,077
- ARE POISONED.
- --ARE NOW READILY
AVAILABLE

414
00:16:16,110 --> 00:16:17,812
ALL YEAR LONG.

415
00:16:17,845 --> 00:16:20,413
IN ALL PARTS OF OUR
VIGOROUS NATION.

416
00:16:20,447 --> 00:16:22,148
PRAISE THE TRUCK FARMER!

417
00:16:22,182 --> 00:16:23,683
BOW DOWN BEFORE HIM!

418
00:16:23,717 --> 00:16:26,120
WORSHIP THE TRUCK FARMER
AT THE CHURCH OF YOUR CHOICE.

419
00:16:26,153 --> 00:16:29,022
OFFER BURNT SACRIFICES
TO THE ALMIGHTY TRUCK FARMER!

420
00:16:29,055 --> 00:16:31,258
[ALL]
HAIL, TRUCK FARMER!

421
00:16:31,292 --> 00:16:33,593
HAIL, TRUCK FARMER!

422
00:16:33,627 --> 00:16:35,728
A-LALALALALALA!

423
00:16:44,270 --> 00:16:47,473
PENILE REPLACEMENT CORPORATION
PICTURES PRESENTS!

424
00:16:52,645 --> 00:16:55,215
TEAHOUSE
OF THE AUGUST MOON.

425
00:16:56,983 --> 00:16:59,318
THE JOHN BRADSHAW STORY.

426
00:17:05,058 --> 00:17:07,160
AS LONG AS IT'S NOT
JOHN HUGHES.

427
00:17:07,193 --> 00:17:09,062
- INDEED.
- YEAH.

428
00:17:09,095 --> 00:17:11,398
OH, ROBERT LOWELL, THE POET.

429
00:17:11,432 --> 00:17:13,533
HEY, WE DIDN'T
GET TO READ THE-- OH.

430
00:17:16,203 --> 00:17:18,938
MUSIC BY THE LITTLE RASCALS.

431
00:17:18,972 --> 00:17:22,642
OH, SONGS, I HOPE
THIS ISN'T A MUSICAL.

432
00:17:22,675 --> 00:17:24,043
[SERVO SINGS]
♪ THEY LAUGHED ♪

433
00:17:24,077 --> 00:17:26,247
♪ WHEN I ACCUSED
MY PARENTS ♪

434
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:29,015
♪ AND I KILLED THEM ♪

435
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:30,517
♪ LET'S SEE IF ♪

436
00:17:30,550 --> 00:17:32,018
♪ THEY'LL BE LAUGHING ♪

437
00:17:32,052 --> 00:17:34,353
♪ NOW... ♪

438
00:17:36,157 --> 00:17:37,925
DID YOU KNOW THAT
THE ROLE OF AL FRAZIER

439
00:17:37,958 --> 00:17:39,358
WAS THE MOST COVETED ROLE
AT THAT TIME?

440
00:17:39,392 --> 00:17:41,662
REALLY? WOW.

441
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:50,103
SAM NEWFIELD? HE DIRECTED
JUNGLE GODDESS.

442
00:17:50,137 --> 00:17:53,107
OH, WELL, TH-- AAH!

443
00:17:53,140 --> 00:17:55,375
PART FOUR,
CITIZENS ON PATROL!

444
00:17:58,012 --> 00:18:00,347
HEY, WHERE'S THE CANTANKEROUS
BUT FUNNY BAILIFF?

445
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:02,615
[POUNDS GAVEL]

446
00:18:02,648 --> 00:18:05,152
WHO'S THERE?

447
00:18:05,185 --> 00:18:06,587
JAMES WILSON?

448
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:08,422
DURING THE PROGRESS
OF THIS TRIAL,

449
00:18:08,455 --> 00:18:11,057
YOU HAVE REFUSED TO TESTIFY
IN YOUR OWN DEFENSE.

450
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:13,960
AND BY YOUR SILENCE,
HAVE PREVENTED YOUR COUNSEL

451
00:18:13,993 --> 00:18:15,495
FROM ADEQUATELY
DEFENDING YOU.

452
00:18:15,528 --> 00:18:17,030
YOU CAN'T HANDLE THE TRUTH!

453
00:18:17,063 --> 00:18:18,232
-- WITH MANSLAUGHTER.

454
00:18:18,265 --> 00:18:19,733
AND IN THE EVIDENCE
PRESENTED,

455
00:18:19,767 --> 00:18:21,235
IN THE ABSENCE
OF EXPLANATION

456
00:18:21,268 --> 00:18:23,970
WOULD WARRANT THIS COURT
IN FINDING YOU GUILTY.

457
00:18:24,003 --> 00:18:25,405
BEFORE WE GO ANY FARTHER,

458
00:18:25,438 --> 00:18:27,942
I URGE YOU
ONCE AGAIN TO SPEAK.

459
00:18:27,975 --> 00:18:29,877
IF THERE IS ANYTHING YOU
CAN SAY IN YOUR OWN DEFENSE.

460
00:18:29,910 --> 00:18:32,212
UH, SORRY, I WAS LOOKING
AT YOUR MOLE, SIR.

461
00:18:34,447 --> 00:18:37,417
♪ KISS THE DAY GOODBYE... ♪

462
00:18:39,318 --> 00:18:41,222
- BLONDIE, NO!
- YOU KEEP OUT OF THIS!

463
00:18:41,255 --> 00:18:43,457
I LIKE JELLO.

464
00:18:45,458 --> 00:18:48,762
GIVE 'EM HELL, HARRY!

465
00:18:48,795 --> 00:18:50,597
WELL, MAYBE I SHOULDN'T
SAY THIS YOUR HONOR--

466
00:18:50,630 --> 00:18:51,865
BUT I'M ESTHER ROLLE.

467
00:18:51,898 --> 00:18:53,933
--BUT I ACCUSE MY PARENTS.

468
00:18:53,967 --> 00:18:56,470
- WE HAVE A TITLE!
- WE HAVE A TITLE, YES!

469
00:18:58,005 --> 00:19:01,308
WHOA, HUH,
THAT'S MAKING ME SICK.

470
00:19:01,342 --> 00:19:03,210
WELL, THAT WAS
A SHORT MOVIE.

471
00:19:03,243 --> 00:19:04,612
LET US HAVE ORDER
IN THIS COURT.

472
00:19:04,645 --> 00:19:08,415
OH, IF ONLY I WAS
HANS HALL RIGHT NOW.

473
00:19:08,448 --> 00:19:10,617
TELL US EXACTLY
WHAT IS IN YOUR MIND.

474
00:19:10,650 --> 00:19:12,285
YOU KNOW, STUFF.

475
00:19:12,318 --> 00:19:14,755
WELL, YOUR HONOR.

476
00:19:14,788 --> 00:19:16,055
I DON'T BELIEVE
MY MOTHER AND FATHER

477
00:19:16,088 --> 00:19:17,223
SHOULD'VE EVER HAD A CHILD.

478
00:19:17,257 --> 00:19:18,925
I WAS ABUSED AS A ZYGOTE.

479
00:19:18,958 --> 00:19:20,193
--THEY EVER WANTED
THE RESPONSIBILITY.

480
00:19:20,227 --> 00:19:22,328
WELL, EVERYBODY, SETTLE IN.

481
00:19:22,362 --> 00:19:23,863
--NEVER UNKIND TO ME.

482
00:19:23,897 --> 00:19:25,932
THEY GAVE ME EVERYTHING
I EVER WANTED EXCEPT--

483
00:19:25,965 --> 00:19:27,633
- PANCAKES.
- --TIME AND ATTENTION.

484
00:19:27,667 --> 00:19:28,935
AND MONEY.

485
00:19:28,968 --> 00:19:30,270
I LEARNED
TO PUT MYSELF TO BED

486
00:19:30,303 --> 00:19:31,838
WHEN I WAS
FOUR OR FIVE YEARS OLD.

487
00:19:31,872 --> 00:19:33,307
AND TO GET MY OWN BREAKFAST

488
00:19:33,340 --> 00:19:34,975
IF THEY WEREN'T UP YET WHEN IT
WAS TIME TO GO TO SCHOOL.

489
00:19:35,008 --> 00:19:36,810
YEAH, BOO-HOO,
WE ALL HAVE PROBLEMS.

490
00:19:36,843 --> 00:19:39,278
DID YOU GET ALONG WELL
IN SCHOOL?

491
00:19:39,312 --> 00:19:40,713
OH, YES, SIR. I LIKED IT.

492
00:19:40,747 --> 00:19:42,315
I HAD SOME PRETTY GOOD FRIENDS
AMONG MY CLASSMATES.

493
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:44,183
HEY, A SIMPLE
YES OR NO WILL DO.

494
00:19:44,217 --> 00:19:45,818
AND NOW I'M GOING
TO ANNOUNCE THE WINNER

495
00:19:45,852 --> 00:19:47,120
OF THE ESSAY CONTEST.

496
00:19:47,153 --> 00:19:49,022
SERGEANT, TAKE THE GUN
AND SHOOT THE CORPORAL.

497
00:19:49,055 --> 00:19:51,023
--AND PROUD THAT
THIS HONOR HAS FALLEN

498
00:19:51,057 --> 00:19:52,658
TO A PUPIL OF OUR SCHOOL,

499
00:19:52,692 --> 00:19:53,927
JAMES WILSON,

500
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:55,362
FOR HIS SPLENDID ESSAY--

501
00:19:55,395 --> 00:19:57,797
I WON, I WON. [LAUGHS]

502
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:02,368
COME FORWARD, JAMES.

503
00:20:02,402 --> 00:20:05,205
WELL, MAYBE HE JUST SUSPECTS
HIS PARENTS AT THIS POINT.

504
00:20:05,238 --> 00:20:07,207
I WOULD LIKE TO QUOTE
A CLOSING LINE

505
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:08,775
FROM JAMES' ESSAY,

506
00:20:08,808 --> 00:20:10,510
WHICH MADE
A PARTICULAR APPEAL

507
00:20:10,543 --> 00:20:12,012
TO THE JUDGES--

508
00:20:12,045 --> 00:20:14,080
- ALL LIFE IS TRAVESTY.
- IN THE IDEAL

509
00:20:14,113 --> 00:20:15,848
AMERICAN HOME,

510
00:20:15,882 --> 00:20:18,585
- THE FATHER--
- CONFORM.
- CONFORM.

511
00:20:18,618 --> 00:20:21,888
- [ALL] CONFORM. CONFORM.
- WHO IS HAPPY TO CARE
FOR HER CHILDREN,

512
00:20:21,922 --> 00:20:23,390
AND THEY ARE THANKFUL

513
00:20:23,423 --> 00:20:25,658
FOR THEIR HAPPINESS
AND SECURITY.

514
00:20:25,692 --> 00:20:27,527
WHEN I ACCEPTED
THE WOMAN IN ME--

515
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,697
--WANT TO MEET
YOUR MOTHER, JAMES.

516
00:20:29,730 --> 00:20:32,232
WE WANT TO KNOW THE WOMAN
WHO HAS INSPIRED

517
00:20:32,265 --> 00:20:33,500
THIS SPLENDID ESSAY.

518
00:20:33,533 --> 00:20:34,768
JOAN CRAWFORD?

519
00:20:34,802 --> 00:20:36,770
THE COMMITTEE OF MOTHERS
IS MEETING HERE TOMORROW

520
00:20:36,803 --> 00:20:38,005
AT 11:00.

521
00:20:38,038 --> 00:20:39,673
- OH, IT'S B.Y.O.M.
- TO DISCUSS PLANS

522
00:20:39,707 --> 00:20:41,975
FOR THE GRADUATION
EXERCISES.

523
00:20:42,008 --> 00:20:43,343
AND WE'D LOVE
TO HAVE YOUR MOTHER

524
00:20:43,377 --> 00:20:45,178
SERVE ON THE COMMITTEE,
JAMES.

525
00:20:45,212 --> 00:20:47,547
I DON'T HAVE A MOM,
MY DOG ATE HER.

526
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:49,582
VERY WELL, JAMES.

527
00:20:49,615 --> 00:20:51,050
OH BOY, OH BOY,
I WON, I WON!

528
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:52,452
AFTER 11 YEARS
IN HIGH SCHOOL,

529
00:20:52,485 --> 00:20:54,220
I FINALLY WON!...SOMETHING.

530
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:56,288
- HEY, EVERYBODY
LIVES IN THAT HOUSE.
- YEAH.

531
00:20:56,322 --> 00:20:58,125
MOM! MOM!

532
00:20:58,158 --> 00:20:59,392
OH, MOM--

533
00:20:59,425 --> 00:21:02,295
OH NO, MOM'S
IN THE BOTTLE AGAIN!

534
00:21:02,328 --> 00:21:05,498
EH, LOOKS LIKE MOM INVITED
JOE E. LEWIS OVER AGAIN.

535
00:21:07,667 --> 00:21:10,003
WELL, SHE TIDIED UP
THE PLACE.

536
00:21:14,908 --> 00:21:16,377
HMM.
"WENT TO STORE,

537
00:21:16,410 --> 00:21:18,712
"SCOTCH IN FRIDGE.
LOVE, MOM."

538
00:21:20,847 --> 00:21:23,683
"BUY YOURSELF
ANOTHER MOTHER."

539
00:21:23,717 --> 00:21:25,752
IT SAYS "P.S. SAY YES

540
00:21:25,785 --> 00:21:28,522
TO MARTINI AND ROSSI
ON THE ROCKS-- SAY YES."

541
00:21:30,123 --> 00:21:31,825
DIDN'T CROSS HER T.

542
00:21:31,858 --> 00:21:33,660
JEEZ, HER HANDWRITING
IS TERRIBLE!

543
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,368
SHE DRANK ALL THE GIN.

544
00:21:44,637 --> 00:21:46,640
HUH, IRONICALLY,
THE HUMORFUL PART

545
00:21:46,673 --> 00:21:48,408
IS HE BUYS LIQUOR
WITH THE TEN BUCKS.

546
00:21:48,442 --> 00:21:50,810
- D'OH!
- HE DOES.

547
00:21:50,843 --> 00:21:53,180
WHERE DO I START?
IT ALL LOOKS SO GOOD.

548
00:21:53,213 --> 00:21:56,550
THE VODKA CLASHES WITH
THE COFFEE TABLE.

549
00:21:56,583 --> 00:21:57,817
MOM IS HOT!

550
00:21:57,850 --> 00:21:59,418
- [BOTS GROWL]
- HELLO, JIMMY.

551
00:21:59,452 --> 00:22:01,522
- OH, HELLO, SHIRLEY.
- IS YOUR MOTHER HOME?

552
00:22:01,555 --> 00:22:03,022
- NO, SHE ISN'T.
- OH, NEVER MIND.

553
00:22:03,055 --> 00:22:04,858
I DIDN'T WANT
TO SEE HER ESPECIALLY.

554
00:22:04,892 --> 00:22:06,258
BESIDES, I CAN
SEE HER LATER.

555
00:22:06,292 --> 00:22:07,793
OKAY, WHO ARE YOU?

556
00:22:07,827 --> 00:22:10,163
YOU CAN OFFER ME A DRINK
IF YOU WANNA.

557
00:22:10,197 --> 00:22:11,432
AND I THINK YOU WANNA.

558
00:22:11,465 --> 00:22:12,598
SURE, HELP YOURSELF.

559
00:22:12,632 --> 00:22:14,533
- JUST PICK A TABLE.
- THANKS.

560
00:22:14,567 --> 00:22:17,203
IT'S A BOOZE PROGRESSIVE
DINNER, HERE.

561
00:22:17,237 --> 00:22:18,538
WELL, HOW ABOUT YOU?

562
00:22:18,572 --> 00:22:19,940
COME ON, JOIN ME.

563
00:22:19,973 --> 00:22:21,408
CAN'T DO ANY MORE
THAN KILL YOU.

564
00:22:21,442 --> 00:22:22,842
NO THANKS, NOT FOR ME.

565
00:22:22,875 --> 00:22:24,677
I'VE BEEN HITTING IT
TOO HARD, LATELY.

566
00:22:24,710 --> 00:22:26,278
YEAH, I KNOW,
IT'S KIND OF TOUGH

567
00:22:26,312 --> 00:22:27,680
WHEN IT GETS
THE BEST OF YOU.

568
00:22:27,713 --> 00:22:30,350
WELL, HERE GOES
FOR BOTH OF US.

569
00:22:30,383 --> 00:22:33,253
HEY, THAT'S MY BOOZE.

570
00:22:33,287 --> 00:22:35,555
LOOKS LIKE YOU'RE HAVING
YOURSELVES A TIME, YOU TOO.

571
00:22:35,588 --> 00:22:36,957
SUDDENLY,
THE THIN MAN ENTERS.

572
00:22:36,990 --> 00:22:38,258
WHAT GOES ON HERE?

573
00:22:38,292 --> 00:22:39,827
THIS IS MY FIRST.

574
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:41,828
- I WOULDN'T KNOW ABOUT JIM.
- BEAM.

575
00:22:41,862 --> 00:22:43,997
- MOTHER HOME YET?
- NO.

576
00:22:44,030 --> 00:22:45,765
MEANS ANOTHER COLD SUPPER,
I SUPPOSE.

577
00:22:45,798 --> 00:22:47,567
VODKA SANDWICHES.

578
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:49,635
WHAT CAN YOU EXPECT?
NINE TIMES OUT OF TEN,

579
00:22:49,668 --> 00:22:51,838
IF SHE DID STAY HOME
ALL DAY COOKING,

580
00:22:51,872 --> 00:22:53,807
YOU'D PHONE THE LAST MINUTE
YOU HAD A BUSINESS DATE

581
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:55,508
- AND COULDN'T MAKE IT.
- YOU THE GREEK CHORUS?

582
00:22:55,542 --> 00:22:57,810
YOU WOMEN CERTAINLY
STICK TOGETHER, DON'T YOU?

583
00:22:57,843 --> 00:22:59,813
NOT NECESSARILY.

584
00:22:59,847 --> 00:23:01,948
I'D RATHER STICK
TO AN ATTRACTIVE MAN.

585
00:23:01,982 --> 00:23:03,750
DAD, DO YOU MIND?

586
00:23:03,783 --> 00:23:06,653
WHOOP, WARDEN.

587
00:23:06,687 --> 00:23:08,388
HOME SO EARLY, DAN?

588
00:23:08,422 --> 00:23:10,090
I WAS A HALF HOUR LATE.

589
00:23:10,123 --> 00:23:12,292
BUT I WAS ONLY DETAINED
ON BUSINESS.

590
00:23:12,325 --> 00:23:14,693
YOU PROBABLY HAD
MORE IMPORTANT THINGS TO DO.

591
00:23:14,727 --> 00:23:16,028
YOU NEEDN'T BE
SO CROSS ABOUT IT.

592
00:23:16,062 --> 00:23:17,530
I'M SORRY IF I'M LATE.

593
00:23:17,563 --> 00:23:20,067
BUT THE BUSES ARE SO CROWDED,
AND I COULDN'T GET A TAXI.

594
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:22,035
I SUPPOSE YOU COULDN'T'VE
TRIED AN HOUR EARLIER.

595
00:23:22,068 --> 00:23:23,403
NO, I COULDN'T.

596
00:23:23,437 --> 00:23:25,505
FIX MOTHER A DRINK, JAMES.
I'M-- I'M EXHAUSTED.

597
00:23:25,538 --> 00:23:26,840
FROM DRINKING SO MUCH.

598
00:23:26,873 --> 00:23:28,542
ARE WE GONNA HAVE
ANY DINNER TONIGHT?

599
00:23:28,575 --> 00:23:30,477
IN A MINUTE,
IT'S ALL IN THE ICE BOX.

600
00:23:30,510 --> 00:23:32,812
HEY, COULD SOMEBODY PLEASE
DO AN INTERVENTION?

601
00:23:32,845 --> 00:23:34,380
- --SHIRLEY?
- OH, NO THANKS.

602
00:23:34,413 --> 00:23:35,615
I HAVE A DATE.

603
00:23:35,648 --> 00:23:37,983
- ANOTHER TIME, THEN.
- THANKS.

604
00:23:38,017 --> 00:23:39,552
- READY FOR OUR DATE?
- WELL,

605
00:23:39,585 --> 00:23:41,420
MAY THE BEST MAN WIN.

606
00:23:41,453 --> 00:23:43,022
WHO IS THAT?

607
00:23:43,055 --> 00:23:44,623
I'VE HAD JUST ABOUT
ENOUGH OF THIS.

608
00:23:44,657 --> 00:23:46,125
I WON'T PUT UP
WITH IT ANY LONGER.

609
00:23:46,158 --> 00:23:48,462
- WHAT'RE YOU TALKING ABOUT?
- THE WHOLE SETUP!

610
00:23:48,495 --> 00:23:50,030
NO DECENT MEALS ON TIME.

611
00:23:50,063 --> 00:23:51,463
THE HOUSE IS ALWAYS
IN A MESS.

612
00:23:51,497 --> 00:23:53,333
WHILE YOU'RE GADDING ABOUT,
MAKING A FOOL OF YOURSELF.

613
00:23:53,367 --> 00:23:54,733
- I GOT AN "A"--
- YOU DO WHAT YOU PLEASE.

614
00:23:54,767 --> 00:23:56,002
WHY SHOULDN'T I DO
WHAT I PLEASE?

615
00:23:56,035 --> 00:23:57,470
- THAT'S OKAY WITH ME.
- THE TEACHER SAID--

616
00:23:57,503 --> 00:23:59,272
BUT YOU'RE NOT GOING
TO DO IT WHILE YOU'RE MY WIFE.

617
00:23:59,305 --> 00:24:00,673
THAT SUITS ME.

618
00:24:00,707 --> 00:24:02,475
YOU DON'T SUPPOSE I LIKE
GOING ON LIKE THIS, DO YOU?

619
00:24:02,508 --> 00:24:04,177
I'D'VE DIVORCED YOU YEARS AGO
IF IT HADN'T BEEN FOR JIMMY.

620
00:24:04,210 --> 00:24:05,512
MOTHER, DAD, PLEASE.

621
00:24:05,545 --> 00:24:07,280
A FLOOD OF HELP
YOU'VE BEEN TO HIM.

622
00:24:07,313 --> 00:24:09,148
A FINE HOME YOU'VE
MADE FOR HIM.

623
00:24:09,182 --> 00:24:10,483
- BUT I GOT A--
- WELL, HOW ABOUT
THE EXAMPLE

624
00:24:10,517 --> 00:24:12,585
YOU'VE SET HIM?
OUT GAMBLING EVERY NIGHT.

625
00:24:12,618 --> 00:24:14,320
SOMETIMES NOT EVEN
COMING HOME AT ALL.

626
00:24:14,353 --> 00:24:16,255
- REALLY GOOD PAPER--
- A MAN HAS TO DO SOMETHING
TO PASS THE TIME.

627
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:18,358
- TEACHER SAID I WAS--

628
00:24:18,392 --> 00:24:20,360
- THEN WHY DO YOU COME HOME?
- MAYBE I WON'T IN THE FUTURE.

629
00:24:20,393 --> 00:24:21,962
- BUT I CAN'T--
- DAD.

630
00:24:21,995 --> 00:24:23,330
- FRESHEN YOUR DRINK?
- I'VE GOT SOMETHING
TO SAY TO YOU.

631
00:24:23,363 --> 00:24:24,697
- YEAH SON?
- IT'S SOMETHING
ABOUT SCHOOL.

632
00:24:24,730 --> 00:24:26,600
I WON THE ESSAY CONTEST,
AND THE PRINCIPAL SAID--

633
00:24:26,633 --> 00:24:28,768
WELL, SAY, THAT'S FINE.

634
00:24:28,802 --> 00:24:31,037
HERE'S $5.
GO OUT AND CELEBRATE.

635
00:24:31,070 --> 00:24:32,838
SPEND IT ON
LOOSE LEAF PAPER.

636
00:24:32,872 --> 00:24:35,342
THERE GOES A GREAT MAN.

637
00:24:35,375 --> 00:24:37,710
WHAT ABOUT MY $5?

638
00:24:39,012 --> 00:24:40,147
OH, JEEZ.

639
00:24:40,180 --> 00:24:41,715
THIS GUY'S MADE
MORE MONEY TODAY

640
00:24:41,748 --> 00:24:43,250
THAN I DID ALL THE WAY
THROUGH HIGH SCHOOL.

641
00:24:43,283 --> 00:24:45,052
- HE'LL BE BACK.
- WITH ANOTHER WOMAN.

642
00:24:45,085 --> 00:24:47,320
I DON'T CARE
IF HE COMES BACK OR NOT.

643
00:24:47,353 --> 00:24:48,522
WON'T BE ANY DIFFERENT
IF HE DOES.

644
00:24:48,555 --> 00:24:49,788
WELL, MAYBE IT WILL.

645
00:24:49,822 --> 00:24:51,190
YOU SEE, I DIDN'T TELL DAD
ALL THAT HAPPENED

646
00:24:51,223 --> 00:24:52,325
AT SCHOOL TODAY.

647
00:24:52,358 --> 00:24:53,460
THE PRINCIPAL
WANTS YOU TO MEET WITH

648
00:24:53,493 --> 00:24:55,695
THE PARENTS GRADUATION COMMITTEE
TOMORROW AT 11.

649
00:24:55,728 --> 00:24:57,997
MRS. CARLYLE AND MRS. WHITNEY
ARE GONNA BE THERE.

650
00:24:58,030 --> 00:24:59,698
ALL THE MOST IMPORTANT WOMEN
IN THE NEIGHBORHOOD.

651
00:24:59,732 --> 00:25:01,602
- IS THERE A BAR?
- OH, JIMMY.

652
00:25:01,635 --> 00:25:03,237
--AND THEY REALLY
WANT ME TO BE THERE?

653
00:25:03,270 --> 00:25:05,572
OH, SURE THEY DO,
AND I WANT YOU TO GO, MOM.

654
00:25:05,605 --> 00:25:08,542
YEAH, THEY NEED
A LAUGHINGSTOCK.

655
00:25:08,575 --> 00:25:10,877
I COULD WEAR MY NEW
AFTERNOON DRESS.

656
00:25:10,910 --> 00:25:12,745
AND THAT HAT I JUST BOUGHT.

657
00:25:12,778 --> 00:25:14,982
OH, WAIT TILL HE GETS
THE BILL FOR THAT HAT.

658
00:25:23,590 --> 00:25:25,592
OKAY, SO, IS EVERYBODY DONE

659
00:25:25,625 --> 00:25:27,260
WITH THEIR
ART THERAPY PROJECT?

660
00:25:27,293 --> 00:25:28,528
JOEL, WHAT'S THE POINT

661
00:25:28,562 --> 00:25:30,230
OF THIS ART THERAPY STUFF
ANYWAY, HUH?

662
00:25:30,263 --> 00:25:31,965
WELL, BY HAVING YOU
DRAW PICTURES

663
00:25:31,998 --> 00:25:35,002
OF YOUR IDEALIZED FAMILY,
MAYBE YOU CAN ESCAPE

664
00:25:35,035 --> 00:25:37,170
SOME OF THE DEEP
PSYCHOLOGICAL PROBLEMS

665
00:25:37,203 --> 00:25:39,072
THAT JIMMY,
THE STAR OF TODAY'S MOVIE,

666
00:25:39,105 --> 00:25:40,440
SUFFER BECAUSE
OF HIS FAMILY.

667
00:25:40,473 --> 00:25:41,975
SO LET'S SEE WHAT
YOU'VE DRAWN, OKAY?

668
00:25:42,008 --> 00:25:43,277
THIS IS CROW'S.

669
00:25:43,310 --> 00:25:45,312
THAT'S MY DAD.
HE'S ALL-POWERFUL.

670
00:25:45,345 --> 00:25:47,147
HIS HANDS ARE MADE
OF STAINLESS STEEL,

671
00:25:47,180 --> 00:25:48,348
AND HE HAS LASERS THAT

672
00:25:48,382 --> 00:25:50,217
SHOOT OUT OF HIS CHEST.
PEW-PEW!

673
00:25:50,250 --> 00:25:51,818
I DON'T HAVE TO TELL YOU
HE'S THE COOLEST DAD

674
00:25:51,852 --> 00:25:53,052
IN THE WHOLE NEIGHBORHOOD.

675
00:25:53,085 --> 00:25:55,122
AND WE-- WHEN WE GO
TO FATHER-SON PICNICS,

676
00:25:55,155 --> 00:25:56,723
WE WIN EVERY EVENT.

677
00:25:56,757 --> 00:25:58,425
AND HE DISPENSES
HOMESPUN WISDOM,

678
00:25:58,458 --> 00:26:00,260
AND TEACHES
SOLID MIDWESTERN VALUES

679
00:26:00,293 --> 00:26:02,028
WHILE CRUSHING ALL
WHO BLOCK HIS PATH.

680
00:26:02,062 --> 00:26:05,065
UH-HUH, WHAT ABOUT
THE HANDLEBAR MUSTACHE?

681
00:26:05,098 --> 00:26:06,198
I DON'T KNOW.

682
00:26:06,232 --> 00:26:07,767
O-KAY.

683
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:09,068
LET'S SEE HERE.

684
00:26:09,102 --> 00:26:12,738
UH, ORAL OBSESSION
WITH MUSTACHE

685
00:26:12,772 --> 00:26:15,942
INDICATES
NASAL-LABIAL SHAME.

686
00:26:15,975 --> 00:26:17,477
- SOUNDS SERIOUS.
- OKAY.

687
00:26:17,510 --> 00:26:19,712
NOW LET'S SEE YOURS HERE.
TOM, WHAT'S THIS?

688
00:26:19,745 --> 00:26:22,315
OKEY-DOKE, UH,
THAT'S MY MOM, MY DAD,

689
00:26:22,348 --> 00:26:24,650
AND MY MOM.
MY MOM IS HAYLEY MILLS,

690
00:26:24,683 --> 00:26:27,653
MY DAD IS GIGANTOR,
AND MY MOM IS PEGGY CASS.

691
00:26:27,687 --> 00:26:31,423
UH-HUH, AND WHY ARE YOUR MOMS
HOLDING HANDS, TOM?

692
00:26:31,457 --> 00:26:32,525
I DON'T KNOW.

693
00:26:32,558 --> 00:26:33,960
O-KAY.

694
00:26:33,993 --> 00:26:37,530
LET'S SEE, LATENT
PARENT-TRAP SYNDROME.

695
00:26:37,563 --> 00:26:39,465
MAN SHOULD BE
IN A STRAITJACKET.

696
00:26:39,498 --> 00:26:41,633
OKAY, GYPSY, WELL,
THIS ONE'S REALLY NICE.

697
00:26:41,667 --> 00:26:42,902
WHAT'S THIS ONE?

698
00:26:42,935 --> 00:26:45,772
JOEL, MY IDEAL FAMILY
IS RIGHT HERE.

699
00:26:45,805 --> 00:26:48,508
AND I KNOW RICHARD BASEHART
WATCHES OVER US ALL.

700
00:26:48,542 --> 00:26:49,742
- HUH.
- OH...

701
00:26:49,775 --> 00:26:51,778
THAT'S REALLY SWEET, GYPSY,
BUT TELL ME--

702
00:26:51,812 --> 00:26:54,113
WHY DOES RICHARD BASEHART
GET TO PLAY GOD?

703
00:26:54,147 --> 00:26:55,382
I DON'T KNOW.

704
00:26:55,415 --> 00:26:56,817
JOEL, WHY ARE YOU
SPENDING YOUR TIME

705
00:26:56,850 --> 00:26:58,150
PSYCHOANALYZING ROBOTS?

706
00:26:58,183 --> 00:27:00,487
UM... I DON'T KNOW.

707
00:27:00,520 --> 00:27:02,388
I'M KIDDING, OF COURSE.
WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

708
00:27:02,422 --> 00:27:04,190
I DO KNOW.
I REALLY DO KNOW.

709
00:27:11,297 --> 00:27:13,265
[DAN LAUGHS]

710
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:14,533
WHAT? WHAT'S SO FUNNY?

711
00:27:14,567 --> 00:27:15,835
THAT JOE BOLSTER.

712
00:27:15,868 --> 00:27:17,103
HE JUST CRACKS ME UP.

713
00:27:17,137 --> 00:27:18,972
THE MIRROR
OUGHT TO TELL YOU.

714
00:27:19,005 --> 00:27:20,940
I'M GETTING READY
TO GO TO JIM'S SCHOOL.

715
00:27:20,973 --> 00:27:23,377
WELL, YOU CERTAINLY
LOOK THE PART.

716
00:27:23,410 --> 00:27:25,812
WHY DON'T YOU ACT YOUR AGE?

717
00:27:25,845 --> 00:27:27,447
STOP CRITICIZING ME.

718
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:29,615
YOU DON'T LIKE MY CLOTHES.
YOU DON'T LIKE MY HAT.

719
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:30,850
YOU DON'T LIKE IT
IF I SIT AROUND HERE.

720
00:27:30,883 --> 00:27:32,118
YOU DON'T LIKE IT
IF I GO OUT.

721
00:27:32,152 --> 00:27:34,020
OH, LET'S STOP
THIS RIDICULOUS FARCE.

722
00:27:34,053 --> 00:27:35,188
WHY DON'T WE QUIT?

723
00:27:35,222 --> 00:27:37,157
- I-- I LIKE YOUR HAT.
- GREAT IDEA.

724
00:27:37,190 --> 00:27:38,792
THANKS FOR THE SUGGESTION.

725
00:27:38,825 --> 00:27:41,762
SO THEY'RE DIVORCED NOW?
THAT WAS EASY.

726
00:27:41,795 --> 00:27:43,362
HMM, HE'S A GOOD HUSBAND.

727
00:27:43,395 --> 00:27:45,998
HE JUST HAS A HARD TIME
EXPRESSING HIS FEELINGS.

728
00:27:47,867 --> 00:27:51,838
SHE'S GOT A SEA ANEMONE
ON HER HEAD.

729
00:27:51,872 --> 00:27:54,573
♪ MIRROR MIRROR
ON THE WALL ♪

730
00:27:54,607 --> 00:27:56,542
CAN I MAKE IT TO LAST CALL?

731
00:27:58,812 --> 00:28:00,380
I'M GONNA WORK ON
THE DECORATING COMMITTEE.

732
00:28:00,413 --> 00:28:01,647
OH, ISN'T THAT SWELL?

733
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:03,483
SOME OF US GIRLS THOUGHT
WE COULD BRING SOME FLOWERS.

734
00:28:03,517 --> 00:28:05,285
I'M GONNA BUILD A BLIMP
AND FIGHT THE NAZIS.

735
00:28:05,318 --> 00:28:06,652
--TO WIN THE CONTEST.

736
00:28:06,685 --> 00:28:09,188
I THINK HE SHOULD READ IT AT
THE GRADUATION EXERCISES.

737
00:28:09,222 --> 00:28:10,623
WHY, YES, WHAT
AN EXCELLENT IDEA.

738
00:28:10,657 --> 00:28:12,058
WOW, THE WHOLE SCHOOL
SEEMS TO BE

739
00:28:12,092 --> 00:28:13,527
BUZZING ABOUT THAT ESSAY.

740
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:14,727
--MY HOME, THAT'S ALL.

741
00:28:14,760 --> 00:28:16,395
IT'S THE WAY
ANY OTHER FELLA'S IS.

742
00:28:16,428 --> 00:28:17,663
THE WAY A HOME OUGHT TO BE.

743
00:28:17,697 --> 00:28:19,265
A VERY HAPPY HOME,
OBVIOUSLY.

744
00:28:19,298 --> 00:28:21,067
I'M MOST ANXIOUS
TO MEET YOUR MOTHER.

745
00:28:21,100 --> 00:28:22,235
OH, MOM'S SWELL.

746
00:28:22,268 --> 00:28:25,070
[ALL]
♪ LIAR! LIAR! LIAR! ♪

747
00:28:25,103 --> 00:28:26,940
--I HAD A LOT
OF BROTHERS AND SISTERS.

748
00:28:26,973 --> 00:28:28,942
SHE MUST TAKE
A GREAT INTEREST IN HER HOME.

749
00:28:28,975 --> 00:28:30,377
SHE DOES. THAT'S ALL
SHE THINKS ABOUT.

750
00:28:30,410 --> 00:28:31,912
OH, THAT AND TWIST-OFF CAPS.

751
00:28:31,945 --> 00:28:34,080
WHAT'S MORE IMPORTANT WHEN
YOU COME RIGHT DOWN TO IT?

752
00:28:34,113 --> 00:28:36,315
A WOMAN'S JOB IS HER HOME
AND FAMILY, ISN'T IT?

753
00:28:36,348 --> 00:28:38,050
AT LEAST, THAT'S THE WAY
MY MOM FIGURES.

754
00:28:38,083 --> 00:28:40,320
MRS.- HELLO EVERYBODY.
- OH, AND DID I TELL YOU
SHE DRINKS?

755
00:28:40,353 --> 00:28:41,922
SORRY IF I'M LATE.

756
00:28:41,955 --> 00:28:44,423
MISS REARDON DRINKS A LOT.

757
00:28:44,457 --> 00:28:46,458
I'M JIMMY WILSON'S MOTHER.

758
00:28:46,492 --> 00:28:48,928
- [GIGGLES] SHE'S DRUNK.
- IT'S FUNNY!

759
00:28:48,962 --> 00:28:50,363
HOW SHOCKING.

760
00:28:50,397 --> 00:28:52,165
ELEANOR ROOSEVELT'S PISSED.

761
00:28:52,198 --> 00:28:54,500
- OOH.
- HOW TERRIBLE.

762
00:28:54,533 --> 00:28:55,735
- HOW DREADF--
- MOM!

763
00:28:55,768 --> 00:28:57,003
DID YOU BRING ANOTHER GLASS?

764
00:28:57,037 --> 00:28:59,038
AM I LATE?
WHEN'S THE MEETING START?

765
00:28:59,072 --> 00:29:00,573
COME ON, MOM, LET'S GO HOME.

766
00:29:00,607 --> 00:29:02,575
OH, WHAT'S YOUR HURRY?
AREN'T YOU GONNA INTRODUCE ME?

767
00:29:02,608 --> 00:29:05,178
SOME OTHER TIME, MOM, PLEASE.
COME ON, LET'S GO HOME.

768
00:29:05,212 --> 00:29:07,180
SO LONG, MRS.... UM,
"LUSH," WAS IT? YES.

769
00:29:07,213 --> 00:29:09,015
I WANNA GO TO THE MEETING.

770
00:29:09,048 --> 00:29:10,550
LATER, IN PRISON.

771
00:29:10,583 --> 00:29:12,452
- SHE'S DRUNK.
- IT'S FUNNY.

772
00:29:12,485 --> 00:29:13,853
HOW SHOCKING.

773
00:29:13,887 --> 00:29:15,555
I WISH MY PEERS WOULD
GET OUT OF MY HEAD.

774
00:29:15,588 --> 00:29:17,190
I'M TRYING TO SLEEP.

775
00:29:17,223 --> 00:29:20,527
HOW DREADFUL.

776
00:29:20,560 --> 00:29:22,495
♪ I'M WALKING
YES, INDEED ♪

777
00:29:22,528 --> 00:29:24,530
♪ I'M TALKING
I ACCUSE MY PARENTS--

778
00:29:24,563 --> 00:29:27,067
HE WANTS TO TURN HIS ESSAY
INTO A SCREENPLAY.

779
00:29:27,100 --> 00:29:28,433
OH, THERE'S SOME PEOPLE
FROM LORIMAR

780
00:29:28,467 --> 00:29:31,503
WHO ARE INTERESTED.

781
00:29:31,537 --> 00:29:33,507
WANTED. MOTHER.

782
00:29:33,540 --> 00:29:36,275
HMM.

783
00:29:36,308 --> 00:29:38,343
- DID YOU EVER
SELL SHOES BEFORE?
- UH, NO SIR.

784
00:29:38,377 --> 00:29:39,745
A YOUNG AL BUNDY.

785
00:29:39,778 --> 00:29:41,380
- --IF YOU GIVE ME A TRY.
- YOU LIVE WITH YOUR PARENTS?

786
00:29:41,413 --> 00:29:42,648
UH, YES, SIR.

787
00:29:42,682 --> 00:29:45,050
- WELL, YOU LOOK
LIKE A GOOD BOY.
- [ALL] HEY.

788
00:29:45,083 --> 00:29:46,887
NOW, THE JOB PAYS
$25 A WEEK,

789
00:29:46,920 --> 00:29:48,420
AND YOU GET
AN HOUR OFF FOR LUNCH.

790
00:29:48,453 --> 00:29:49,622
GOTTA BE HERE
EVERY MORNING AT NINE.

791
00:29:49,655 --> 00:29:51,123
WORK TILL SIX. OKAY?

792
00:29:51,157 --> 00:29:52,425
- YES, SIR.
- OKAY.

793
00:29:52,458 --> 00:29:54,893
AND I'LL SHOW YOU THE STOCK.

794
00:29:54,927 --> 00:29:58,732
HEY, HE SNEEZED
ALL OVER THE WINDOW.

795
00:29:58,765 --> 00:30:00,165
LET HER OUT!
LET HER OUT!

796
00:30:00,198 --> 00:30:02,635
SHE'S FROZEN.

797
00:30:02,668 --> 00:30:06,272
OH, SHE'S A FROSTED
MINI-PEARL.

798
00:30:06,305 --> 00:30:09,675
THE HAT.

799
00:30:09,708 --> 00:30:12,078
THE BIG GOOBER OVER HERE.

800
00:30:12,112 --> 00:30:13,612
AND DOWN THERE.

801
00:30:16,682 --> 00:30:19,552
OH, I GET IT.
YOU WANNA SEE MY KNEES.

802
00:30:22,188 --> 00:30:24,990
WHY DID HE SPRAY DESENEX
ALL OVER THE WINDOW?

803
00:30:25,023 --> 00:30:26,860
HE JUST DOESN'T GET IT,
DOES HE?

804
00:30:29,328 --> 00:30:31,230
NO, NO, YOU'RE
RUINING IT FOR ME.

805
00:30:31,263 --> 00:30:33,298
I WANT YOU
TO PUT ON SOME SHOES.

806
00:30:35,768 --> 00:30:39,072
OH, COME ON, JUST CLEAN
THE WHOLE WINDOW.

807
00:30:39,105 --> 00:30:40,807
JEEZ.

808
00:30:43,375 --> 00:30:45,110
YOUR MOTHER'S IN DETOX.

809
00:30:45,143 --> 00:30:47,780
COME QUICKLY.

810
00:30:47,813 --> 00:30:49,815
AH, GET IN HERE. JEEZ.

811
00:30:49,848 --> 00:30:52,452
AAH, THAT'S A GOOD IDEA.

812
00:30:52,485 --> 00:30:56,322
PLEASE DON'T TOUCH
THE CUSTOMERS, JIM.

813
00:30:56,355 --> 00:30:57,623
YOU INTERESTED
IN SOMETHING IN SHOES?

814
00:30:57,657 --> 00:30:58,925
NO, A FISH SANDWICH--
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

815
00:30:58,958 --> 00:31:00,327
YES.

816
00:31:00,360 --> 00:31:02,528
I'D LIKE TO SEE THOSE
SUEDE SLIPPERS IN THE WINDOW.

817
00:31:02,562 --> 00:31:04,330
THE BLACK ONES WITH THE BOWS.

818
00:31:04,363 --> 00:31:07,767
I WON AN ESSAY CONTEST.

819
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:11,103
MY MOM DOESN'T DRINK.

820
00:31:11,137 --> 00:31:12,438
[ALONG WITH SCORE]
♪ I'LL SELL SOME SHOES ♪

821
00:31:12,472 --> 00:31:14,173
♪ I'LL SELL SOME SHOES ♪

822
00:31:14,207 --> 00:31:15,942
- ♪ I'LL SELL SOME SHOES ♪
- YOU'D BETTER
LET ME HELP YOU.

823
00:31:15,975 --> 00:31:17,177
OH, THAT'S ALL RIGHT.

824
00:31:17,210 --> 00:31:18,778
CRUEL SHOES.

825
00:31:18,812 --> 00:31:20,045
OW.

826
00:31:20,078 --> 00:31:23,315
I LIKE YOUR UNDERWEAR.

827
00:31:23,348 --> 00:31:25,485
[ALL] P-U!

828
00:31:25,518 --> 00:31:27,653
THERE'S CHEESE IN HERE!

829
00:31:29,855 --> 00:31:33,092
BRANNICK! DA-DA DA-DA.

830
00:31:33,125 --> 00:31:35,127
EIGHT? OH,
YOU'D BETTER TRY AGAIN.

831
00:31:35,160 --> 00:31:37,230
THERE'S SOMETHING WRONG.

832
00:31:39,232 --> 00:31:40,600
♪ I'LL TRY AGAIN ♪

833
00:31:40,633 --> 00:31:41,767
♪ 'CAUSE SOMETHING'S WRONG ♪

834
00:31:41,800 --> 00:31:44,803
- BETTER WITH YOUR HAND OUT.
- OH.

835
00:31:44,837 --> 00:31:46,805
WELL, IT SAYS HERE
YOUR FEET DON'T EXIST.

836
00:31:46,838 --> 00:31:48,642
SIXES.

837
00:31:48,675 --> 00:31:51,010
[LAUGHS] SIXES.

838
00:31:51,043 --> 00:31:53,545
OH! MY AREA.

839
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:55,280
HOGAN, PUSH THE OTHER SHOES.

840
00:31:55,313 --> 00:31:57,183
HEIL HITLER.

841
00:31:57,217 --> 00:31:59,418
CAN I SHOW YOU SOMETHING
IN A SIZE "ME"?

842
00:32:02,722 --> 00:32:05,925
HEY, THOSE ARE
HER OLD SHOES.

843
00:32:05,958 --> 00:32:08,260
THESE ARE RED GOOSE SHOES,
SO YOU GET A FREE EGG.

844
00:32:10,262 --> 00:32:11,530
I GOT MY THUMB CAUGHT.

845
00:32:11,563 --> 00:32:12,732
JEEZ, IT'S A GOOD THING

846
00:32:12,765 --> 00:32:16,602
SHE'S NOT TRYING ON
A GIRDLE.

847
00:32:16,635 --> 00:32:17,870
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

848
00:32:17,903 --> 00:32:20,205
BEAUTIFUL.

849
00:32:20,238 --> 00:32:22,008
- THE SHOES, I MEAN.
- OH-- UGLY.

850
00:32:22,042 --> 00:32:24,510
OH, THEY LOOK LIKE THEY
MIGHT'VE BEEN MADE FOR YOU.

851
00:32:24,543 --> 00:32:27,447
- THEY PROBABLY WERE.
- MY HUSBAND IS BUSTER BROWN.

852
00:32:27,480 --> 00:32:29,182
I'M A FATALIST.
I BELIEVE THAT

853
00:32:29,215 --> 00:32:31,117
EVERYTHING HAPPENS
AS IT SHOULD HAPPEN.

854
00:32:31,150 --> 00:32:32,252
JUST LIKE MY COMING IN HERE

855
00:32:32,285 --> 00:32:33,853
AND BUYING THESE SHOES
FROM YOU.

856
00:32:33,887 --> 00:32:35,922
- YOU REALLY BELIEVE THAT?
- OF COURSE.

857
00:32:35,955 --> 00:32:39,125
- HOW MUCH ARE THEY?
- UM, $9.95
INCLUDING TAX.

858
00:32:39,158 --> 00:32:41,427
WELL, YOU'LL HAVE
TO SEND THEM C.O.D.

859
00:32:41,460 --> 00:32:42,928
OH, I'M SORRY,
WE CAN'T DO THAT.

860
00:32:42,962 --> 00:32:44,597
I MEAN, WE DON'T
MAKE DELIVERIES, SEE.

861
00:32:44,630 --> 00:32:47,333
I MEAN YOU'RE A BAD PERSON--
I MEAN--

862
00:32:47,367 --> 00:32:49,202
MAYBE YOU COULD DROP THEM OFF
ON YOUR WAY HOME.

863
00:32:49,235 --> 00:32:51,437
- YEAH, MAYBE I COULD.
- MY NAME'S KITTY REED.

864
00:32:51,470 --> 00:32:53,973
OH YEAH, BRING IT IN.
THAT'S RIGHT.

865
00:32:54,007 --> 00:32:55,775
SET THE HOOK, THERE YOU GO.

866
00:32:55,808 --> 00:32:57,243
WHAT TIME WILL YOU BE BY?

867
00:32:57,277 --> 00:32:58,812
WELL, I GET OFF WORK
ABOUT SIX.

868
00:32:58,845 --> 00:33:00,278
I GUESS I COULD MAKE IT
IN ABOUT TEN MINUTES.

869
00:33:00,312 --> 00:33:01,980
OH, THAT'S FINE,
I'LL BE LOOKING FOR YOU.

870
00:33:02,013 --> 00:33:03,248
- OKAY. BYE.
- BYE.

871
00:33:03,282 --> 00:33:07,053
ARE WE IN LOVE YET?
UH, OKAY.

872
00:33:07,087 --> 00:33:10,857
GEE, IT'S 6:11 ALREADY.
WHERE IS HE?

873
00:33:10,890 --> 00:33:12,292
[DOORBELL BUZZES]

874
00:33:12,325 --> 00:33:13,592
OH, QUICK, OUT THE BACK WAY.

875
00:33:13,625 --> 00:33:16,062
SHE'S GOT A CLOSET
FULL OF DEAD SHOE-SALESMEN.

876
00:33:18,330 --> 00:33:19,798
- LOVE ME!
- HELLO.

877
00:33:19,832 --> 00:33:21,933
- HERE'S YOUR SHOES.
- THANKS.

878
00:33:21,967 --> 00:33:23,268
BUT, UH, YOU'RE
TWO MINUTES LATE.

879
00:33:23,302 --> 00:33:25,738
YEAH, I KNOW, I HAD
TO PUT AWAY SOME OF THE STOCK.

880
00:33:25,772 --> 00:33:26,905
WELL, COME ON IN.

881
00:33:26,938 --> 00:33:29,275
QUACK, QUACK.
QUACK-QUACK-QUACK.

882
00:33:29,308 --> 00:33:30,577
[MORE QUACKING]

883
00:33:30,610 --> 00:33:32,010
YOU KNOW, IT MIGHT
NOT BE IMPORTANT,

884
00:33:32,043 --> 00:33:33,980
BUT IF SOMEONE DROPPED IN
ACCIDENTALLY

885
00:33:34,013 --> 00:33:35,247
AND I HAD TO INTRODUCE YOU--

886
00:33:35,280 --> 00:33:37,717
IF I WAS IN MY UNDERWEAR
AND YOU WERE ON THE TRAPEZE.

887
00:33:37,750 --> 00:33:39,352
- --I KNEW YOUR NAME.
- OH, JAMES WILSON.

888
00:33:39,385 --> 00:33:40,820
BUT EVERYBODY CALLS ME JIMMY.

889
00:33:40,853 --> 00:33:42,955
OKAY, JIMMY.
EVERYONE CALLS ME KITTY.

890
00:33:42,988 --> 00:33:44,623
I DON'T KNOW WHY--
MY NAME IS SUSAN.

891
00:33:44,657 --> 00:33:46,625
OKAY, KITTY.

892
00:33:46,658 --> 00:33:48,060
AND WILL YOU HAVE SOME?

893
00:33:48,093 --> 00:33:49,395
OR WOULD YOU
RATHER HAVE A DRINK?

894
00:33:49,428 --> 00:33:50,763
OH, NO THANKS, NOT FOR ME.

895
00:33:50,797 --> 00:33:52,565
I'VE BEEN HITTING THAT STUFF
KIND OF HEAVY LATELY.

896
00:33:52,598 --> 00:33:53,900
BESIDES, MY MOTHER DOESN'T LIKE

897
00:33:53,933 --> 00:33:55,902
TO SMELL IT ON MY BREATH.
YOU KNOW HOW MOTHERS ARE.

898
00:33:55,935 --> 00:33:57,537
WELL, THEN,
HOW ABOUT A BONG?

899
00:33:57,570 --> 00:34:00,138
I NEVER HAD ONE MYSELF.
ENOUGH TO REMEMBER.

900
00:34:00,172 --> 00:34:02,875
I WAS TORN FROM
THE THIGH OF ZEUS.

901
00:34:02,908 --> 00:34:05,077
I GOT USED TO BEING
ON MY OWN A LONG TIME AGO.

902
00:34:05,110 --> 00:34:06,878
- [SERVO LAUGHS]
- DO YOU LIVE HERE ALONE?

903
00:34:06,912 --> 00:34:09,215
NO, WITH VERA MOORE.
SHE'S IN THE SHOW WITH ME.

904
00:34:09,248 --> 00:34:10,750
OH, ARE YOU AN ACTRESS?

905
00:34:10,783 --> 00:34:12,685
WELL, NOT
AN ACTRESS EXACTLY.

906
00:34:12,718 --> 00:34:14,120
I-- I WORK IN A NIGHTCLUB.

907
00:34:14,153 --> 00:34:15,688
THE PARADISE-- HAVE YOU
EVER BEEN THERE?

908
00:34:15,722 --> 00:34:17,490
NO, BUT I'LL COME
AND SEE YOU SOME NIGHT.

909
00:34:17,523 --> 00:34:19,592
OH, THAT'S SWELL, JIMMY.
I'LL BE LOOKING FOR YOU.

910
00:34:26,365 --> 00:34:27,667
YOU KNOW, IT'D SEEM
KIND OF STRANGE TO ME.

911
00:34:27,700 --> 00:34:30,068
JUST LIVING HERE LIKE THIS
WITH ANOTHER FRIEND.

912
00:34:30,102 --> 00:34:31,837
YEAH, I KNOW.

913
00:34:31,870 --> 00:34:34,040
NOT HAVING ANYONE
TO COME HOME TO.

914
00:34:34,073 --> 00:34:36,075
- LIKE A FAMILY.
- THAT'S RIGHT.

915
00:34:36,108 --> 00:34:38,510
WHY, WHEN I OPEN THE DOOR,
MY MOM IS SURE TO CALL OUT

916
00:34:38,543 --> 00:34:39,678
- "IS THAT YOU, JIM?"
- LIAR.

917
00:34:39,712 --> 00:34:41,680
NO MATTER WHAT TIME
OF DAY OR NIGHT IT IS.

918
00:34:41,713 --> 00:34:43,415
- I GET SO I EXPECT IT.
- DOUBLE-LIE.

919
00:34:43,448 --> 00:34:44,717
OF COURSE, I ALWAYS TELL HER

920
00:34:44,750 --> 00:34:45,918
TO GO TO BED
WHEN I'M GONNA BE LATE,

921
00:34:45,952 --> 00:34:47,353
- BUT SHE NEVER DOES.
- BIG FAT LIE.

922
00:34:47,387 --> 00:34:48,687
SHE WORRIES ABOUT ME,
I GUESS, SHE...

923
00:34:48,720 --> 00:34:50,222
CAN'T REST UNTIL I GET HOME.

924
00:34:50,255 --> 00:34:51,923
HE'S A GIFTED STORYTELLER.

925
00:34:51,957 --> 00:34:53,225
OH, SHE IS, SHE'S WONDERFUL.

926
00:34:53,258 --> 00:34:55,027
- LIE.
- SHE'S THE BEST MOTHER
A GUY EVER HAD.

927
00:34:55,060 --> 00:34:56,995
- DOUBLE-LIE.
- AND DAD'S
PRETTY SWELL, TOO.

928
00:34:57,028 --> 00:34:59,232
HE TAKES AN INTEREST
IN EVERYTHING I DO.

929
00:34:59,265 --> 00:35:00,633
WHY, WHEN WE TALK,
IT'S JUST LIKE

930
00:35:00,667 --> 00:35:03,002
TWO FELLAS MY AGE
INSTEAD OF FATHER AND SON.

931
00:35:03,035 --> 00:35:04,937
MOM SAYS SHE REALLY
HAS TWO BEAUS.

932
00:35:04,970 --> 00:35:07,540
WELL, IT'S GETTING
REALLY LATE-- I THINK...

933
00:35:07,573 --> 00:35:10,342
--LIKE THAT.
I ALMOST DID.

934
00:35:10,375 --> 00:35:12,578
MY FOLKS SPLIT UP
ABOUT THREE YEARS AGO,

935
00:35:12,612 --> 00:35:14,013
AND I'VE BEEN
ON MY OWN EVER SINCE.

936
00:35:14,047 --> 00:35:16,048
WELL, YOU SEEM TO HAVE DONE
PRETTY WELL ON YOUR OWN.

937
00:35:16,082 --> 00:35:17,683
NOT NEARLY AS WELL AS ME
WITH MY MOTHER, OF COURSE.

938
00:35:17,717 --> 00:35:20,018
I WISH I COULD BELIEVE THAT.

939
00:35:20,052 --> 00:35:21,420
CAN I JUST TELL YOU
ONE MORE THING ABOUT MY MOM?

940
00:35:21,453 --> 00:35:22,822
WELL, I'D BETTER
PAY YOU FOR THE SHOES

941
00:35:22,855 --> 00:35:24,023
BEFORE I TALK YOU OUT OF IT.

942
00:35:24,057 --> 00:35:25,490
OH, NO, DON'T DO THAT.
I MEAN,

943
00:35:25,523 --> 00:35:26,825
I'D LIKE TO GIVE THEM
TO YOU AS A GIFT.

944
00:35:26,858 --> 00:35:28,627
IF YOU LET ME.
AS A SORT OF A CELEBRATION.

945
00:35:28,660 --> 00:35:31,230
YOU SEE, YOU WERE
MY FIRST CUSTOMER.

946
00:35:31,263 --> 00:35:33,332
- WELL, THAT'S
AWFULLY SWEET, BUT--
- WEIRD.

947
00:35:33,365 --> 00:35:35,300
--YOU CAN'T AFFORD TO GIVE ME
A GIFT LIKE THAT, CAN YOU?

948
00:35:35,333 --> 00:35:37,203
OH, SURE I CAN,
I'VE GOT PLENTY OF MONEY.

949
00:35:37,237 --> 00:35:39,072
I'M NOT JUST AN ORDINARY
SHOE SALESMAN--

950
00:35:39,105 --> 00:35:42,073
[ALL]
♪ LIAR, LIAR, LIAR ♪

951
00:35:42,107 --> 00:35:44,377
--IF I LIKE IT AND DECIDE
TO STAY, WHY, MY DAD--

952
00:35:44,410 --> 00:35:45,812
THE CLOCK IS BUGGED!

953
00:35:45,845 --> 00:35:47,045
OH, I SEE.

954
00:35:47,078 --> 00:35:49,182
1,700 LIES LATER.

955
00:35:49,215 --> 00:35:51,717
AND, OF COURSE, I WAS
THE LAST ONE OUT OF SAIGON.

956
00:35:51,750 --> 00:35:53,218
THAT'S MY FIRST
BABY PICTURE.

957
00:35:53,252 --> 00:35:55,420
- ISN'T IT AWFUL?
- NO, I THINK IT'S KIND OF CUTE.

958
00:35:55,453 --> 00:35:57,022
DID I MENTION I'M
AN OLYMPIC CHAMPION?

959
00:35:57,055 --> 00:35:58,523
- --I WAS TEN.
- HEY, EVEN AT TEN,

960
00:35:58,557 --> 00:36:01,393
- YOU WERE GONNA BE BEAUTIFUL.
- WHAT HAPPENED?

961
00:36:01,427 --> 00:36:02,695
AND THAT'S AUNT HARRIET.

962
00:36:02,728 --> 00:36:03,897
'NUFF SAID.

963
00:36:03,930 --> 00:36:05,798
SHE SUFFERED FROM
CHRONIC INDIGESTION.

964
00:36:05,832 --> 00:36:07,433
YEAH, I GUESS SHE WAS
SUFFERING FROM SOMETHING.

965
00:36:07,467 --> 00:36:08,533
TAKE IT BACK! TAKE IT BACK!

966
00:36:08,567 --> 00:36:09,935
OH, SAY, IT'S LATE,
I HAVE TO BE

967
00:36:09,968 --> 00:36:11,370
AT THE PARADISE
IN A HALF HOUR.

968
00:36:11,403 --> 00:36:12,538
OH, WELL I'D BETTER GO, THEN.

969
00:36:12,572 --> 00:36:14,007
AND QUICK.

970
00:36:14,040 --> 00:36:16,508
SO, WILL I SEE YOU SOON?

971
00:36:16,542 --> 00:36:19,412
I HOPE SO, JIMMY.

972
00:36:19,445 --> 00:36:20,713
WOW.

973
00:36:20,747 --> 00:36:23,215
THIS IS ONE SUCCESSFUL
SHOE SALESMAN.

974
00:36:23,248 --> 00:36:25,483
OPEN MOUTH, CLOSE SALE.

975
00:36:25,517 --> 00:36:28,320
PARDON ME, I THOUGHT
YOU'D BE GONE.

976
00:36:28,353 --> 00:36:29,588
KIND OF LATE, AREN'T YOU?

977
00:36:29,622 --> 00:36:31,190
CAN I JUST TELL YOU
ABOUT MY MOM ONCE?

978
00:36:31,223 --> 00:36:34,093
OH, I WAS
JUST READY TO LEAVE.

979
00:36:34,127 --> 00:36:36,062
MISS VERA MOORE,
MR. JIMMY WILSON.

980
00:36:36,095 --> 00:36:38,497
- HOW DO YOU DO?
- I'M DOING FINE.

981
00:36:38,530 --> 00:36:39,965
SO ARE YOU, I SEE.

982
00:36:39,998 --> 00:36:42,200
- WELL, SO LONG, KITTY.
- BYE, JIMMY.

983
00:36:42,233 --> 00:36:45,070
QUACK QUACK QUACK.
QUACK QUACK.

984
00:36:45,103 --> 00:36:46,838
♪ OH, YES,
IT'S LATE AS NIGHT ♪

985
00:36:46,872 --> 00:36:48,340
♪ AND THE FEELING'S RIGHT ♪

986
00:36:48,373 --> 00:36:50,342
OH, WHAT A NIGHT.

987
00:36:50,375 --> 00:36:52,545
HEY, WHAT IS THIS?

988
00:36:52,578 --> 00:36:54,180
YOU'D BETTER WATCH YOUR STEP,
HADN'T YOU?

989
00:36:54,213 --> 00:36:56,348
WELL, NO PROBLEM
WITH MY NEW SHOES.

990
00:36:56,382 --> 00:36:58,317
- BLAKE?
- YEAH, BLAKE.

991
00:36:58,350 --> 00:37:00,953
IN CASE YOU'D FORGOTTEN,
HE'S MADLY IN LOVE WITH YOU.

992
00:37:00,987 --> 00:37:02,488
OH, BLAKE!

993
00:37:02,522 --> 00:37:05,523
YEAH, I KNOW.

994
00:37:05,557 --> 00:37:08,327
BUT JIMMY SEEMS SO DIFFERENT.
HE'S SO SWEET.

995
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:09,728
HE KNOWS MY SHOE SIZE.

996
00:37:09,762 --> 00:37:11,663
THE KIND OF A KID
EVERY GIRL DREAMS ABOUT.

997
00:37:11,697 --> 00:37:13,198
HE WON AN ESSAY CONTEST,
YOU KNOW.

998
00:37:13,232 --> 00:37:16,368
--DON'T TELL ME
IT'S LOVE AT FIRST SIGHT.

999
00:37:16,402 --> 00:37:19,505
WELL, WHAT'S SO IMPOSSIBLE
ABOUT THAT?

1000
00:37:19,538 --> 00:37:21,373
WHO KNOWS WHAT LURKS
IN THE HEARTS OF MEN?

1001
00:37:21,407 --> 00:37:23,008
THE SHADOW KNOWS.

1002
00:37:23,042 --> 00:37:25,778
- HE LIVES IN MONTICELLO.
- DOESN'T EVERYBODY?

1003
00:37:25,812 --> 00:37:28,513
I-- HUH?

1004
00:37:28,547 --> 00:37:32,017
HEY, I WON THE ESSAY C-- OH.

1005
00:37:32,050 --> 00:37:35,387
WELL, COME ON IN, WE INVITED
THE CAST FROM GIGI OVER.

1006
00:37:40,158 --> 00:37:42,193
- THANKS, SISTER.
- HEY, COME BACK WITH THAT!

1007
00:37:42,227 --> 00:37:45,363
WALT DISNEY INTERVIEWING
ANOTHER SNOW WHITE.

1008
00:37:45,397 --> 00:37:48,667
GEE, KIND OF SLOW NIGHT
FOR A MONDAY.

1009
00:37:48,700 --> 00:37:50,335
YOU KNOW, THE TROUBLE WITH
COCKTAIL PARTIES

1010
00:37:50,368 --> 00:37:51,570
IS THAT THEY END TOO SOON.

1011
00:37:51,603 --> 00:37:52,772
THEY DON'T HAVE TO.

1012
00:37:52,805 --> 00:37:54,107
YOU CAN MAKE THEM LAST
AS LONG AS YOU LIKE.

1013
00:37:54,140 --> 00:37:56,275
WELL, I'D LIKE THIS ONE
TO LAST AT LEAST THREE DAYS.

1014
00:37:56,308 --> 00:37:58,310
STEP-ONE-TWO-THREE-FOUR
AND STEP.

1015
00:37:58,343 --> 00:37:59,845
--HE'S AT THE BEACH.
HE'S GOT LOTS OF ROOM,

1016
00:37:59,878 --> 00:38:01,847
LOTS OF LIQUOR.
WE COULD SPEND THE WEEKEND.

1017
00:38:01,880 --> 00:38:03,782
THAT'S A WONDERFUL IDEA.

1018
00:38:03,815 --> 00:38:05,650
LISTEN EVERYBODY,
HOW ABOUT GOING DOWN

1019
00:38:05,683 --> 00:38:07,487
TO JACK TAYLOR'S AT THE BEACH
FOR THE WEEKEND?

1020
00:38:07,520 --> 00:38:08,753
[PEOPLE SHOUT]

1021
00:38:08,787 --> 00:38:12,057
ANYBODY KNOW
WHO JACK TAYLOR IS?

1022
00:38:12,090 --> 00:38:14,493
HEY, DON'T LEAVE
'CAUSE I'M HERE.

1023
00:38:14,527 --> 00:38:16,162
HUH?

1024
00:38:16,195 --> 00:38:18,163
I WON THE...
ESSAY... CONTEST.

1025
00:38:18,197 --> 00:38:19,598
--TO THE BEACH TONIGHT.

1026
00:38:19,632 --> 00:38:21,400
OH, JIMMY, I DIDN'T KNOW
YOU WERE HOME.

1027
00:38:21,433 --> 00:38:23,502
WELL, I GUESS YOU FORGOT.
TOMORROW'S MY BIRTHDAY.

1028
00:38:23,535 --> 00:38:24,970
IT WAS YOUR BIRTHDAY
LAST YEAR!

1029
00:38:25,003 --> 00:38:27,440
--BUT HERE, HERE'S $20.

1030
00:38:27,473 --> 00:38:29,242
GO OUT AND HAVE A PARTY
WITH YOUR OWN FRIENDS.

1031
00:38:29,275 --> 00:38:30,743
TAKE OUT YOUR BEST GIRL.

1032
00:38:30,777 --> 00:38:33,378
WELL, THAT'S WHAT I WANTED
TO TALK TO YOU AND MOM ABOUT.

1033
00:38:33,412 --> 00:38:35,147
OH, THEN THERE IS A WOMAN
IN THE CASE.

1034
00:38:35,180 --> 00:38:37,450
AND WHAT A WOMAN--
TAKE A LOOK AT THIS.

1035
00:38:37,483 --> 00:38:39,818
HEY, GANG,
JIMMY'S GOT A GIRL.

1036
00:38:39,852 --> 00:38:41,453
OH-HO-HO.

1037
00:38:41,487 --> 00:38:44,257
- LET'S STRIP HIM!
- YEAH, COME ON!

1038
00:38:46,092 --> 00:38:47,927
WAIT A MINUTE,
BY MY CALCULATIONS,

1039
00:38:47,960 --> 00:38:49,428
HE'S MADE $35.

1040
00:38:49,462 --> 00:38:51,763
MINUS $9.95 FOR THE SHOES.

1041
00:38:54,500 --> 00:38:56,002
MOM'S SWELL.

1042
00:38:56,035 --> 00:38:59,372
BIRTHDAY SCAM WORKED AGAIN.

1043
00:38:59,405 --> 00:39:01,973
UH. SO THAT'S WHY
THAT GUY ON THE BUS

1044
00:39:02,007 --> 00:39:04,577
WAS LOOKING AT ME ALL FUNNY.

1045
00:39:04,610 --> 00:39:08,347
OH, A WISE GUY, EH?

1046
00:39:08,380 --> 00:39:11,550
HAPPY BIRTHDAY TO ME.

1047
00:39:11,583 --> 00:39:15,153
GUESS I COULD BUY
A FRIEND WITH THIS.

1048
00:39:15,187 --> 00:39:17,857
JACK TAYLOR'S
GOT A GREAT PLACE!

1049
00:39:19,292 --> 00:39:23,162
WELCOME BACK TO THE 12TH ANNUAL
ESSAY AWARDS CEREMONY.

1050
00:39:23,195 --> 00:39:24,530
AH, MONSIEUR WICK.

1051
00:39:24,563 --> 00:39:26,232
- DO YOU DESIRE A TABLE?
- UH, YES.

1052
00:39:26,265 --> 00:39:28,500
- THIS WAY PL--
- DO YOU KNOW WHEN
MS. KITTY REED GOES ON?

1053
00:39:28,533 --> 00:39:29,835
RIGHT AFTER THIS NUMBER.

1054
00:39:29,868 --> 00:39:31,870
SHE'S PUTTING ON
HER TASSELS NOW.

1055
00:39:34,307 --> 00:39:35,775
HI, I'M THE ESSAY GUY.

1056
00:39:35,808 --> 00:39:38,143
HI! ESSAY GUY'S HERE.
THAT'S ME.

1057
00:39:38,177 --> 00:39:40,412
ESSAY'S MY NAME.

1058
00:39:40,445 --> 00:39:42,915
- MONSIEUR.
- MONSIEUR,
I MUST WARN YOU.

1059
00:39:42,948 --> 00:39:44,150
THE ACT IS MESSY.

1060
00:39:44,183 --> 00:39:46,218
YOU WILL GET WET
ON THIS RIDE.

1061
00:39:46,252 --> 00:39:49,555
[SPEAKS FRENCH]

1062
00:39:49,588 --> 00:39:51,957
UH, WELL, BRING ME
TWO CHAMPAGNE COCKTAILS.

1063
00:39:51,990 --> 00:39:53,558
- TWO?
- YES, TWO.

1064
00:39:53,592 --> 00:39:56,028
YEAH, AND PUT THEM IN ONE OF
THOSE BIG SLURPEE GLASSES TOO.

1065
00:39:56,062 --> 00:39:58,730
♪♪ [HORN SECTION]

1066
00:39:58,763 --> 00:40:01,167
- CHARGE!
- NOW, LADIES
AND GENTLEMEN.

1067
00:40:01,200 --> 00:40:03,135
IT GIVES ME GREAT PLEASURE
TO INTRODUCE TO YOU

1068
00:40:03,168 --> 00:40:05,603
OUR SINGING STAR,
MISS KITTY REED.

1069
00:40:07,540 --> 00:40:10,075
THIS IS HER OVER HERE.
ISN'T SHE BEAUTIFUL?

1070
00:40:10,108 --> 00:40:11,543
TAKE A LOOK.

1071
00:40:11,577 --> 00:40:14,078
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

1072
00:40:14,112 --> 00:40:15,213
♪♪ [MUSIC STARTS]

1073
00:40:15,247 --> 00:40:17,215
[SERVO LAUGHS NERVOUSLY]

1074
00:40:17,248 --> 00:40:19,752
GEENA DAVIS.

1075
00:40:19,785 --> 00:40:21,487
♪ ARE YOU HAPPY ♪

1076
00:40:21,520 --> 00:40:24,022
- DEFINE HAPPY.
- ♪ IN YOUR WORK? ♪

1077
00:40:24,055 --> 00:40:26,625
AH, DON'T SING THIS
TO ME ON A MONDAY.

1078
00:40:26,658 --> 00:40:29,462
♪ EVER SHIRK? ♪

1079
00:40:29,495 --> 00:40:31,730
♪ DOES YOUR MORNING MENU ♪

1080
00:40:31,763 --> 00:40:33,432
♪ REALLY SEND YOU
ON YOUR WAY? ♪

1081
00:40:33,465 --> 00:40:35,367
I'LL HAVE THE SKILLET
SCRAMBLED AND FRIES.

1082
00:40:35,400 --> 00:40:36,902
♪ GREET EACH DAY ♪

1083
00:40:36,935 --> 00:40:39,672
♪ AND IS IT A STEAL?
A REAL APPEAL ♪

1084
00:40:39,705 --> 00:40:41,373
♪ TO FEEL YOU'RE
EARNING YOUR PAY? ♪

1085
00:40:41,407 --> 00:40:43,175
I CAME TO TELL YOU YOU HAVE
TO PAY FOR THE SHOES.

1086
00:40:43,208 --> 00:40:45,543
♪ ARE YOU GRATEFUL ♪

1087
00:40:45,577 --> 00:40:47,913
♪ YOU'RE ALIVE? ♪

1088
00:40:47,947 --> 00:40:49,682
♪ IS YOUR DAY FULL-- ♪

1089
00:40:49,715 --> 00:40:51,350
HEY, WALTER LANCE!

1090
00:40:51,383 --> 00:40:52,752
HEY, WHAT DO YOU KNOW?

1091
00:40:52,785 --> 00:40:54,820
♪ LIVIN' IN THE RHYTHM ♪

1092
00:40:54,853 --> 00:40:57,255
♪ THAT I'M SPEAKING OF ♪

1093
00:40:57,288 --> 00:40:58,823
CAN I ORDER PLEASE!

1094
00:40:58,857 --> 00:41:01,993
♪ --YOUR WORK
IF YOU'RE IN LOVE ♪

1095
00:41:02,027 --> 00:41:05,763
I KNOW HOW TOAST WORKS.

1096
00:41:05,797 --> 00:41:08,333
♪ ARE YOU HAPPY ♪

1097
00:41:08,367 --> 00:41:09,735
♪ IN YOUR WORK? ♪

1098
00:41:09,768 --> 00:41:11,003
WELL, I WAS.

1099
00:41:11,037 --> 00:41:13,405
♪ THOUGH YOU'RE BANKER ♪

1100
00:41:13,438 --> 00:41:16,075
♪ OR A CLERK ♪

1101
00:41:16,108 --> 00:41:17,643
WHERE IS THIS GUY?
DO YOU KNOW WHAT TABLE?

1102
00:41:17,677 --> 00:41:19,412
- ♪ --DELICIOUS-- ♪
- HEY, SHOWBIZ,

1103
00:41:19,445 --> 00:41:20,845
CAN WE GET OUR FOOD
OVER HERE?

1104
00:41:20,878 --> 00:41:23,048
♪ --DO YOUR HOURS SPIN? ♪

1105
00:41:23,082 --> 00:41:25,850
♪ AND ARE YOU AGLOW
THE CHECKS YOU PULL ♪

1106
00:41:25,883 --> 00:41:27,553
♪ KNOW YOU'RE
MAKING YOUR TIN ♪

1107
00:41:27,587 --> 00:41:29,053
BITE ME.

1108
00:41:29,087 --> 00:41:31,457
♪ COULD YOU CARRY ♪

1109
00:41:31,490 --> 00:41:32,858
♪ CRUMBS AWAY ♪

1110
00:41:32,892 --> 00:41:34,025
UH, NO, HEH.

1111
00:41:34,058 --> 00:41:36,495
♪ ARE YOU MARRIED ♪

1112
00:41:36,528 --> 00:41:38,563
- ♪ WITH YOUR TRAY? ♪
- IT'S DIFFICULT.

1113
00:41:38,597 --> 00:41:41,233
- ♪ NEVER-- ♪
- UH, I'LL JUST GO NOW.

1114
00:41:41,267 --> 00:41:42,735
♪ SPEAKING OF-- ♪

1115
00:41:42,768 --> 00:41:44,035
- HEY, I GOT A GREAT IDEA.
- WHAT?

1116
00:41:44,068 --> 00:41:45,570
YOU GO GET GYPSY.
I'LL GET THE COSTUMES.

1117
00:41:45,603 --> 00:41:48,007
IT JUST MIGHT WORK.

1118
00:41:55,280 --> 00:41:57,182
♪♪ [MUSIC STARTS]

1119
00:41:57,215 --> 00:41:59,017
[SERVO LIP-SYNCS MOVIE]
AND NOW, LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.

1120
00:41:59,050 --> 00:42:00,752
IT GIVES ME GREAT PLEASURE
TO INTRODUCE TO YOU

1121
00:42:00,785 --> 00:42:03,288
OUR SINGING STAR,
MISS KITTY REED.

1122
00:42:03,322 --> 00:42:06,758
[APPLAUSE]

1123
00:42:06,792 --> 00:42:08,760
THANK YOU, THANK YOU.

1124
00:42:08,793 --> 00:42:11,797
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.
THANK YOU.

1125
00:42:11,830 --> 00:42:13,898
♪♪ [MUSIC STARTS]

1126
00:42:17,737 --> 00:42:20,005
♪ ARE YOU HAPPY ♪

1127
00:42:20,038 --> 00:42:22,608
♪ IN YOUR WORK? ♪

1128
00:42:22,642 --> 00:42:25,143
♪ DO YOU NEVER ♪

1129
00:42:25,177 --> 00:42:27,545
♪ EVER SHIRK? ♪

1130
00:42:27,578 --> 00:42:29,415
♪ DOES YOUR MORNING MENU ♪

1131
00:42:29,448 --> 00:42:32,483
♪ REALLY SEND YOU
ON YOUR WAY? ♪

1132
00:42:32,517 --> 00:42:35,020
♪ DO YOU GREET EACH DAY ♪

1133
00:42:35,053 --> 00:42:37,623
♪ AND IS IT A STEAL?
A REAL APPEAL ♪

1134
00:42:37,657 --> 00:42:40,725
♪ TO FEEL YOU'RE
EARNING YOUR PAY? ♪

1135
00:42:40,758 --> 00:42:43,128
♪ ARE YOU GRATEFUL ♪

1136
00:42:43,162 --> 00:42:45,630
♪ YOU'RE ALIVE? ♪

1137
00:42:45,663 --> 00:42:48,167
♪ IS YOUR DAY FULL ♪

1138
00:42:48,200 --> 00:42:50,402
♪ NINE TO FIVE? ♪

1139
00:42:50,435 --> 00:42:52,470
♪ LIVIN' IN THE RHYTHM ♪

1140
00:42:52,503 --> 00:42:55,107
♪ THAT I'M SPEAKING OF ♪

1141
00:42:55,140 --> 00:42:57,175
♪ YOU'LL BE HAPPY
IN YOUR WORK ♪

1142
00:42:57,208 --> 00:42:59,512
♪ IF YOU'RE IN LOVE ♪

1143
00:43:03,815 --> 00:43:06,052
♪ ARE YOU HAPPY ♪

1144
00:43:06,085 --> 00:43:08,720
♪ IN YOUR WORK? ♪

1145
00:43:08,753 --> 00:43:10,990
♪ THOUGH YOU'RE BANKER ♪

1146
00:43:11,023 --> 00:43:13,592
♪ OR A CLERK ♪

1147
00:43:13,625 --> 00:43:16,128
♪ ARE YOUR DISHES
AS DELICIOUS ♪

1148
00:43:16,162 --> 00:43:18,730
♪ AS YOUR HAPPY GRIN? ♪

1149
00:43:18,763 --> 00:43:21,033
♪ DO YOUR HOURS SPIN? ♪

1150
00:43:21,067 --> 00:43:23,802
♪ AND ARE YOU AGLOW
THE CHECKS YOU PULL ♪

1151
00:43:23,835 --> 00:43:26,605
♪ NO, YOU'RE MAKING
YOUR TIN ♪

1152
00:43:26,638 --> 00:43:29,207
♪ COULD YOU CARRY ♪

1153
00:43:29,240 --> 00:43:31,777
♪ CRUMBS AWAY ♪

1154
00:43:31,810 --> 00:43:34,447
♪ ARE YOU MARRIED ♪

1155
00:43:34,480 --> 00:43:36,648
♪ WITH YOUR TRAY? ♪

1156
00:43:36,682 --> 00:43:38,383
♪ LIVIN' IN THE RHYTHM ♪

1157
00:43:38,417 --> 00:43:41,253
♪ THAT I'M SPEAKING OF ♪

1158
00:43:41,287 --> 00:43:43,155
♪ YOU'LL BE HAPPY
IN YOUR WORK ♪

1159
00:43:43,188 --> 00:43:44,657
♪ IF YOU'RE IN LOVE ♪

1160
00:43:44,690 --> 00:43:45,823
♪♪ [MUSIC SLOWS, STOPS]

1161
00:43:45,857 --> 00:43:47,258
OH, WHAT HAPPENED?

1162
00:43:47,292 --> 00:43:49,528
OH, GEE, I THINK WE SPILLED
SOME CHAMPAGNE COCKTAIL

1163
00:43:49,562 --> 00:43:51,163
INTO CAMBOT'S
SEQUENCER HERE.

1164
00:43:51,197 --> 00:43:53,365
- SORRY EVERYBODY, SORRY.
- TOM SERVO, YOU KNOW
WHAT TO DO.

1165
00:43:53,398 --> 00:43:54,633
GET DOWN THERE
AND MOP THAT UP.

1166
00:43:54,667 --> 00:43:56,435
I'M SORRY, GYPSY,
IT WAS GOING SO GOOD.

1167
00:43:56,468 --> 00:43:58,670
WELL, I GUESS WE'LL HAVE
TO TAKE IT FROM THE TOP!

1168
00:43:58,703 --> 00:44:00,105
OH NO! NOT AGAIN!

1169
00:44:00,138 --> 00:44:01,307
[ALL CLAMOR]

1170
00:44:01,340 --> 00:44:04,242
I THINK WE GOT
MOVIE SIGN!

1171
00:44:16,955 --> 00:44:18,490
OH, THANKS.

1172
00:44:18,523 --> 00:44:20,258
AND NOW, THOM McAN
AND THE PAYLESS ORCHESTRA.

1173
00:44:21,893 --> 00:44:23,795
WITH COLE HAAN
ON THE SAXOPHONE,

1174
00:44:23,828 --> 00:44:25,130
THEN THE NATURALIZERS SING

1175
00:44:25,163 --> 00:44:26,832
SOMETHING BY
JOHNSTON AND MURPHY.

1176
00:44:26,865 --> 00:44:29,468
I SYNTHESIZED ANIMAL PROTEIN
IN MY LAB TODAY.

1177
00:44:31,670 --> 00:44:33,438
YOU KNOW, I'M GLAD
YOU CAME OVER AT THAT.

1178
00:44:33,472 --> 00:44:34,840
- ARE YOU REALLY?
- NO.

1179
00:44:34,873 --> 00:44:36,208
WELL, IF WE'RE
GONNA BE FRIENDS,

1180
00:44:36,242 --> 00:44:38,210
IT'LL GIVE US A CHANCE
TO GET BETTER ACQUAINTED.

1181
00:44:38,243 --> 00:44:40,478
OH, I FEEL AS THOUGH I'VE
KNOWN YOU FOR YEARS ALREADY.

1182
00:44:40,512 --> 00:44:42,113
OH, YOU DO?

1183
00:44:42,147 --> 00:44:44,315
WELL, SUPPOSE YOU START TELLING
ME SOMETHING ABOUT MYSELF.

1184
00:44:44,348 --> 00:44:45,650
- ALL RIGHT.
- WELL, YOU'RE HOT.

1185
00:44:45,683 --> 00:44:47,218
LET'S SEE, WHEN YOU WERE
TEN YEARS OLD--

1186
00:44:47,252 --> 00:44:48,687
OH, NOW, WAIT A MINUTE.

1187
00:44:48,720 --> 00:44:51,357
THAT'S GONNA
BE A LONG STORY.

1188
00:44:51,390 --> 00:44:52,858
SUPPOSE WE SIT
THE REST OF THIS ONE OUT.

1189
00:44:52,892 --> 00:44:55,127
OKAY.

1190
00:44:57,195 --> 00:44:58,530
I TOOK THE LIBERTY
OF SITTING HERE.

1191
00:44:58,563 --> 00:44:59,898
I HOPE YOU DON'T MIND.

1192
00:44:59,932 --> 00:45:02,200
- NOT AT ALL.
- WHO ARE YOU?

1193
00:45:02,233 --> 00:45:03,668
OH, THIS IS JIMMY WILSON.

1194
00:45:03,702 --> 00:45:05,603
BOY FROM MY HOMETOWN.

1195
00:45:05,637 --> 00:45:07,105
I MET HIM TODAY BY ACCIDENT.

1196
00:45:07,138 --> 00:45:08,740
THIS IS MR. BLAKE, JIMMY.
MY BOSS.

1197
00:45:08,773 --> 00:45:09,942
HOW DO YOU DO?

1198
00:45:09,975 --> 00:45:11,810
I'M GLAD TO KNOW
ANY FRIEND OF KITTY'S.

1199
00:45:11,843 --> 00:45:13,445
YOU GONNA BE IN TOWN LONG,
MR. WILSON?

1200
00:45:13,478 --> 00:45:16,013
- I LIVE HERE.
- IN A CASTLE AND STUFF.

1201
00:45:16,047 --> 00:45:17,715
I GUESS YOU SEE
QUITE A CHANGE IN KITTY

1202
00:45:17,748 --> 00:45:19,083
SINCE THE LAST TIME
YOU SAW HER, HUH?

1203
00:45:19,117 --> 00:45:20,452
OH, NOT SO VERY MUCH.

1204
00:45:20,485 --> 00:45:22,087
OF COURSE,
HER CLOTHES ARE DIFFERENT.

1205
00:45:22,120 --> 00:45:23,422
YES, I'M SURE THEY ARE.
YOU SEE,

1206
00:45:23,455 --> 00:45:24,723
SHE SPENDS
A LOT MORE NOWADAYS

1207
00:45:24,757 --> 00:45:26,525
THEN SHE DID BACK IN IOWA.

1208
00:45:26,558 --> 00:45:28,560
- OOH, THAT'S COLD. OUCH.
- RIGHT, KITTY?

1209
00:45:28,593 --> 00:45:30,028
OKAY, CHARLIE.

1210
00:45:30,062 --> 00:45:31,563
NOW, IF YOU'LL EXCUSE US--

1211
00:45:31,597 --> 00:45:33,198
OH, SURE, GO RIGHT AHEAD.

1212
00:45:33,232 --> 00:45:36,668
THANK YOU.

1213
00:45:36,702 --> 00:45:38,237
I'M WAITING FOR A CALL
FROM THE PRESIDENT,

1214
00:45:38,270 --> 00:45:41,740
SO I COULDN'T DANCE ANYWAY.

1215
00:45:41,773 --> 00:45:43,075
SO WHO'S THE STIFF?

1216
00:45:43,108 --> 00:45:45,277
WHERE'D YOU RUN INTO
LITTLE LORD FAUNTLEROY?

1217
00:45:45,310 --> 00:45:46,512
IN A SHOE STORE.

1218
00:45:46,545 --> 00:45:48,513
I WENT IN TO BUY SOME SHOES,
AND THERE HE WAS.

1219
00:45:48,547 --> 00:45:49,782
ISN'T THAT
A FUNNY COINCIDENCE?

1220
00:45:49,815 --> 00:45:51,650
SELLING SHOES, HUH?

1221
00:45:51,683 --> 00:45:52,918
HI, I SELL SHOES.

1222
00:45:52,952 --> 00:45:54,520
SEEMS LIKE A NICE KID.

1223
00:45:54,553 --> 00:45:56,522
I MIGHT BE ABLE
TO HELP HIM DO BETTER.

1224
00:45:56,555 --> 00:45:58,123
LOOK, CHARLIE, LAY OFF.

1225
00:45:58,157 --> 00:45:59,558
I'M ONLY TRYING TO HELP HIM.

1226
00:45:59,592 --> 00:46:01,260
I KNOW OTHER PEOPLE YOU'VE
HELPED, AND THEY ALL--

1227
00:46:01,293 --> 00:46:03,328
--END UP LIKE
WHEN YOU WAS A KID.

1228
00:46:03,362 --> 00:46:06,198
JUST WHOSE WELFARE ARE YOU
INTERESTED IN? HIS OR MINE?

1229
00:46:06,232 --> 00:46:07,465
YOURS, OF COURSE.

1230
00:46:07,498 --> 00:46:09,502
OKAY, SEE THAT
IT STAYS THAT WAY.

1231
00:46:09,535 --> 00:46:11,203
I WANT YOU TO GIVE ME
A BUILDUP FOR THE KID.

1232
00:46:11,237 --> 00:46:13,005
TELL HIM WHAT
A GREAT GUY I AM.

1233
00:46:13,038 --> 00:46:15,240
WHAT A GOOD FRIEND
I'VE BEEN TO YOU.

1234
00:46:15,273 --> 00:46:16,708
I MIGHT FIND HIM USEFUL.

1235
00:46:16,742 --> 00:46:19,443
THEN I'LL THROW HIM AWAY
LIKE A PAPER TOWEL.

1236
00:46:23,282 --> 00:46:26,117
IN OUR AUDIENCE TONIGHT?
TONY "BIG TUNA" ACCARDO.

1237
00:46:26,150 --> 00:46:29,655
STAND UP, TONY.

1238
00:46:29,688 --> 00:46:31,623
I WENT AND LIBERATED FRANCE
WHILE YOU WERE DANCING.

1239
00:46:31,657 --> 00:46:34,125
YEAH, I FIXED YOUR CHAIR TOO.
DOESN'T SQUEAK ANYMORE.

1240
00:46:34,158 --> 00:46:35,793
WELL, I ORDERED FOR ALL OF US.
I HOPE IT'S ALL RIGHT.

1241
00:46:35,827 --> 00:46:37,395
BUT, YOU SEE,
TOMORROW'S MY BIRTHDAY,

1242
00:46:37,428 --> 00:46:39,565
- AND I'M CELEBRATING.
- OKAY, ENOUGH WITH
THE BIRTHDAY.

1243
00:46:39,598 --> 00:46:41,833
ALL RIGHT. AS A MATTER OF FACT,
WE'LL MAKE A NIGHT OUT OF IT.

1244
00:46:41,867 --> 00:46:43,335
- WHAT DO YOU SAY, KITTEN?
- MEOW!

1245
00:46:43,368 --> 00:46:45,603
WELL-- FINE, I'M FOR IT.

1246
00:46:45,637 --> 00:46:47,472
WELL, HERE YOU ARE, JIMMY.
HAPPY BIRTHDAY TO YOU.

1247
00:46:47,505 --> 00:46:50,908
- THANK YOU.
- HAPPY BIRTHDAY, JIMMY.

1248
00:46:50,942 --> 00:46:53,145
SO THEN MY MOM SAYS
TO ROOSEVELT AND CHURCHILL,

1249
00:46:53,178 --> 00:46:56,182
SHE SAYS, "WHAT ABOUT SOME KIND
OF LEND-LEASE PROGRAM?"

1250
00:46:58,317 --> 00:46:59,885
SSSSO...

1251
00:46:59,918 --> 00:47:03,688
SUDDENLY THEY'RE AT
A HEE-HAW WRAP PARTY.

1252
00:47:03,722 --> 00:47:05,157
OH, THEY'D BETTER NOT SING

1253
00:47:05,190 --> 00:47:07,092
"ACHY BREAKY HEART" AGAIN.

1254
00:47:09,828 --> 00:47:11,597
JULES AND JIM.

1255
00:47:14,498 --> 00:47:16,235
WELP, WE'RE GOING
TO THE BUFFET.

1256
00:47:19,437 --> 00:47:21,440
♪ OH, YOU GROOVIN' ♪

1257
00:47:21,473 --> 00:47:24,508
♪ WITH YOUR CUCKOO WORK,
HEY! ♪

1258
00:47:24,542 --> 00:47:26,043
EVERYTHING SATISFACTORY,
MR. BLAKE?

1259
00:47:26,077 --> 00:47:27,345
OH, FINE. THANKS, TRENT.

1260
00:47:27,378 --> 00:47:29,047
SAY, YOU HAVEN'T FORGOTTEN
ABOUT THAT PACKAGE

1261
00:47:29,080 --> 00:47:30,415
YOU LEFT WITH ME?

1262
00:47:30,448 --> 00:47:31,783
WELL, NO. NO.

1263
00:47:31,817 --> 00:47:33,018
I'LL HAVE IT PICKED UP
IN A COUPLE OF DAYS.

1264
00:47:33,052 --> 00:47:34,318
- OKAY.
- AND TRENT?

1265
00:47:34,352 --> 00:47:36,988
- I LOVE YOU.
- THIS PARTY'S ON THE KID.

1266
00:47:37,022 --> 00:47:38,757
THANKS.

1267
00:47:38,790 --> 00:47:40,092
SAY, WHAT'RE YOU
DOING TOMORROW?

1268
00:47:40,125 --> 00:47:41,260
OR TODAY, I GUESS.

1269
00:47:41,293 --> 00:47:42,693
IT MUST BE
SUNDAY MORNING ALREADY.

1270
00:47:42,727 --> 00:47:44,395
IT IS-- WHY?
WHAT'S ON YOUR MIND?

1271
00:47:44,428 --> 00:47:45,863
WELL, I THOUGHT WITH
MY FOLKS AWAY,

1272
00:47:45,897 --> 00:47:47,632
THAT WE COULD SPEND
MY BIRTHDAY TOGETHER.

1273
00:47:47,665 --> 00:47:49,167
OH, WHY NOT?

1274
00:47:49,200 --> 00:47:51,670
I'LL TELL YOU JIMMY, YOU COME
TO MY APARTMENT ABOUT 12:00,

1275
00:47:51,703 --> 00:47:53,305
AND I'LL FIX YOU
AN OLD-FASHIONED
BIRTHDAY BREAKFAST.

1276
00:47:53,338 --> 00:47:55,107
YOU KNOW,
COFFEE AND CIGARETTES.

1277
00:47:55,140 --> 00:47:57,108
OH, SWELL. YOU KNOW,
TONIGHT'S BEEN GREAT,

1278
00:47:57,142 --> 00:47:59,110
ONLY IT'D BE NICER IF
MR. BLAKE HADN'T COME ALONG.

1279
00:47:59,143 --> 00:48:01,447
YOU'D ASK HIM, HE'D SAY
THE SAME ABOUT YOU.

1280
00:48:01,480 --> 00:48:03,048
DON'T YOU LIKE MR. BLAKE?

1281
00:48:03,082 --> 00:48:04,817
OH, I GUESS HE'S
ALL RIGHT, ONLY...

1282
00:48:04,850 --> 00:48:06,285
WELL, ISN'T HE ALL RIGHT?

1283
00:48:06,318 --> 00:48:08,187
YEAH, I GUESS.

1284
00:48:08,220 --> 00:48:09,453
WELL, DON'T YOU LIKE HIM?

1285
00:48:09,487 --> 00:48:11,490
HE'S MY MAIN SQUEEZE, JIMMY.

1286
00:48:11,523 --> 00:48:12,790
--I WOULDN'T WANT YOU
TO BE LIKE HIM.

1287
00:48:12,823 --> 00:48:14,192
WHY? WHAT'S WRONG WITH HIM?

1288
00:48:14,225 --> 00:48:16,395
OH, HE'S A MONEY MAN.
WANTS TO GET RICH QUICK.

1289
00:48:16,428 --> 00:48:17,895
HEY, IS THAT BAD?

1290
00:48:17,928 --> 00:48:19,597
SOMETIMES.

1291
00:48:19,630 --> 00:48:20,965
I THINK YOU HAVE
A BETTER FUTURE

1292
00:48:20,998 --> 00:48:22,333
IN THE SHOE BUSINESS.

1293
00:48:22,367 --> 00:48:24,535
HOW ABOUT ESSAY-WRITING?
I'M GOOD AT THAT.

1294
00:48:26,270 --> 00:48:28,007
THANK YOU.

1295
00:48:30,375 --> 00:48:32,677
OH, KITTY, TRENT'S BEEN ASKING
IF YOU'D SING A SONG.

1296
00:48:32,710 --> 00:48:34,145
WHY, I'D BE GLAD TO,
MR. TRENT.

1297
00:48:34,178 --> 00:48:36,247
THANKS, MS. REED, IT'LL BE
A TREAT FOR MY PATRONS.

1298
00:48:36,280 --> 00:48:40,085
- EXCUSE ME.
- HOW ABOUT
"LOVE TO LOVE YOU BABY"?

1299
00:48:40,118 --> 00:48:43,388
SO, JIMMY, DO YOU LIKE
YOUR KNEECAPS?

1300
00:48:43,422 --> 00:48:44,723
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,

1301
00:48:44,757 --> 00:48:46,625
I HAVE A BIG SURPRISE
FOR YOU THIS EVENING.

1302
00:48:46,658 --> 00:48:47,958
I'M RUDOLPH HESS.

1303
00:48:47,992 --> 00:48:49,193
--MS. KITTY REED.

1304
00:48:49,227 --> 00:48:51,397
HEY, WE WANT GRANDPA JONES!

1305
00:48:51,430 --> 00:48:53,665
YOU'RE TOO OLD
TO CUT THE MUSTARD!

1306
00:48:53,698 --> 00:48:55,233
YOU KNOW ANYTHING
BY DONNA SUMMER?

1307
00:48:55,267 --> 00:48:57,235
- NICE GIRL, ISN'T SHE?
- OH, SHE SURE IS.

1308
00:48:57,268 --> 00:48:59,003
I'VE NEVER MET
ANYONE LIKE HER BEFORE.

1309
00:48:59,037 --> 00:49:00,372
TAKE IT BACK, TAKE IT BACK!

1310
00:49:00,405 --> 00:49:02,340
--EXPENSIVE GIRL
TO TAKE OUT.

1311
00:49:02,373 --> 00:49:05,710
OH, NOTHING'S TOO GOOD
FOR A GIRL LIKE HER.

1312
00:49:05,743 --> 00:49:07,912
♪♪ [MUSIC STARTS]

1313
00:49:07,945 --> 00:49:09,280
HONEY, DON'T SLOUCH.

1314
00:49:09,313 --> 00:49:12,417
UP STRAIGHT.

1315
00:49:12,450 --> 00:49:13,718
WHEE!

1316
00:49:13,752 --> 00:49:17,522
♪ LOVE CAME BETWEEN US ♪

1317
00:49:17,555 --> 00:49:21,192
♪ SHOWED US THE WAY ♪

1318
00:49:21,225 --> 00:49:22,560
♪ LOVE MUST'VE SEEN US ♪

1319
00:49:22,593 --> 00:49:24,562
THE SILO OF POWER HORN SECTION.

1320
00:49:24,595 --> 00:49:27,032
[BOTS LAUGH]

1321
00:49:27,065 --> 00:49:29,333
DING DING! ORDER UP!
COME ON, PICK IT UP!

1322
00:49:29,367 --> 00:49:31,235
♪ WE WERE GOING THIS WAY ♪

1323
00:49:31,268 --> 00:49:33,138
♪ THAT WAY, THIS WAY ♪

1324
00:49:33,172 --> 00:49:35,373
♪ THEN IT TOOK US
BY THE HAND ♪

1325
00:49:35,407 --> 00:49:36,908
WAIT A SECOND-- SHE'S GOT

1326
00:49:36,942 --> 00:49:38,943
A PIG IN A BLANKET
ON HER HEAD.

1327
00:49:38,977 --> 00:49:41,145
♪ SHOWED US THE KISS WAY ♪

1328
00:49:41,178 --> 00:49:43,548
♪ TO THE PROMISED LAND ♪

1329
00:49:43,582 --> 00:49:45,650
THE "KISS WAY
TO THE PROMISED LAND"?

1330
00:49:45,683 --> 00:49:48,587
♪ --RECOMMENDED ♪

1331
00:49:48,620 --> 00:49:51,088
♪ TAKING A SPIN ♪

1332
00:49:51,122 --> 00:49:53,425
YES, SATAN, SPEAK TO ME
THROUGH THIS SONG.

1333
00:49:53,458 --> 00:49:55,860
[CROW CHUCKLES]

1334
00:49:55,893 --> 00:49:57,995
♪ WE SHOULD GET IN ♪

1335
00:49:58,028 --> 00:50:00,432
♪ THE SWIM ♪

1336
00:50:00,465 --> 00:50:02,300
♪ RIGHT FROM THE START ♪

1337
00:50:02,333 --> 00:50:03,635
♪ MY HEART HAS ♪

1338
00:50:03,668 --> 00:50:05,270
♪ FELT NO PAIN ♪

1339
00:50:05,303 --> 00:50:08,173
'CAUSE I'M
HAND-DIPPED IN GIN.

1340
00:50:08,207 --> 00:50:10,308
♪ FOR GRASS
IS THE GREENEST ♪

1341
00:50:10,342 --> 00:50:12,443
- SHE'S LOOKING AT ME.
- NO, SHE'S LOOKING AT ME.

1342
00:50:12,477 --> 00:50:13,778
- AM TOO!
- AM NOT!

1343
00:50:13,812 --> 00:50:15,880
[BOTH] HUH?

1344
00:50:15,913 --> 00:50:18,617
ALL SKATE, NOW. ALL SKATE.

1345
00:50:18,650 --> 00:50:22,253
♪ LOVE CAME BETWEEN US ♪

1346
00:50:22,287 --> 00:50:23,555
♪ LA-DA-DA DA ♪

1347
00:50:23,588 --> 00:50:25,790
♪ FORGOT THE WORDS
A LITTLE BIT-AH ♪

1348
00:50:25,823 --> 00:50:27,425
♪ --MUST'VE SEEN US ♪

1349
00:50:27,458 --> 00:50:29,227
♪ WANDERING AROUND ♪

1350
00:50:29,260 --> 00:50:32,263
K-- KOWALSKI, TABLE
FOR SEVEN. KOWALSKI.

1351
00:50:32,297 --> 00:50:34,298
♪ WE WERE GOING THIS WAY ♪

1352
00:50:34,332 --> 00:50:36,333
♪ THAT WAY THIS WAY ♪

1353
00:50:36,367 --> 00:50:40,138
♪ THEN IT TOOK US
BY THE HAND ♪

1354
00:50:40,172 --> 00:50:41,573
- CHECK PLEASE!
- CHECK PLEASE!

1355
00:50:41,607 --> 00:50:43,375
ARE OUR MOZZARELLA STICKS
ALMOST UP?

1356
00:50:43,408 --> 00:50:44,810
CHECK PLEASE, PLEASE.

1357
00:50:44,843 --> 00:50:47,345
♪ --TO THE PROMISED LAND ♪

1358
00:50:49,213 --> 00:50:51,415
LAST CALL!
LAST CALL FOR ALCOHOL.

1359
00:50:51,448 --> 00:50:52,750
♪ -- RECOMMENDED ♪

1360
00:50:52,783 --> 00:50:54,185
[CHUCKLES] I LIKE SONGS.

1361
00:50:54,218 --> 00:50:55,887
♪ LA DA DA DA ♪

1362
00:50:55,920 --> 00:50:58,757
♪ DA-- LOVE SURE INTENDED ♪

1363
00:50:58,790 --> 00:51:01,560
♪ WE SHOULD
GET IN THE SWIM ♪

1364
00:51:01,593 --> 00:51:03,662
[SERVO MIMICS INTERCOM]
ALL CHEESE-BUSTERS

1365
00:51:03,695 --> 00:51:05,597
ARE NOW $1.45.

1366
00:51:05,630 --> 00:51:07,832
THERE IS ALSO A GREEN
AND WHITE STATION WAGON

1367
00:51:07,865 --> 00:51:10,135
PARKED IN THE DELIVERY ZONE.

1368
00:51:10,168 --> 00:51:12,170
[CHUCKLES] WEAR PANTS.

1369
00:51:12,203 --> 00:51:13,938
♪ THE GRASS
IS THE GREENEST ♪

1370
00:51:13,972 --> 00:51:15,840
♪ SINCE LOVE
CAME BETWEEN US ♪

1371
00:51:15,873 --> 00:51:17,275
♪ TO LEAD US DOWN ♪

1372
00:51:17,308 --> 00:51:18,610
♪ THE LANE-- ♪

1373
00:51:18,643 --> 00:51:20,045
♪ TO HELL ♪

1374
00:51:20,078 --> 00:51:21,747
♪ YOU SHOULD'VE SEEN US ♪

1375
00:51:21,780 --> 00:51:23,748
♪ WHEN LOVE
CAME BETWEEN US ♪

1376
00:51:23,782 --> 00:51:25,850
♪ TO LEAD US DOWN THAT ♪

1377
00:51:25,883 --> 00:51:28,853
♪ LOVER'S LANE ♪

1378
00:51:28,887 --> 00:51:31,990
BOY, SHE'S REALLY ROCKING
THIS MOTHER, ISN'T SHE?

1379
00:51:32,023 --> 00:51:34,558
- OUCH.
- THANK YOU!

1380
00:51:34,592 --> 00:51:37,095
OH, THE MOB'S GONE COUNTRY.

1381
00:51:37,128 --> 00:51:39,030
- THANK YOU, MS. REED.
- THANK YOU, MS. REED.

1382
00:51:39,063 --> 00:51:40,365
GEE, YOU WERE SWELL, KITTY.

1383
00:51:40,398 --> 00:51:42,400
- THANKS, JIMMY.
- SO, AS I WAS SAYING, JIMMY.

1384
00:51:42,433 --> 00:51:44,435
IF YOU'D LIKE TO ADD
TO YOUR INCOME SOMETIME,

1385
00:51:44,468 --> 00:51:46,437
I MIGHT BE ABLE TO THROW
A FEW ODD JOBS YOUR WAY.

1386
00:51:46,470 --> 00:51:47,638
WHAT KIND OF ODD JOBS?

1387
00:51:47,672 --> 00:51:49,207
OH, LITTLE THINGS
YOU COULD DO FOR ME.

1388
00:51:49,240 --> 00:51:51,175
- AFTER WORKING HOURS.
- SOD FARMING.

1389
00:51:51,208 --> 00:51:52,677
HERE'S MY CARD,
IF YOU'RE INTERESTED.

1390
00:51:52,710 --> 00:51:54,947
- LOOK ME UP SOMETIME.
- WELL, THANKS. I WILL.

1391
00:51:54,980 --> 00:51:56,982
- MOBS "R" US.
- WE GOT PLACES TO GO.

1392
00:51:57,015 --> 00:51:59,217
- WAITER, CHECK.
- CHECKMATE.

1393
00:52:02,453 --> 00:52:03,655
- OH, THANKS.
- OH, LET ME HAVE THAT.

1394
00:52:03,688 --> 00:52:05,157
YOU TOOK CARE OF IT
AT THE PARADISE.

1395
00:52:05,190 --> 00:52:07,092
- OKAY.
- I'LL JUST TAKE A-- OOP!

1396
00:52:07,125 --> 00:52:09,527
[SERVO STAMMERS]

1397
00:52:09,560 --> 00:52:11,830
JEEZ, WHO ATE
ALL THIS STUFF?

1398
00:52:11,863 --> 00:52:15,000
AND A COVER.

1399
00:52:15,033 --> 00:52:17,835
DO YOU REMEMBER
A FOURTH PERSON SITTING HERE?

1400
00:52:17,868 --> 00:52:20,172
GEE, I'M AFRAID I DON'T HAVE
QUITE ENOUGH CASH TO COVER THIS.

1401
00:52:20,205 --> 00:52:22,007
OH, THEY'LL TAKE A CHECK.

1402
00:52:22,040 --> 00:52:24,442
OH, WILL THEY? WELL,
HAVE YOU GOT A BLANK CHECK?

1403
00:52:24,475 --> 00:52:27,578
- SURE.
- HOW'RE YOU FIXED
FOR SOCKS AND UNDERWEAR?

1404
00:52:27,612 --> 00:52:29,747
HER CIGARETTE
IS VELCROED TO HER LIP.

1405
00:52:35,887 --> 00:52:37,922
I SEE YOU USE
THE SAME BANK I DO.

1406
00:52:37,955 --> 00:52:41,727
OH, WELL THEY'RE
YOUR CHECKS.

1407
00:52:41,760 --> 00:52:44,295
EVER GET BIT BY A DEAD BEE?

1408
00:52:45,830 --> 00:52:48,132
OH, I DON'T HAVE
ANY OTHER TABLES.

1409
00:52:48,165 --> 00:52:50,135
THAT'S OKAY.

1410
00:52:50,168 --> 00:52:52,037
IS EVERYTHING CURRENT,
MR. DISRAELI?

1411
00:52:52,070 --> 00:52:53,472
HERE, BUY YOURSELF
A ROTOTILLER.

1412
00:52:53,505 --> 00:52:54,838
WELL, LET'S GET GOING.

1413
00:52:54,872 --> 00:52:57,075
COME ON.

1414
00:52:58,310 --> 00:52:59,643
YES, SIR?

1415
00:52:59,677 --> 00:53:01,512
I WANT YOU TO GO TO THE BANK
FOR ME AND MAKE A DEPOSIT.

1416
00:53:01,545 --> 00:53:04,382
- YES, SIR.
- AND, UH, JIMMY?

1417
00:53:04,415 --> 00:53:05,850
- UH, I LOVE YOU.
- YOU MIGHT PUT THESE THROUGH.

1418
00:53:05,883 --> 00:53:07,285
MAYBE THEY'LL BE GOOD NOW.

1419
00:53:07,318 --> 00:53:08,687
THEY BOUNCE BACK AGAIN,

1420
00:53:08,720 --> 00:53:10,855
I'M GONNA PUT
THAT MR. SMITH IN JAIL.

1421
00:53:10,888 --> 00:53:12,023
GEE, THAT'S QUITE
A COINCIDENCE,

1422
00:53:12,057 --> 00:53:13,190
'CAUSE I JUST
WROTE A BAD CHECK,

1423
00:53:13,223 --> 00:53:16,060
AND IF I HAD SOME
EXTRA CASH, I-- OH.

1424
00:53:16,093 --> 00:53:18,397
ONE PLUS ONE IS... TWO.

1425
00:53:25,570 --> 00:53:28,138
♪ DO I KNOW WHERE
I'M GOING TO... ♪

1426
00:53:30,542 --> 00:53:32,443
♪ I'M STUPID, YES INDEED ♪

1427
00:53:32,477 --> 00:53:34,478
♪ I'M STUPID ♪

1428
00:53:37,015 --> 00:53:39,517
- WEE-HOO!
- [THEY MIMIC GUNFIGHT]

1429
00:53:39,550 --> 00:53:42,053
WEE-HOO!

1430
00:53:42,087 --> 00:53:45,390
AH, QUITE A LONG LINE
AT THE PETTY LARCENY WINDOW.

1431
00:53:45,423 --> 00:53:48,460
AH... ONE.

1432
00:53:48,493 --> 00:53:50,695
AH... TWO.

1433
00:53:52,230 --> 00:53:55,133
UH-OH, I THINK HE'S GONNA GIVE
MR. POTTER HIS NEWSPAPER.

1434
00:53:55,167 --> 00:53:57,035
RIGHT.

1435
00:53:59,370 --> 00:54:01,372
- MY MOM DOESN'T DRINK!
- TAKE THE OTHER WINDOW.

1436
00:54:01,405 --> 00:54:04,608
OH, THANKS.

1437
00:54:04,642 --> 00:54:06,010
WHAT'S THE SECRET WORD?

1438
00:54:06,043 --> 00:54:08,078
SAY THE SECRET WORD
AND WIN A HUNDRED DOLLARS.

1439
00:54:08,112 --> 00:54:09,613
I'D LIKE TO DEPOSIT
SOME GUILT

1440
00:54:09,647 --> 00:54:12,750
AND WITHDRAW
SOME DENIAL, PLEASE?

1441
00:54:12,783 --> 00:54:15,020
I'M SORRY, YOU CAN'T
DEPOSIT THIS.

1442
00:54:15,053 --> 00:54:17,855
OH.

1443
00:54:17,888 --> 00:54:19,157
I'M SORRY, YOU CAN'T

1444
00:54:19,190 --> 00:54:22,993
PUT THAT IN YOUR
POCKET EITHER.

1445
00:54:23,027 --> 00:54:25,163
NICE CUTICLES.

1446
00:54:27,265 --> 00:54:29,900
SIT DOWN.
I'M GLAD YOU DROPPED IN.

1447
00:54:29,933 --> 00:54:31,435
YOU'VE BEEN THINKING
ABOUT MY SUGGESTION.

1448
00:54:31,468 --> 00:54:33,738
YES, IN A WAY, I HAVE.
YOU SEE--

1449
00:54:33,772 --> 00:54:35,473
AND YOU COULD USE A LITTLE
CASH, IS THAT RIGHT?

1450
00:54:35,507 --> 00:54:37,475
YES, THERE'S A FRIEND
OF MINE IN TROUBLE,

1451
00:54:37,508 --> 00:54:38,877
AND I'D LIKE
TO HELP HIM OUT.

1452
00:54:38,910 --> 00:54:40,678
- WELL, HOW MUCH DO YOU WANT?
- ABOUT $100.

1453
00:54:40,712 --> 00:54:43,013
- OR $72.80.
- WELL, THAT'S A LOT
OF MONEY, JIMMY.

1454
00:54:43,047 --> 00:54:45,183
- GET OUT, GET OUT!
- BUT I GUESS I CAN
ADVANCE IT TO YOU.

1455
00:54:45,217 --> 00:54:47,085
WHEN YOU BEGIN
TO WORK FOR ME, WHY,

1456
00:54:47,118 --> 00:54:48,252
YOU CAN PAY ME BACK.

1457
00:54:48,285 --> 00:54:49,887
THAT'D BE SWELL
IF YOU WOULD, MR. BLAKE.

1458
00:54:49,920 --> 00:54:51,857
I COULD START WORKING
FOR YOU ANY TIME YOU SAY.

1459
00:54:51,890 --> 00:54:53,892
GOOD, YOU CAN
BEGIN RIGHT NOW.

1460
00:54:53,925 --> 00:54:55,393
FIRST THING
I WANT YOU TO DO IS

1461
00:54:55,427 --> 00:54:57,828
TO GO TO THE BANK
AND RENT A SAFE DEPOSIT BOX.

1462
00:54:57,862 --> 00:54:59,830
AT TIMES, THERE MAY BE
SOME VALUABLE PAPERS

1463
00:54:59,863 --> 00:55:01,065
I WANT YOU
TO TAKE CARE OF FOR ME.

1464
00:55:01,098 --> 00:55:02,500
- ALL RIGHT, I'LL DO THAT.
- DO WHAT?-- OH!

1465
00:55:02,533 --> 00:55:03,868
NOW, DON'T BE SURPRISED
IF THIS JOB

1466
00:55:03,902 --> 00:55:05,103
GETS YOU UP AT ODD HOURS
OF THE NIGHT.

1467
00:55:05,137 --> 00:55:06,303
I'LL MAKE IT
WORTH YOUR WHILE.

1468
00:55:06,337 --> 00:55:08,338
WELL, MAYBE I OUGHT
TO QUIT THE SHOE STORE.

1469
00:55:08,372 --> 00:55:09,807
NO, THERE'S NO NEED
TO DO THAT.

1470
00:55:09,840 --> 00:55:11,943
YOU STAY AT THE STORE UNTIL
I GET YOU ON A FULL-TIME JOB.

1471
00:55:11,977 --> 00:55:13,143
IF YOU SAY SO.

1472
00:55:13,177 --> 00:55:15,880
NOW, TONIGHT, I WANT YOU
TO GO TO THIS ADDRESS.

1473
00:55:15,913 --> 00:55:17,148
AND PICK UP A PACKAGE.

1474
00:55:17,182 --> 00:55:18,683
- AND WHACK SOMEBODY.
- YOU JUST SHOW HIM THIS,

1475
00:55:18,717 --> 00:55:20,485
AND HE'LL KNOW IT'S OKAY.

1476
00:55:20,518 --> 00:55:21,820
WELL, SHOULD I BRING
THE PACKAGE BACK?

1477
00:55:21,853 --> 00:55:24,222
- NO--
- NO, NO, NO!

1478
00:55:24,255 --> 00:55:25,823
--BOX, AND I'LL LET YOU KNOW
WHEN I WANT IT.

1479
00:55:25,857 --> 00:55:27,292
- ALL RIGHT.
- JIMMY.

1480
00:55:27,325 --> 00:55:28,693
THIS'LL TAKE CARE
OF THE RENTAL OF THE BOX,

1481
00:55:28,727 --> 00:55:30,262
AND YOU CAN KEEP
THE REST OF IT.

1482
00:55:30,295 --> 00:55:31,730
- THANKS.
- BY THE WAY,

1483
00:55:31,763 --> 00:55:32,897
I'D RATHER YOU
WOULDN'T SAY ANYTHING

1484
00:55:32,930 --> 00:55:34,232
TO ANYONE ABOUT
WORKING FOR ME.

1485
00:55:34,265 --> 00:55:35,533
YOU KNOW,
IF YOUR BOSS FOUND OUT,

1486
00:55:35,567 --> 00:55:37,102
- HE MIGHT NOT LIKE IT.
- I WON'T.

1487
00:55:37,135 --> 00:55:38,603
AND WHEN YOU GET THROUGH WORK
TOMORROW, GIVE ME A RING.

1488
00:55:38,637 --> 00:55:39,803
- YES, SIR.
- OH, AND, UH,

1489
00:55:39,837 --> 00:55:41,338
LEAVE YOUR SOUL
WITH THE RECEPTIONIST.

1490
00:55:41,372 --> 00:55:44,475
♪ I KNEW I'D GO
FROM RAGS TO RICHES! ♪

1491
00:55:46,143 --> 00:55:47,445
NOPE, SORRY, HONEY,
I'M EATING

1492
00:55:47,478 --> 00:55:49,180
ALL FOUR OF MY LOBSTERS.

1493
00:55:54,185 --> 00:55:55,487
OKAY, HERE YOU GO, JIMMY.

1494
00:55:55,520 --> 00:55:58,490
AND MAKE SURE NOBODY SEES
THIS POUND OF BACON, SEE?

1495
00:55:58,523 --> 00:56:00,625
I'M TAKING YOU
DOWNTOWN, HONEY.

1496
00:56:00,658 --> 00:56:03,828
[JOEL LAUGHS] I'M KIDDING!

1497
00:56:03,862 --> 00:56:05,530
UH, BU-- WHERE SHOULD
I PUT MY HAND?

1498
00:56:05,563 --> 00:56:07,098
IT'S KIND OF AWKWARD.

1499
00:56:07,132 --> 00:56:09,700
SENATOR PAUL SIMON.

1500
00:56:09,733 --> 00:56:11,402
HEY, YOU TWO
STAYING HOME TONIGHT?

1501
00:56:11,435 --> 00:56:13,237
HAH, WELL, YOUR FATHER'S
GOING TO THE CLUB

1502
00:56:13,270 --> 00:56:14,505
TO PLAY CARDS LATER.

1503
00:56:14,538 --> 00:56:15,940
I THOUGHT YOU AND I
MIGHT DO SOMETHING,

1504
00:56:15,973 --> 00:56:17,875
BUT I SEE YOU
HAVE OTHER PLANS.

1505
00:56:17,908 --> 00:56:20,112
- OH, I'M SORRY--
- HE'S DEAD!

1506
00:56:20,145 --> 00:56:21,645
WHY DON'T YOU CALL UP
ONE OF YOUR GANG?

1507
00:56:21,678 --> 00:56:23,013
MAYBE I WILL.

1508
00:56:23,047 --> 00:56:24,315
WELL, GOODBYE NOW.

1509
00:56:24,348 --> 00:56:25,550
- BYE.
- [DAD GROANS]

1510
00:56:25,583 --> 00:56:27,318
[CROW MIMICS GROAN]

1511
00:56:27,352 --> 00:56:28,720
YOU THINK
HE'D EVER ACCUSE US?

1512
00:56:28,753 --> 00:56:31,322
--CHANGED THESE LAST FEW WEEKS.
HAVE YOU NOTICED IT, DAN?

1513
00:56:31,355 --> 00:56:34,258
- JIMMY WHO?
- YEAH, HE SEEMS TO HAVE
GROWN UP OVERNIGHT.

1514
00:56:34,292 --> 00:56:35,960
WELL, I DON'T LIKE IT.

1515
00:56:35,993 --> 00:56:38,428
WHAT DO YOU SUPPOSE HE'S DOING
OUT EVERY NIGHT IN THE WEEK?

1516
00:56:38,462 --> 00:56:40,365
FOR SEVERAL NIGHTS,
HE DIDN'T COME HOME AT ALL.

1517
00:56:40,398 --> 00:56:43,535
MAYBE HE STAYED
WITH A FRIEND.

1518
00:56:43,568 --> 00:56:46,170
IT'S A LITTLE LATE TO START
ASKING QUESTIONS NOW.

1519
00:56:46,203 --> 00:56:47,805
WELL, AFTER ALL,
YOUR HIS FATHER.

1520
00:56:47,838 --> 00:56:48,907
YOU OUGHT TO
KEEP AN EYE ON HIM.

1521
00:56:48,940 --> 00:56:50,442
WELL, YOU'RE HIS MOTHER.

1522
00:56:50,475 --> 00:56:52,777
YOU STAY HOME ONCE IN A WHILE,
YOU MIGHT KNOW WHAT HE'S UP TO.

1523
00:56:52,810 --> 00:56:54,578
THE TALKING CORPSE,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.

1524
00:56:54,612 --> 00:56:56,580
--A GIRLFRIEND, THAT'S ALL.

1525
00:56:56,613 --> 00:56:57,882
I HAD WHEN I WAS HIS AGE.

1526
00:56:57,915 --> 00:56:59,417
AND THEN I DIED INSIDE.

1527
00:56:59,450 --> 00:57:01,185
--TAKING AFTER YOU.

1528
00:57:01,218 --> 00:57:03,120
THAT'S IT,
THERE'S A SIX-PACK

1529
00:57:03,153 --> 00:57:04,922
CALLING MY NAME.

1530
00:57:10,662 --> 00:57:11,997
- HELLO, KITTY.
- QUACK, QUACK, QUACK.

1531
00:57:12,030 --> 00:57:13,798
I BROUGHT YOU
A LITTLE SOMETHING.

1532
00:57:13,832 --> 00:57:15,367
- QUACK QUACK QUACK.
- OH, JIMMY.

1533
00:57:15,400 --> 00:57:16,935
- LEFTOVER CHINESE!
- NOT ANOTHER PRESENT!

1534
00:57:16,968 --> 00:57:18,637
WHY, SURE. I LIKE BUYING
PRESENTS FOR YOU.

1535
00:57:18,670 --> 00:57:20,672
- IT'S FUN.
- BUT I ALWAYS HAVE
TO PAY FOR THEM.

1536
00:57:20,705 --> 00:57:22,840
JIMMY, I DON'T WANT YOU
TO BE OFFENDED,

1537
00:57:22,873 --> 00:57:24,108
BUT I'VE GOT
TO ASK YOU SOMETHING.

1538
00:57:24,142 --> 00:57:25,743
DO I HAVE A WEIRD PROFILE?

1539
00:57:25,777 --> 00:57:27,878
--MIXED UP IN ANYTHING THAT
ISN'T QUITE ON THE LEVEL,
ARE YOU?

1540
00:57:27,912 --> 00:57:29,113
WHATEVER GAVE YOU THAT IDEA?

1541
00:57:29,147 --> 00:57:30,815
I'M JUST SELLING DRUGS
TO SCHOOL KIDS.

1542
00:57:30,848 --> 00:57:33,150
--EXCEPT THAT YOU HAVE SO MUCH
MORE MONEY TO SPEND LATELY.

1543
00:57:33,183 --> 00:57:34,585
- OH, THE MOB TIES.
- LOOK,

1544
00:57:34,618 --> 00:57:35,820
DON'T YOU WORRY ABOUT ME.

1545
00:57:35,853 --> 00:57:37,188
I WOULDN'T DO
ANYTHING THAT WASN'T

1546
00:57:37,222 --> 00:57:38,723
ON THE RIGHT SIDE
OF THE LAW.

1547
00:57:38,757 --> 00:57:40,258
I HOPE NOT, JIMMY.

1548
00:57:40,292 --> 00:57:42,327
YOU'RE SO SWEET, I WOULDN'T
WANT YOU TO CHANGE.

1549
00:57:42,360 --> 00:57:44,462
- WHY SHOULD I CHANGE?
- I'LL ALWAYS WEAR
JED CLAMPETT'S HAT.

1550
00:57:44,495 --> 00:57:45,897
PEOPLE DO IN THIS TOWN.

1551
00:57:45,930 --> 00:57:48,700
- CIRCLE PINES'LL DO THAT.
- --YOU DON'T, KITTY.

1552
00:57:48,733 --> 00:57:52,403
NOW LET ME HAVE
THAT TONGUE OF YOURS.

1553
00:57:52,437 --> 00:57:53,672
SAY, EDDIE MENDEZ GAVE ME

1554
00:57:53,705 --> 00:57:54,905
TWO TICKETS FOR
THE FOLLIES SUNDAY.

1555
00:57:54,938 --> 00:57:57,342
HEY, WHAT DO I BID FOR TWO
TICKETS TO FOLLIES? HEY!

1556
00:57:57,375 --> 00:57:58,710
--CANCEL THAT LIKE YOU DID
OUR LUNCHEON DATE TODAY?

1557
00:57:58,743 --> 00:58:01,045
OH, NOW, LOOK, KITTEN.
CAN I HELP IT IF I'M BUSY?

1558
00:58:01,078 --> 00:58:02,413
I'M HANGED
IF I CAN FIND TIME

1559
00:58:02,447 --> 00:58:03,915
TO DO THE THINGS
WE'VE PLANNED.

1560
00:58:03,948 --> 00:58:05,417
BUT BUSINESS
IS SURE PICKING UP.

1561
00:58:05,450 --> 00:58:07,785
- WELL, THAT'S GOOD.
- YOU BET, FOR BOTH OF US.

1562
00:58:07,818 --> 00:58:08,987
THE HIGHER
CHARLIE BLAKE GOES...

1563
00:58:09,020 --> 00:58:10,755
- THE HIGHER KITTY REED.
- YOU SAID IT.

1564
00:58:10,788 --> 00:58:12,723
WELL, BYE, DARLING.

1565
00:58:12,757 --> 00:58:14,825
OH, UH, I MEANT
TO ASK YOU BEFORE.

1566
00:58:14,858 --> 00:58:16,527
HAVE YOU PUT
JIMMY WILSON TO WORK?

1567
00:58:16,560 --> 00:58:19,063
WHY, UH, I HAVEN'T LAID EYES
ON HIM-- HAVE YOU SEEN HIM?

1568
00:58:19,097 --> 00:58:21,365
[ALL] ♪ LIAR! LIAR! ♪

1569
00:58:21,398 --> 00:58:22,900
--YOU ASKED ME TO GIVE YOU
A BUILDUP, REMEMBER?

1570
00:58:22,933 --> 00:58:24,102
MUST'VE BEEN A SWELL BUILDUP

1571
00:58:24,135 --> 00:58:25,437
YOU GAVE HIM TO
KEEP HIM AWAY LIKE THIS.

1572
00:58:25,470 --> 00:58:27,738
MAN, EVERYBODY LIES
IN THIS MOVIE.

1573
00:58:27,772 --> 00:58:29,540
--BY NOW, HE'D BE POUNDING
ON YOUR DOOR FOR A JOB.

1574
00:58:29,573 --> 00:58:30,775
WELL, I HAVEN'T SEEN HIM.

1575
00:58:30,808 --> 00:58:32,143
I GUESS HE'S POUNDING
ON THE WRONG DOOR.

1576
00:58:32,177 --> 00:58:33,612
- YOU SAID IT.
- HEY, YOU TALK ABOUT

1577
00:58:33,645 --> 00:58:35,513
ME GIVING YOU A STAND-UP--

1578
00:58:35,547 --> 00:58:37,782
WHERE HAVE YOU BEEN DISAPPEARING
TO AFTER THE SHOW EVERY NIGHT?

1579
00:58:37,815 --> 00:58:40,217
YOU SURE GET OUT OF THAT
DRESSING ROOM IN A HURRY.

1580
00:58:40,250 --> 00:58:41,485
AND I'VE BEEN MISSING YOU.

1581
00:58:41,518 --> 00:58:43,253
WELL, CHARLIE,
YOU KNOW THE OLD SAYING.

1582
00:58:43,287 --> 00:58:45,657
EARLY TO BED
AND EARLY TO RISE.

1583
00:58:45,690 --> 00:58:47,958
- HUH?
- THAT'S ME. BYE, NOW.
- GOODBYE.

1584
00:58:47,992 --> 00:58:49,627
I ALSO KNOW ABOUT
A BIRD IN THE HAND.

1585
00:58:49,660 --> 00:58:52,297
NOW, GET OUT OF HERE.
"EARLY TO BED AND EARLY..."

1586
00:58:52,330 --> 00:58:53,932
YOU'RE NEW WITH MR. BLAKE.

1587
00:58:53,965 --> 00:58:55,467
HOW LONG HAVE YOU
BEEN WITH HIM?

1588
00:58:55,500 --> 00:58:57,435
A FEW WEEKS-- I'M NOT WORKING
FULL-TIME FOR HIM YET.

1589
00:58:57,468 --> 00:58:59,003
MMM, I SEE.

1590
00:58:59,037 --> 00:59:00,605
I'LL BE WITH YOU
IN A MINUTE.

1591
00:59:00,638 --> 00:59:03,107
UH, NOTE TO SELF.
FIND OUT CORRECT TIME.

1592
00:59:05,643 --> 00:59:07,645
UH, IT'S MY BIRTHDAY
TOMORROW, MISTER.

1593
00:59:10,280 --> 00:59:12,417
WHAT IS THIS GUY,
BUTCHER TO THE MOB?

1594
00:59:14,218 --> 00:59:15,853
HERE YOU GO.
HAPPY BIRTHDAY, JIMMY.

1595
00:59:15,887 --> 00:59:17,455
THIS IS VERY IMPORTANT.

1596
00:59:17,488 --> 00:59:20,358
YOU SEE THAT MR. BLAKE
GETS THIS NOTE TONIGHT.

1597
00:59:20,392 --> 00:59:22,760
AND BE SURE THAT YOU
GIVE IT TO NO ONE BUT HIM.

1598
00:59:22,793 --> 00:59:23,995
ALL RIGHT, I'LL DO THAT.

1599
00:59:24,028 --> 00:59:27,498
AND THIS IS SKAG.
BE CAREFUL WITH IT.

1600
00:59:27,532 --> 00:59:29,300
I'LL LET YOU OUT
THE BACK DOOR.

1601
00:59:29,333 --> 00:59:32,170
DON'T TELL THE NAZIS
WHERE I AM.

1602
00:59:38,843 --> 00:59:40,010
HI, I HAVE
AN IMPORTANT THING

1603
00:59:40,043 --> 00:59:42,647
AND SOME STUFF CALLED SKAG?

1604
00:59:42,680 --> 00:59:43,915
WHAT'S THE IDEA
COMING BACK HERE?

1605
00:59:43,948 --> 00:59:45,248
I TOLD YOU WHAT TO DO
WITH THAT PACKAGE.

1606
00:59:45,282 --> 00:59:47,152
I KNOW YOU DID, MR. BLAKE,
BUT MR. CARLTON SAID

1607
00:59:47,185 --> 00:59:48,618
TO GIVE YOU THIS NOTE.
HE SAID IT WAS IMPORTANT.

1608
00:59:48,652 --> 00:59:51,088
IS THIS A CAPER?

1609
00:59:51,122 --> 00:59:54,825
NEVER SHOULD'VE GONE
TO OLD COUNTRY BUFFET WITH HIM.

1610
00:59:54,858 --> 00:59:56,227
LET'S SEE,
WHAT DOES IT SAY HERE?

1611
00:59:56,260 --> 00:59:59,197
"ISN'T THIS GUY CARRYING
THE LETTER A DINK?"

1612
01:00:00,865 --> 01:00:02,700
IT'S ALL RIGHT, JIMMY,
YOU DID THE RIGHT THING.

1613
01:00:02,733 --> 01:00:03,868
BETTER WAIT OUT
IN THE OTHER OFFICE.

1614
01:00:03,902 --> 01:00:05,268
I MAY HAVE SOMETHING ELSE
FOR YOU TO DO.

1615
01:00:05,302 --> 01:00:06,537
OKAY, MR. BLAKE.

1616
01:00:06,570 --> 01:00:08,640
AND, UH, DO SOME FILING
WHILE YOU'RE OUT THERE.

1617
01:00:11,975 --> 01:00:14,345
HUH, YEAH,
I GOT A REAL KNACK

1618
01:00:14,378 --> 01:00:16,913
FOR SHADOWY ERRANDS.
THAT'S ME.

1619
01:00:20,017 --> 01:00:21,218
ALL RIGHT, BOYS, COME ON IN.

1620
01:00:21,252 --> 01:00:22,753
WE'RE GONNA
PANTS THE COURIER.

1621
01:00:22,787 --> 01:00:24,522
WILLIAM FRAWLEY!
MONTGOMERY CLIFT!

1622
01:00:24,555 --> 01:00:26,290
GET THIS. "CHUCK,

1623
01:00:26,323 --> 01:00:27,558
"I TRIED TO GET THE PAINTING

1624
01:00:27,592 --> 01:00:29,193
"OUT OF GORDON'S
DEAD STORAGE.

1625
01:00:29,227 --> 01:00:31,362
"COULDN'T MAKE IT AS
THE PLACE IS BEING WATCHED.

1626
01:00:31,395 --> 01:00:33,197
"DON'T SEND
ANY MORE PACKAGES.

1627
01:00:33,230 --> 01:00:35,600
"I'M LEAVING TOWN.
TAKE MY TIP AND DO THE SAME.

1628
01:00:35,633 --> 01:00:37,202
- CARL."
- WELL, HOW DO YOU
LIKE THAT?

1629
01:00:37,235 --> 01:00:39,270
- HE CALLED YOU CHUCK.
- I THOUGHT THAT STUFF
WAS SAFE THERE.

1630
01:00:39,303 --> 01:00:41,038
$30,000 WORTH OF DIAMONDS.

1631
01:00:41,072 --> 01:00:42,307
WHAT'RE YOU GONNA
DO NOW, CHARLIE?

1632
01:00:42,340 --> 01:00:43,640
WE'RE GONNA TALK
LIKE DIS, SEE?

1633
01:00:43,673 --> 01:00:44,875
-- TO THE WAREHOUSE
AND GET IT OUT.

1634
01:00:44,908 --> 01:00:46,310
TONIGHT, AND TAKE
THE KID WITH YOU.

1635
01:00:46,343 --> 01:00:47,812
TAKE THE KID? WHAT FOR?

1636
01:00:47,845 --> 01:00:49,280
MAY TAKE TWO OF YOU
TO DO THE JOB.

1637
01:00:49,313 --> 01:00:50,882
I'LL HAVE HIM RUN A CAR,
AND HE CAN DRIVE FOR YOU.

1638
01:00:50,915 --> 01:00:54,285
I'M DUE ON
THE SUPERMAN SET NOW.

1639
01:00:54,318 --> 01:00:55,653
- OH, JIMMY.
- OH HI!

1640
01:00:55,687 --> 01:00:57,355
I WANT YOU TO GO DOWN
TO OLSON'S BEFORE IT CLOSES

1641
01:00:57,388 --> 01:00:58,723
AND RENT A CAR.

1642
01:00:58,757 --> 01:01:00,057
COME BACK HERE
AT 12:00 TONIGHT

1643
01:01:00,090 --> 01:01:01,325
AND PICK UP THE BOYS,
AND TAKE THEM DOWN

1644
01:01:01,358 --> 01:01:03,493
TO GORDON'S WAREHOUSE
TO PICK UP A PACKAGE.

1645
01:01:03,527 --> 01:01:05,228
THEN DRIVE THEM BACK HERE.

1646
01:01:05,262 --> 01:01:06,663
OKAY, MR. BLAKE.

1647
01:01:06,697 --> 01:01:09,400
HE'S GOT FRAMED
RUBBER VOMIT ON THE WALL.

1648
01:01:11,035 --> 01:01:12,903
YOU KNOW WHAT,
I SHOULD CALL MR. BLAKE

1649
01:01:12,937 --> 01:01:14,872
AND TELL HIM
HOW MUCH I LIKE HIM.

1650
01:01:17,942 --> 01:01:19,477
HELLO, KITTY?
THIS IS JIMMY,

1651
01:01:19,510 --> 01:01:21,045
REMEMBER ME?
I'M YOUR BOYFRIEND.

1652
01:01:21,078 --> 01:01:22,380
YOU'D BETTER BE.

1653
01:01:22,413 --> 01:01:23,815
CAN I SEE YOU TONIGHT?
WE'LL GO DANCING.

1654
01:01:23,848 --> 01:01:25,617
OH, THIS IS LATE-NIGHT HOT.

1655
01:01:25,650 --> 01:01:26,883
OH, SWELL.

1656
01:01:26,917 --> 01:01:28,485
I'VE GOT A LITTLE BUSINESS
TO TAKE CARE OF,

1657
01:01:28,518 --> 01:01:30,253
AND I'LL BE ABOUT
HALF AN HOUR LATE.

1658
01:01:30,287 --> 01:01:31,988
I'VE GOT SOMETHING
AWFULLY IMPORTANT TO ASK YOU.

1659
01:01:32,022 --> 01:01:34,425
NOW, DON'T TELL ME
YOU'RE GOING TO PROPOSE TO ME.

1660
01:01:34,458 --> 01:01:36,460
- MAYBE.
- ALL RIGHT, HON,
I'LL BE LOOKING FOR YOU.

1661
01:01:36,493 --> 01:01:38,963
JIMMY'S CHEATING ON ME!

1662
01:01:38,997 --> 01:01:42,167
THAT GUY'S EAVES-DROPPING
ON HIS EAVES-DROPPING.

1663
01:01:42,200 --> 01:01:43,533
WAIT HERE, I'LL BE BACK
IN AN HOUR.

1664
01:01:43,567 --> 01:01:45,368
WITH SQUEAKY SHOES ON.

1665
01:01:49,740 --> 01:01:51,908
[JOEL]
♪ LOVE CAME BETWEEN US ♪

1666
01:01:54,245 --> 01:01:55,580
QUACK, QUACK.
QUACK-QUACK QUACK.

1667
01:01:55,613 --> 01:01:58,015
OH, HELLO. I DIDN'T EXPECT
TO SEE YOU, CHARLIE.

1668
01:01:58,048 --> 01:02:00,050
I KNOW YOU DIDN'T.
YOU EXPECTED THE KID.

1669
01:02:00,083 --> 01:02:02,687
NOBODY EXPECTS
TO SEE CHARLIE!

1670
01:02:02,720 --> 01:02:05,055
♪ LOVE CAME BETWEEN US ♪

1671
01:02:05,088 --> 01:02:06,623
OH, UH, BUTTERMINTS, HUH?

1672
01:02:06,657 --> 01:02:09,427
DON'T MIND IF I DO. MMM.

1673
01:02:09,460 --> 01:02:12,363
FIRST OF ALL, YOU AND I ARE
GONNA STRAIGHTEN OUT SOMETHING.

1674
01:02:12,397 --> 01:02:14,132
WHAT'S GOING ON
BETWEEN YOU TWO?

1675
01:02:14,165 --> 01:02:15,933
UH, CHEAP LOVE. WHY?

1676
01:02:15,967 --> 01:02:17,835
I DON'T KNOW WHAT YOU'RE
TALKING ABOUT, CHARLIE.

1677
01:02:17,868 --> 01:02:19,970
WHY IS SHE DRESSED LIKE
MAJOR BARBARA?

1678
01:02:20,003 --> 01:02:21,538
NO?

1679
01:02:21,572 --> 01:02:23,507
- WELL, I'LL MAKE IT CLEAR.
- [JOEL MUMBLES]

1680
01:02:23,540 --> 01:02:26,677
I HEARD THAT PHONE CONVERSATION
YOU HAD A LITTLE WHILE AGO.

1681
01:02:26,710 --> 01:02:28,245
HE WAS TALKING
FROM MY OFFICE.

1682
01:02:28,278 --> 01:02:30,047
IT WAS FUNNY.
MADE ME LAUGH-- HAH!

1683
01:02:30,080 --> 01:02:32,283
SO YOU REALLY
FELL IN LOVE WITH THE KID.

1684
01:02:32,317 --> 01:02:34,152
NOW, LOOK.

1685
01:02:34,185 --> 01:02:36,453
NOBODY'S GONNA
TAKE YOU AWAY FROM ME.

1686
01:02:36,487 --> 01:02:38,455
- NOBODY.
- NOT EVEN ME, SEE?

1687
01:02:38,488 --> 01:02:39,857
I'LL KILL ME
BEFORE THAT HAPPENS.

1688
01:02:39,890 --> 01:02:42,227
WHY... WHY, CHARLIE.

1689
01:02:42,260 --> 01:02:45,128
YOU DON'T REALLY THINK
I FELL FOR THAT KID, DO YOU?

1690
01:02:45,162 --> 01:02:47,063
WHY, YOU ASKED ME
TO STRING HIM ALONG.

1691
01:02:47,097 --> 01:02:48,632
CAN I HELP IT
IF HE FELL FOR ME?

1692
01:02:48,665 --> 01:02:51,968
WELL, HE DID WIN
THAT ESSAY CONTEST.

1693
01:02:52,002 --> 01:02:53,437
HE'S AS GOOD AS FORGOTTEN.

1694
01:02:53,470 --> 01:02:56,273
[ALL] ♪ LIAR! LIAR! ♪

1695
01:02:56,307 --> 01:02:58,808
WHEN HE GETS HERE,
I WANT YOU TO GET RID OF HIM.

1696
01:02:58,842 --> 01:03:01,012
- YOUR WAY.
- OR THE HIGHWAY.

1697
01:03:01,045 --> 01:03:03,380
OR WOULD YOU RATHER
HAVE ME DO IT?

1698
01:03:03,413 --> 01:03:04,682
OKAY, CHARLIE.

1699
01:03:04,715 --> 01:03:06,150
I'LL BE HAPPY IN MY WORK.

1700
01:03:06,183 --> 01:03:07,885
IT OUGHT TO BE A CINCH.

1701
01:03:07,918 --> 01:03:11,088
- [DOOR BUZZES]
- OH, IT'S THE THREE
HARD-BOILED EGGS SHE ORDERED.

1702
01:03:11,122 --> 01:03:12,357
I'LL BE IN THERE LISTENING.

1703
01:03:12,390 --> 01:03:15,325
LIKE I USUALLY AM.

1704
01:03:15,358 --> 01:03:16,960
WATCH OUT! AAH!

1705
01:03:16,993 --> 01:03:19,363
- [ALL MIMIC CRASH]
- [DOORBELL BUZZES]

1706
01:03:21,265 --> 01:03:24,102
[SERVO MUFFLED]
HEY, I THOUGHT YOU WERE GONNA
HAVE THIS STUFF DRY-CLEANED.

1707
01:03:24,135 --> 01:03:26,237
WELL, AREN'T I MISS POPULAR?

1708
01:03:28,605 --> 01:03:30,373
WELL, I'VE JOINED
THE BLACK HAND. HI!

1709
01:03:30,407 --> 01:03:31,908
--LET'S GET GOING.
WE'VE ONLY GOT A FEW HOURS.

1710
01:03:31,942 --> 01:03:34,478
I HAVE SOME WORK TO DO
LATER ON.

1711
01:03:34,512 --> 01:03:36,213
I'M NOT GOING.

1712
01:03:36,247 --> 01:03:39,350
WELL, WHAT THE--
WAIT A MINUTE!

1713
01:03:39,383 --> 01:03:41,252
HEY, ARE YOU KIDDING?
WHY, OVER THE PHONE,

1714
01:03:41,285 --> 01:03:42,820
YOU JUST GOT THROUGH
SAYING WE'D GO SOMEPLACE.

1715
01:03:42,853 --> 01:03:45,355
[JOEL AS SCHWARZENEGGER]
I LIED.

1716
01:03:45,388 --> 01:03:46,757
I KNOW,
BUT AFTER I TALKED TO YOU,

1717
01:03:46,790 --> 01:03:48,592
- I CHANGED MY MIND.
- GUY IN THE CLOSET.

1718
01:03:48,625 --> 01:03:49,993
AN OLD FRIEND OF MINE CALLED,

1719
01:03:50,027 --> 01:03:51,828
- AND I'M GOING OUT WITH HIM.
- GUY IN THE CLOSET.

1720
01:03:51,862 --> 01:03:53,130
HEY, YOU SAY THAT SO
CONVINCINGLY,

1721
01:03:53,163 --> 01:03:54,698
I ALMOST BELIEVE IT.

1722
01:03:54,732 --> 01:03:56,067
[CROW MUFFLED]
HEY, WHERE'D YOU GET
THESE GOLF CLUBS?

1723
01:03:56,100 --> 01:03:57,268
- SHH!
- YOU CAN BELIEVE IT.

1724
01:03:57,302 --> 01:03:58,635
GUY IN THE CLOSET.

1725
01:03:58,668 --> 01:03:59,970
- DO YOU MEAN IT?
- CLOSET.

1726
01:04:00,003 --> 01:04:01,972
OF COURSE I MEAN IT.

1727
01:04:02,005 --> 01:04:03,440
HEY, I SMELL ITALIAN.

1728
01:04:03,473 --> 01:04:05,108
- LOOK, WH--
- OH, YOU POOR CHUMP.

1729
01:04:05,142 --> 01:04:06,477
[CROW AS BERT LAHR]
COURAGE!

1730
01:04:06,510 --> 01:04:09,280
DID YOU REALLY
TAKE ME SERIOUSLY?

1731
01:04:09,313 --> 01:04:11,215
DID YOU THINK FOR ONE MINUTE
THAT I LOVED YOU?

1732
01:04:11,248 --> 01:04:12,883
THAT I WANTED TO MARRY YOU?

1733
01:04:12,917 --> 01:04:14,185
SHE'S SMOKIN'.

1734
01:04:14,218 --> 01:04:15,687
WHY COULD YOU IMAGINE
KITTY REED

1735
01:04:15,720 --> 01:04:17,422
COOPED UP IN A LITTLE
TWO-BY-FOUR COTTAGE

1736
01:04:17,455 --> 01:04:19,257
WITH A STRING OF KIDS
CLIMBING ALL OVER HER?

1737
01:04:19,290 --> 01:04:20,658
OH, NO, NOT KITTY.

1738
01:04:20,692 --> 01:04:21,858
I AM THE ANGEL OF DEATH.

1739
01:04:21,892 --> 01:04:22,993
THE DAY OF RECKONING
IS UPON US.

1740
01:04:23,027 --> 01:04:24,295
--JIMMY, I THOUGHT
THAT FOR A WHILE

1741
01:04:24,328 --> 01:04:26,397
YOU MIGHT GO SOMEPLACE.

1742
01:04:26,430 --> 01:04:28,165
BUT YOU'LL ALWAYS
BE A SHOE SALESMAN

1743
01:04:28,198 --> 01:04:30,500
- AT 25 A WEEK.
- 18 AFTER TAXES!

1744
01:04:30,533 --> 01:04:34,105
AND, UH, MY AMBITION'S
A LITTLE HIGHER THAN THAT.

1745
01:04:34,138 --> 01:04:35,472
WELL, WAIT A MINUTE,
THEY'RE GONNA PUT ME

1746
01:04:35,505 --> 01:04:36,907
IN CHARGE OF THE SOCK TABLE!

1747
01:04:36,940 --> 01:04:39,777
--AND PEDDLE YOUR PAPERS.
YOU ANNOY ME.

1748
01:04:39,810 --> 01:04:41,545
UH, OKAY.

1749
01:04:41,578 --> 01:04:42,947
GOOD NIGHT, MR. BLAKE.

1750
01:04:42,980 --> 01:04:44,382
[JOEL MUFFLED]
GOOD NIGHT, JIMMY-- D'OH!

1751
01:04:44,415 --> 01:04:47,785
QUACK QUACK QUACK QUACK.

1752
01:04:47,818 --> 01:04:50,553
OUGHT TO GET THAT
TENNIS RACKET RE-STRUNG.

1753
01:04:50,587 --> 01:04:53,090
HONEY, I'M HOME.
HAH. LOVE THAT.

1754
01:04:53,123 --> 01:04:55,158
ARE YOU SATISFIED, CHARLIE?

1755
01:04:55,192 --> 01:04:56,727
WELL, YOU SAVED ME
A LOT OF TROUBLE, KITTEN.

1756
01:04:56,760 --> 01:04:59,130
MEOW.

1757
01:04:59,163 --> 01:05:00,497
I'LL SEE YOU IN THE MORNING.

1758
01:05:00,530 --> 01:05:03,733
YEAH, THANKS FOR COMING BY.

1759
01:05:03,767 --> 01:05:05,368
IF I HAD PARENTS,

1760
01:05:05,402 --> 01:05:06,737
I'D ACCUSE THEM RIGHT NOW.

1761
01:05:06,770 --> 01:05:08,605
I ACCUSE HER HAIR.

1762
01:05:10,808 --> 01:05:12,643
MEANWHILE,
OUTSIDE OF SKOKIE,

1763
01:05:12,677 --> 01:05:16,380
ELIOT NESS AND HIS MEN
CONTINUE THEIR VIGIL.

1764
01:05:16,413 --> 01:05:19,317
WELL, AT LEAST I GOT
A CAPER TO FALL BACK ON.

1765
01:05:19,350 --> 01:05:20,550
[GUNSHOTS]

1766
01:05:20,583 --> 01:05:21,885
HUH? WHAT NOW?

1767
01:05:21,918 --> 01:05:24,955
HOW CAN I GET A BLOWOUT
WHEN I'M JUST SITTING HERE?

1768
01:05:24,988 --> 01:05:26,157
GET GOING, KID, QUICK.

1769
01:05:26,190 --> 01:05:27,758
- WHAT HAPPENED?
- GET GOING.

1770
01:05:27,792 --> 01:05:29,127
THEY STOLE THE BOGART!

1771
01:05:29,160 --> 01:05:30,895
ZE BOGART!

1772
01:05:30,928 --> 01:05:32,397
WAIT, SHOULDN'T WE FIND OUT
WHAT THOSE SHOTS WERE?

1773
01:05:32,430 --> 01:05:33,897
IF ANYONE WAS HURT?

1774
01:05:33,930 --> 01:05:35,465
I KNEW THAT NERVOUS TRIGGER
FINGER OF YOURS

1775
01:05:35,498 --> 01:05:36,933
WOULD GET US INTO TROUBLE
SOONER OR LATER.

1776
01:05:36,967 --> 01:05:38,468
- ALL-AMERICAN.
- IT WAS EITHER HIM OR US.

1777
01:05:38,502 --> 01:05:40,203
- WHAT ABOUT THE KID?
- HE OUGHT TO BE HERE
ANY MINUTE.

1778
01:05:40,237 --> 01:05:41,505
AND HE'S READY TO SCREAM.

1779
01:05:41,538 --> 01:05:43,373
AND YOU'D BETTER DO
SOME FANCY TALKING, BLAKE.

1780
01:05:43,407 --> 01:05:44,542
WE'RE GONNA HAVE
TROUBLE WITH HIM.

1781
01:05:44,575 --> 01:05:47,177
JUST LET ME HANDLE HIM.

1782
01:05:47,210 --> 01:05:49,480
WHY DIDN'T YOU TELL ME I WAS
DRIVING A CAR TO A HOLD-UP?

1783
01:05:49,513 --> 01:05:51,282
- OH BOY.
- I DIDN'T SEE ANY REASON
TO TELL YOU, JIMMY.

1784
01:05:51,315 --> 01:05:52,550
I NEVER TOLD YOU ABOUT ANY

1785
01:05:52,583 --> 01:05:54,252
OF THE OTHER JOBS
YOU DID FOR ME.

1786
01:05:54,285 --> 01:05:56,553
WHAT OTHER JOBS?
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

1787
01:05:56,587 --> 01:05:58,088
RING JOBS.

1788
01:05:58,122 --> 01:05:59,490
YOU DON'T THINK I'VE BEEN PAYING
YOU THE KIND OF MONEY I HAVE

1789
01:05:59,523 --> 01:06:01,025
JUST TO PICK UP PACKAGES.

1790
01:06:01,058 --> 01:06:02,927
IF IT'D BEEN ON THE LEVEL,
I COULD'VE GOTTEN A MESSENGER

1791
01:06:02,960 --> 01:06:04,495
FOR A LOT LESS
THAN YOU'VE BEEN GETTING.

1792
01:06:04,528 --> 01:06:06,530
I DIDN'T KNOW THERE WAS
ANYTHING CROOKED ABOUT THE JOB.

1793
01:06:06,563 --> 01:06:08,432
I DON'T WANT ANY PART OF IT.
I'M QUITTING RIGHT NOW.

1794
01:06:08,465 --> 01:06:10,300
- NO, YOU'RE NOT!
- GIVE ME THAT TIE BACK.

1795
01:06:10,333 --> 01:06:12,068
NOBODY EVER QUITS
ON CHARLIE BLAKE.

1796
01:06:12,102 --> 01:06:13,270
OH, HE'S REALLY IN TROUBLE.

1797
01:06:13,303 --> 01:06:15,205
IF HE DOESN'T WANT 'EM TO.

1798
01:06:15,238 --> 01:06:17,340
WHATEVER I'VE DONE, I'M NOT
GONNA STAND FOR MURDER.

1799
01:06:17,373 --> 01:06:19,210
I'LL TELL THE POLICE.
I'LL TELL THEM ABOUT YOU.

1800
01:06:19,243 --> 01:06:20,712
I'LL TELL THEM WHAT
YOU DID TO ME, I'LL TELL--

1801
01:06:20,745 --> 01:06:22,413
AAH! IT'S MY
BIRTHDAY TOMORROW.

1802
01:06:22,447 --> 01:06:24,248
TELL THEM ANYTHING.

1803
01:06:24,282 --> 01:06:25,983
YOU'RE IN THIS WHETHER
YOU LIKE IT OR NOT.

1804
01:06:26,017 --> 01:06:28,785
JUST AS MUCH AS IF
YOU HANDLED THE GUN.

1805
01:06:28,818 --> 01:06:31,588
YOU TELL THE POLICE,
AND YOU'LL GET 20 YEARS.

1806
01:06:31,622 --> 01:06:33,557
FREE? WITH NO OBLIGATION?

1807
01:06:33,590 --> 01:06:35,727
WHAT IF I TELL
A NOTARY PUBLIC?

1808
01:06:35,760 --> 01:06:37,127
HUH, THAT'S BETTER.

1809
01:06:37,160 --> 01:06:39,028
NO SENSE IN GETTING PANICKY.

1810
01:06:39,062 --> 01:06:40,932
YOU KNOW WHAT YOU DO?

1811
01:06:40,965 --> 01:06:42,533
YOU GO ON HOME AND GET
A GOOD NIGHT'S REST.

1812
01:06:42,567 --> 01:06:44,000
FORGET ABOUT--
TOMORROW MORNING,

1813
01:06:44,033 --> 01:06:46,037
GO BACK TO THE STORE
AS IF NOTHING HAD HAPPENED.

1814
01:06:46,070 --> 01:06:49,005
AND DON'T WORRY ABOUT
GETTING INTO A JAM.

1815
01:06:49,038 --> 01:06:51,042
I HAVE ENOUGH INFLUENCE
TO PULL YOU OUT.

1816
01:06:53,277 --> 01:06:56,880
OKAY, I GUESS
IT'S ALL RIGHT. GOSH.

1817
01:06:56,913 --> 01:06:59,417
YOU, UH, WANT SOME YOGURT?

1818
01:07:00,717 --> 01:07:03,120
OH, IT'S ALL
BECAUSE OF THESE SHOES.

1819
01:07:05,755 --> 01:07:08,125
FAMILY CIRCUS IS REALLY
UPSETTING TO HIM TODAY.

1820
01:07:11,495 --> 01:07:14,030
I'VE GOTTA CONTROL MY URGES.

1821
01:07:20,170 --> 01:07:23,940
JACK BENNY PROGRAM.

1822
01:07:23,973 --> 01:07:26,577
IT'S THE FEATHER McGEE
AND MOLLY SHOW!

1823
01:07:28,812 --> 01:07:31,748
[SOBS] STOP
MOCKING ME, RADIO!

1824
01:07:31,782 --> 01:07:34,050
[SOBS]

1825
01:07:34,083 --> 01:07:35,987
NO, DON'T OPEN
THAT DOOR, MCGEE!

1826
01:07:38,555 --> 01:07:40,523
I HATE THAT HAL ROACH MUSIC.

1827
01:07:46,097 --> 01:07:48,465
YOU FIGURE THAT VASE
IS FILLED WITH SCOTCH?

1828
01:07:52,202 --> 01:07:53,403
- WHAT, JIMMY?
- HELLO?

1829
01:07:53,437 --> 01:07:55,338
HELLO, THIS IS JIMMY WILSON.
IS KITTY THERE?

1830
01:07:55,372 --> 01:07:56,973
- I GOTTA TALK TO HER.
- JUST A MINUTE,

1831
01:07:57,007 --> 01:07:58,375
AND I'LL SEE IF SHE'S HERE.

1832
01:07:58,408 --> 01:08:01,278
IT'S JIMMY WILSON.
HE WANTS TO TALK TO YOU.

1833
01:08:01,312 --> 01:08:03,380
THE YOUNG VIVIAN VANCE
LOOKS HOPEFUL.

1834
01:08:03,413 --> 01:08:05,315
SHE LEANS BACK.

1835
01:08:05,348 --> 01:08:07,818
TELL HIM I'M NOT HERE.

1836
01:08:07,852 --> 01:08:09,487
- SHE SAYS SHE'S NOT HERE.
- I'M SORRY, JIMMY,

1837
01:08:09,520 --> 01:08:11,522
- BUT SHE'S NOT HERE.
- THANKS.

1838
01:08:11,555 --> 01:08:14,358
I WONDER WHO THAT WAS
IN THE BACK-- WAIT A MINUTE!

1839
01:08:14,392 --> 01:08:16,027
HEY.

1840
01:08:16,060 --> 01:08:17,327
MMM.

1841
01:08:17,360 --> 01:08:19,330
THE GLOW OF
THE ESSAY CONTEST

1842
01:08:19,363 --> 01:08:20,865
IS STARTING TO WEAR OFF.

1843
01:08:20,898 --> 01:08:23,733
MMM.

1844
01:08:34,778 --> 01:08:37,280
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,
TODAY WE ARE WATCHING

1845
01:08:37,313 --> 01:08:39,583
A FILM CALLED
I ACCUSE MY PARENTS.

1846
01:08:39,617 --> 01:08:40,918
AND JUST TO GROUND
EVERYBODY,

1847
01:08:40,952 --> 01:08:43,287
IT'S THE ONE WHERE THE KID
ACCUSES HIS PARENTS.

1848
01:08:43,320 --> 01:08:45,055
BUT CAN PARENTS
AND PARENTS ALONE

1849
01:08:45,088 --> 01:08:47,925
EXPLAIN MENTAL ILLNESS
ON THE SCALE OF YOUNG JIMMY'S?

1850
01:08:47,958 --> 01:08:49,660
- HMM.
- HMM, GEE, THAT'D BE NICE.

1851
01:08:49,693 --> 01:08:52,495
BUT, HEY, LET'S TRY TO MAP OUT
THE TRAIL OF HIS PSYCHOSIS.

1852
01:08:52,528 --> 01:08:55,132
MM-HMM. WE'LL GIVE JIMMY
THE BENEFIT OF THE DOUBT

1853
01:08:55,165 --> 01:08:56,967
AND START WITH
THE FILM'S HYPOTENUSE

1854
01:08:57,000 --> 01:08:58,668
THAT, AT THE CENTER
OF JIMMY'S MADNESS,

1855
01:08:58,702 --> 01:09:01,205
WE WILL, IN FACT,
FIND HIS DRUNK FOLKS.

1856
01:09:01,238 --> 01:09:03,140
RIGHT, DRUNK FOLKS.

1857
01:09:03,173 --> 01:09:05,808
CONCERNING WHOM, JIMMY LIES.

1858
01:09:05,842 --> 01:09:07,545
AND THAT'S FINE,
BUT THESE ARE NOT

1859
01:09:07,578 --> 01:09:10,380
SIMPLE, UTILITARIAN LIES
THAT SATISFY YOU AND ME

1860
01:09:10,413 --> 01:09:11,782
AS WE INTERACT
ON A DAILY BASIS.

1861
01:09:11,815 --> 01:09:13,350
NO, NO-NO-NO-NO NO.

1862
01:09:13,383 --> 01:09:15,518
THESE ARE ELABORATE LIES.

1863
01:09:15,552 --> 01:09:17,722
JOEL, IF YOU WILL.
ELABORATE.

1864
01:09:17,755 --> 01:09:19,122
THROUGH WHICH
JIMMY CONSTRUCTS

1865
01:09:19,155 --> 01:09:21,992
A RICHLY CUCKOO
FANTASY WORLD OF LOVE.

1866
01:09:22,025 --> 01:09:24,228
THEN, JIMMY MEETS
A NICE YOUNG WOMAN.

1867
01:09:24,262 --> 01:09:25,628
- AHH.
- HEY. JIM.

1868
01:09:25,662 --> 01:09:27,665
HERE'S SOMEONE YOU
MIGHT WANT TO CONFIDE IN.

1869
01:09:27,698 --> 01:09:28,865
TRUTH, JIM.

1870
01:09:28,898 --> 01:09:31,468
[BOTS] TRUTH. TRUTH.
TRUTH! TRUTH! TRUTH!

1871
01:09:31,502 --> 01:09:33,303
- MM-MM.
- NO.
- NOT A CHANCE.

1872
01:09:33,337 --> 01:09:34,872
IT'S NOT GONNA HAPPEN.
INSTEAD...

1873
01:09:34,905 --> 01:09:37,908
JIMMY FEELS THE NEED TO...

1874
01:09:37,942 --> 01:09:39,510
DENIGRATE OTHERS

1875
01:09:39,543 --> 01:09:42,780
WHILE SIMULTANEOUSLY
ATTRACTING OTHERS.

1876
01:09:42,813 --> 01:09:45,015
WHICH LEADS SOMEHOW
TO A LIFE OF CRIME.

1877
01:09:45,048 --> 01:09:47,752
AND YET HE'S IGNORANT
THAT IT IS CRIME. HUH.

1878
01:09:47,785 --> 01:09:50,553
RELATED BACK TO THE ELABORATE
LIES, PERHAPS, JIM?

1879
01:09:50,587 --> 01:09:52,288
AND WHERE IN GOD'S NAME

1880
01:09:52,322 --> 01:09:54,223
IS THE CONNECTION
TO OUR STARTING POINT?

1881
01:09:54,257 --> 01:09:56,193
- [ALL] DRUNK FOLKS.
- UH-HUH.

1882
01:09:56,227 --> 01:09:57,493
- RIGHT.
- AND WE SHOULDN'T FORGET

1883
01:09:57,527 --> 01:09:58,862
THAT JIMMY MAY BE
KIND OF STUPID, JOEL.

1884
01:09:58,895 --> 01:10:00,163
- RIGHT.
- MM-HMM.

1885
01:10:00,197 --> 01:10:03,233
OH, CAMBOT, IF YOU WILL.
HERE WE GO.

1886
01:10:03,267 --> 01:10:05,835
NOW WE'VE ENTERED
JIMMY'S SUBCONSCIOUS.

1887
01:10:05,868 --> 01:10:08,038
- YUCK.
- AS IT SPINS AND TWIRLS

1888
01:10:08,072 --> 01:10:09,507
TO ILLUSTRATE
TODAY'S LESSON.

1889
01:10:09,540 --> 01:10:11,408
THAT TRUE
JIMMY-SCALE DEMENTIA

1890
01:10:11,442 --> 01:10:13,643
IS INDEED
A COMPLEX PHENOMENON.

1891
01:10:13,677 --> 01:10:15,345
CAUSE AND EFFECT? GOOD LUCK.

1892
01:10:15,378 --> 01:10:16,847
HERE'S, UH, DRUNK FOLKS.

1893
01:10:16,880 --> 01:10:19,583
BUT THAT'S JUST
A PIECE OF THE PUZZLE.

1894
01:10:19,617 --> 01:10:22,185
HEY! THERE'S STUPID.
REALLY BIG.

1895
01:10:22,218 --> 01:10:23,787
AND YET THERE'S
SO MUCH MORE.

1896
01:10:23,820 --> 01:10:25,422
OH-- NO BACKBONE.

1897
01:10:25,455 --> 01:10:28,158
OH, AND AN EXTRA UNEXPLAINED
LEVEL OF DENIAL.

1898
01:10:28,192 --> 01:10:29,793
HIS STRANGE NEED
FOR MOB TIES.

1899
01:10:29,827 --> 01:10:31,862
YEAH, JIMMY'S
COMPLICATED HAIRCUT.

1900
01:10:31,895 --> 01:10:34,230
THERE GOES HIS FAILURE
IN WEBELOS.

1901
01:10:34,263 --> 01:10:37,033
OH, AND ORIGINAL SIN.
DON'T FORGET THAT, FOLKS.

1902
01:10:37,067 --> 01:10:39,370
SO, IF YOU'RE OFF
YOUR DOT YOURSELF--

1903
01:10:39,403 --> 01:10:41,038
DON'T LOOK
FOR SIMPLE ANSWERS.

1904
01:10:41,072 --> 01:10:42,840
REALLY GET INSIDE YOURSELF

1905
01:10:42,873 --> 01:10:45,108
AND JUST RUN AROUND
AND HAVE A GOOD TIME.

1906
01:10:45,142 --> 01:10:48,012
BELIEVE YOU US, IT CAN BE
A WHALE OF A LOT OF FUN.

1907
01:10:48,045 --> 01:10:49,613
AND, YOU KNOW WHAT?
WE GOT COMMERCIAL SIGN.

1908
01:10:49,647 --> 01:10:52,148
- ♪ JIM'S CRAZY ♪
- AND STUPID.

1909
01:10:52,182 --> 01:10:53,717
♪ HE'S CRAZY FOR ♪

1910
01:10:53,750 --> 01:10:57,320
♪ ACCUSING HIS PARENTS ♪

1911
01:11:04,895 --> 01:11:06,697
- GOOD MORNING.
- [JOEL] MORNING.
- MORNING.

1912
01:11:06,730 --> 01:11:08,132
- MR. HOLDEN.
- YES?

1913
01:11:08,165 --> 01:11:09,367
- MORNING.
- IS THERE ANYTHING
I CAN DO FOR YOU?

1914
01:11:09,400 --> 01:11:10,533
YES, HAVE YOU
A BOY WORKING HERE

1915
01:11:10,567 --> 01:11:11,635
- BY THE NAME OF JIMMY WILSON?
- GOOD MORNING.

1916
01:11:11,668 --> 01:11:13,370
- YES.
- WE'D LIKE TO SEE HIM.

1917
01:11:13,403 --> 01:11:15,238
I'M SORRY,
HE HASN'T COME IN YET.

1918
01:11:15,272 --> 01:11:18,008
MOST UNUSUAL.
JIMMY'S ALWAYS ON TIME.

1919
01:11:18,042 --> 01:11:19,242
MILK DUDS?

1920
01:11:19,275 --> 01:11:20,577
WE GOT ORDERS
TO CHECK UP ON HIM.

1921
01:11:20,610 --> 01:11:21,745
CHECK UP ON JIMMY?

1922
01:11:21,778 --> 01:11:23,013
- YEAH.
- WHAT'S HE BEEN DOING?

1923
01:11:23,047 --> 01:11:24,682
THAT'S WHAT WE'RE
GOING TO FIND OUT.

1924
01:11:24,715 --> 01:11:26,817
HE'S BEEN SEEN WITH
SOME PRETTY SHADY CHARACTERS.

1925
01:11:26,850 --> 01:11:28,685
YEAH, LET'S HAVE
HIS ADDRESS.

1926
01:11:28,718 --> 01:11:30,887
- WHY, OF COURSE.
- LET'S SEE-- TUESDAY
GOOD FOR YOU?

1927
01:11:30,920 --> 01:11:32,622
- NO.
- HOW ABOUT SUNDAY?

1928
01:11:32,655 --> 01:11:35,892
465 LINDHURST DRIVE.

1929
01:11:35,925 --> 01:11:37,493
- THANKS, MR. HOLDEN.
- SUNDAY IT IS, THEN.

1930
01:11:37,527 --> 01:11:39,162
I'M AFRAID YOUR BOY
WON'T SHOW UP TODAY.

1931
01:11:39,195 --> 01:11:41,532
WELL, WHO'S GOING TO SELL
THESE SHOES, THEN?

1932
01:11:41,565 --> 01:11:42,800
HEY, UH, YOU FELLAS WANNA

1933
01:11:42,833 --> 01:11:44,502
REACH IN TO
THE TREASURE BARREL?

1934
01:11:44,535 --> 01:11:46,237
OH.

1935
01:11:48,072 --> 01:11:49,873
HMM?

1936
01:11:49,907 --> 01:11:51,375
[SERVO GASPS] THERE HE IS!

1937
01:11:51,408 --> 01:11:53,210
OFFICER, OFFICER!

1938
01:11:55,612 --> 01:11:57,347
WELL, HERE'S
OUR LITTLE FUGITIVE.

1939
01:11:57,380 --> 01:11:59,182
I'M SORRY I'M LATE, MR. HOLDEN,
BUT I HAD SOME BUSINESS--

1940
01:11:59,215 --> 01:12:00,917
THERE'S TWO MEN HERE
ASKING ABOUT YOU.

1941
01:12:00,950 --> 01:12:02,720
- FROM POLICE HEADQUARTERS.
- POLICE HEADQUARTERS?

1942
01:12:02,753 --> 01:12:03,953
WELL, WHAT DID THEY
WANT TO KNOW ABOUT ME?

1943
01:12:03,987 --> 01:12:05,188
THEY DIDN'T SAY.

1944
01:12:05,222 --> 01:12:06,523
HAVE THEY GOT ANYTHING
AGAINST YOU, JIMMY?

1945
01:12:06,557 --> 01:12:08,458
WELL, NO, OF COURSE NOT.
WHAT COULD THEY HAVE AGAINST ME?

1946
01:12:08,492 --> 01:12:10,327
WELL, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT YOU DO OUTSIDE THE SHOP.

1947
01:12:10,360 --> 01:12:12,830
THEY SAY YOU'VE BEEN SEEN WITH
SOME PRETTY SHADY CHARACTERS.

1948
01:12:12,863 --> 01:12:14,097
- HMM.
- MAYBE YOU'D BETTER GO HOME,

1949
01:12:14,130 --> 01:12:15,998
GET YOUR FOLKS TO TAKE YOU DOWN
TO POLICE HEADQUARTERS.

1950
01:12:16,032 --> 01:12:17,633
- [SERVO LAUGHS]
- GET THIS THING
STRAIGHTENED OUT.

1951
01:12:17,667 --> 01:12:19,470
I DON'T LIKE POLICE
COMING HERE, JIMMY.

1952
01:12:19,503 --> 01:12:21,272
- IT ISN'T GOOD FOR BUSINESS.
- WHAT BUSINESS?

1953
01:12:21,305 --> 01:12:22,405
WELL, I DON'T BLAME YOU,
MR. HOLDEN.

1954
01:12:22,438 --> 01:12:23,907
I'LL GO RIGHT HOME
AND DO THAT.

1955
01:12:23,940 --> 01:12:25,308
ALL RIGHT.

1956
01:12:25,342 --> 01:12:27,043
I'M SURE THERE MUST
BE SOME MISTAKE.

1957
01:12:27,077 --> 01:12:28,712
[CROW GROANS]

1958
01:12:28,745 --> 01:12:30,347
TWO PLAINCLOTHESMEN
FROM POLICE HEADQUARTERS

1959
01:12:30,380 --> 01:12:31,882
HAVE BEEN TO THE SHOE STORE
ASKING ABOUT ME.

1960
01:12:31,915 --> 01:12:33,417
HMM, THAT'S PRETTY QUICK WORK.
THEY MUST'VE TRACED THE CAR.

1961
01:12:33,450 --> 01:12:34,585
NOW, LOOK,
YOU GOT ME INTO THIS.

1962
01:12:34,618 --> 01:12:35,752
YOU GOTTA GET ME OUT.
YOU SAID YOU WOULD.

1963
01:12:35,785 --> 01:12:37,187
TAKE IT EASY.
I SAID I WOULD AND I WILL.

1964
01:12:37,220 --> 01:12:39,757
[SERVO MIMICS AUCTIONEER]

1965
01:12:39,790 --> 01:12:41,225
--AND LAY LOW FOR
THE REST OF THE DAY.

1966
01:12:41,258 --> 01:12:42,692
AT 11:00 TONIGHT,
MEET THE BOYS

1967
01:12:42,725 --> 01:12:43,960
- AT SIXTH AND KENT STREET.

1968
01:12:43,993 --> 01:12:45,462
-AND THEN WHAT?
- I'LL HAVE SOME MONEY FOR YOU,

1969
01:12:45,495 --> 01:12:46,663
- AND THEY'LL
SLIP YOU OUT OF TOWN.
- THEN WHAT?

1970
01:12:46,697 --> 01:12:47,730
AFTER A FEW WEEKS,
WHEN IT BLOWS OVER,

1971
01:12:47,763 --> 01:12:49,032
- YOU CAN COME BACK.
- THEN WHAT?

1972
01:12:49,065 --> 01:12:50,333
OKAY, I'LL BE THERE.

1973
01:12:50,367 --> 01:12:51,535
AS LONG AS I TALK REALLY FAST
AND DO WHAT HE SAYS,

1974
01:12:51,568 --> 01:12:54,237
I'M GONNA BE OKAY.

1975
01:12:54,270 --> 01:12:56,173
LIFE ON THE LAMB.

1976
01:12:56,207 --> 01:12:58,975
AN AFFORDABLE VACATION.

1977
01:12:59,008 --> 01:13:00,477
HE'S TAKEN TO
SELLING HIS ESSAYS

1978
01:13:00,510 --> 01:13:02,813
CHEAP ON THE STREET.

1979
01:13:05,648 --> 01:13:08,085
HERE, NOW, WHAT ARE YOU DOING
IN A COCTEAU FILM, BOY?

1980
01:13:08,118 --> 01:13:10,087
GO HOME TO YOUR MOTHER.
THAT'S A GOOD LAD.

1981
01:13:12,455 --> 01:13:14,223
WELL, THAT WAS A CLOSE ONE.

1982
01:13:14,257 --> 01:13:16,693
OOF.

1983
01:13:16,727 --> 01:13:18,762
WE'RE SUPPOSED
TO DEPROGRAM YOU.

1984
01:13:18,795 --> 01:13:20,463
- HAVE YOU GOT THE STUFF?
- IT'S ALL IN HERE.

1985
01:13:20,497 --> 01:13:21,932
LET'S GET BACK IN HERE,
SO NOBODY CAN SEE US.

1986
01:13:21,965 --> 01:13:23,133
OH, THAT SEEMS REASONABLE.

1987
01:13:23,167 --> 01:13:24,868
WALK BACK WITH A COUPLE
OF NICE FELLAS.

1988
01:13:24,902 --> 01:13:26,937
AND THEN ALL OF A SUDDEN,
YOU-- WHOA!

1989
01:13:29,072 --> 01:13:30,440
THIS IS A MESSAGE
FROM THE OTHER KIDS

1990
01:13:30,473 --> 01:13:32,708
IN THE ESSAY CONTEST, JIMMY.

1991
01:13:32,742 --> 01:13:35,245
SO I TOLD HER THAT
I LIKE PLAYTEX-- WHA?

1992
01:13:35,278 --> 01:13:37,680
HUH?

1993
01:13:37,713 --> 01:13:40,117
JIMMY'S REALLY FITTING IN WITH
THE OTHER GANGSTERS HIS AGE.

1994
01:13:40,150 --> 01:13:41,352
HEY, WAIT A MINUTE,
SOMEBODY'S COMING.

1995
01:13:41,385 --> 01:13:42,618
- LET'S GET OUT OF HERE.
- MOBSTERS

1996
01:13:42,652 --> 01:13:44,955
ARE EASILY SCARED.

1997
01:13:44,988 --> 01:13:47,623
WAIT, I FORGOT TO GIVE YOU
THE STUFF HERE.

1998
01:13:50,527 --> 01:13:52,162
WHAT'S A MATTER, KID?
WHAT HAPPENED TO YOU?

1999
01:13:52,195 --> 01:13:54,230
- I DON'T KNOW.
- YOU'D BETTER
COME ALONG WITH US.

2000
01:13:54,263 --> 01:13:55,398
WE'LL REPORT IT
TO THE POLICE.

2001
01:13:55,432 --> 01:13:56,600
NO, NO, FELLAS, JUST--

2002
01:13:56,633 --> 01:13:58,102
JUST HELP ME FIND A CAB,
WILL YOU?

2003
01:13:58,135 --> 01:14:00,503
- I WANNA GO HOME.
- OKAY, KID, JUST AS YOU SAY.

2004
01:14:00,537 --> 01:14:02,405
ALFRED ON THE SPOT.

2005
01:14:05,775 --> 01:14:07,243
MOM? DAD?

2006
01:14:07,277 --> 01:14:09,378
I WON THE "GET THE CRAP
KICKED OUT OF YOU" CONTEST!

2007
01:14:09,412 --> 01:14:11,548
MOM? DAD?

2008
01:14:11,582 --> 01:14:13,317
I'M UP HERE, HONEY,
WITH THE DT'S!

2009
01:14:13,350 --> 01:14:15,418
COULD YOU GET THE YELLOW LIZARD
OUT OF THE BATHROOM?

2010
01:14:18,255 --> 01:14:19,723
UH, WHERE'S THE DEXEDRINE?

2011
01:14:19,757 --> 01:14:22,625
WHERE'S THAT DEXEDRINE?

2012
01:14:22,658 --> 01:14:24,895
IF KNICK-KNACKS
RULED THE WORLD.

2013
01:14:28,832 --> 01:14:30,300
- [PHONE RINGS]
- MEANWHILE,

2014
01:14:30,333 --> 01:14:31,768
AT BLACK PANTHER
HEADQUARTERS.

2015
01:14:31,802 --> 01:14:35,005
I'LL SEE. WHAT HAVE YOU GOT?

2016
01:14:35,038 --> 01:14:36,307
[SERVO] YYYYES?

2017
01:14:36,340 --> 01:14:38,408
HELLO. YES, SIR?

2018
01:14:38,442 --> 01:14:40,410
MR. WILSON IN?
TELL HIM HIS SON WANTS HIM.

2019
01:14:40,443 --> 01:14:42,378
JUST A MINUTE, I'LL SEE.

2020
01:14:42,412 --> 01:14:44,180
OLLIE, TELEPHONE.

2021
01:14:44,213 --> 01:14:45,682
I'VE NEVER HAD SUCH LUCK.

2022
01:14:45,715 --> 01:14:47,817
- MURRAY, USE A COASTER.
- --YOU BEAT ME EVERY HAND.

2023
01:14:47,850 --> 01:14:49,452
YOUR BOY'S ON THE PHONE,
MR. WILSON.

2024
01:14:49,485 --> 01:14:51,388
- HE WANTS TO TALK TO YOU.
- TELL HIM I'M NOT HERE.

2025
01:14:51,422 --> 01:14:53,023
BUT YOU ARE-- OH.

2026
01:14:53,057 --> 01:14:55,758
- COME ON, DEAL.
- YES, SIR.

2027
01:14:55,792 --> 01:14:57,093
HE SAYS HE'S NOT HERE.

2028
01:14:57,127 --> 01:14:59,563
I'M SORRY, SIR,
BUT YOUR FATHER ISN'T HERE.

2029
01:14:59,597 --> 01:15:03,200
WELL, IF HE COMES IN,
TELL HIM I CALLED, WILL YOU?

2030
01:15:03,233 --> 01:15:05,002
UH, I WONDER WHO THAT WAS
IN THE BACKGROUND.

2031
01:15:05,035 --> 01:15:07,737
OH, WELL. MOM!

2032
01:15:07,770 --> 01:15:09,907
[CROW SOBS] I'M JUST
GONNA RUN AWAY!

2033
01:15:12,943 --> 01:15:15,012
I GOT PEANUT BUTTER.
AND UNDERWEAR.

2034
01:15:15,045 --> 01:15:17,915
AND THAT'S ALL I NEED!

2035
01:15:17,948 --> 01:15:20,150
[JOEL SOBS] WELL, I'M GONNA
RUN AWAY TO KANSAS

2036
01:15:20,183 --> 01:15:22,452
AND BECOME A VENTRILOQUIST.

2037
01:15:25,955 --> 01:15:27,490
[CROW SOBS]

2038
01:15:27,523 --> 01:15:29,225
OH, WAIT A MINUTE.

2039
01:15:29,258 --> 01:15:31,928
WHERE'S MY TROWEL-SIZED
PERT SHAMPOO?

2040
01:15:31,962 --> 01:15:33,630
JIMMY IS SUDDENLY SEIZED

2041
01:15:33,663 --> 01:15:37,200
WITH AN ESSAY IDEA.

2042
01:15:37,233 --> 01:15:40,570
SAY, THAT'S WHAT HAPPENED
TO ALL HIS OTHER MOMS.

2043
01:15:46,343 --> 01:15:48,212
"PROBLEM WITH MOB. ON LAMB.

2044
01:15:48,245 --> 01:15:51,147
ACCUSINGLY YOURS,
JIMMY."

2045
01:15:51,180 --> 01:15:53,317
"P.S. HOPE YOU HAD FUN

2046
01:15:53,350 --> 01:15:55,618
AT JACK TAYLOR'S."

2047
01:15:59,088 --> 01:16:01,492
WOULD YOU COMB YOUR HAIR?
THAT'S ANNOYING.

2048
01:16:01,525 --> 01:16:04,160
I'LL JUST PUT THIS OVER HERE
WITH MOM'S SUICIDE NOTE.

2049
01:16:05,562 --> 01:16:08,398
OH, THEY'LL THINK
IT'S A COCKTAIL NAPKIN.

2050
01:16:10,600 --> 01:16:13,303
I SAW SOME KICK-ASS
PARTIES HERE.

2051
01:16:17,340 --> 01:16:20,910
♪♪ [ALL SING "BOOTS ARE
MADE FOR WALKING" INTRO]

2052
01:16:24,047 --> 01:16:26,215
MORE POWERFUL
THAN A LOCOMOTIVE!

2053
01:16:30,320 --> 01:16:32,255
AUNTIE EM! AUNTIE EM!

2054
01:16:36,058 --> 01:16:38,895
- WHAT, IS HE THINKING
ABOUT TRAINS NOW?
- UH, YEAH.

2055
01:16:38,928 --> 01:16:41,498
THESE TRAINS NEVER
STOP FOR YOU.

2056
01:16:41,532 --> 01:16:42,865
AH, BUT HE'S ABLE TO...

2057
01:16:42,898 --> 01:16:46,403
PICK UP A RIDE
WITH THE JOAD FAMILY.

2058
01:16:46,437 --> 01:16:49,005
THIS IS THE LIFE.

2059
01:16:49,038 --> 01:16:50,873
[JOEL LAUGHS]

2060
01:16:53,343 --> 01:16:55,612
MAYBE I'LL TRAVEL SOMEWHERE.

2061
01:17:01,083 --> 01:17:02,585
HEY, CAFE.

2062
01:17:02,618 --> 01:17:04,353
I'VE HEARD OF THIS PLACE.

2063
01:17:06,823 --> 01:17:08,625
I DON'T KNOW IF I'LL FIND
ANY THAI FOOD

2064
01:17:08,658 --> 01:17:10,227
IN THIS OLD TOWN.

2065
01:17:12,628 --> 01:17:14,732
HEY, MAYBE THEY'LL SEE ME
LOOKING DEJECTED

2066
01:17:14,765 --> 01:17:18,235
AND INVITE ME IN.

2067
01:17:18,268 --> 01:17:20,903
ON TOP OF IT ALL,
MY AREA'S GONE.

2068
01:17:24,407 --> 01:17:25,675
BOY, THAT WAS GOOD STUFF.

2069
01:17:25,708 --> 01:17:27,377
I GOTTA LEARN TO ORDER
ONLY ONE CHICKEN.

2070
01:17:27,410 --> 01:17:29,378
OH, AND THAT
WHIPPED CREAM? MMM.

2071
01:17:32,915 --> 01:17:34,818
ONE MILLION, TWO MILLION.

2072
01:17:34,852 --> 01:17:37,720
THREE MILLION, FOUR MILLION.

2073
01:17:39,655 --> 01:17:43,293
14 BILLION, 15 BILLION.

2074
01:17:43,327 --> 01:17:45,828
I'VE DECIDED-- I'M GONNA
DO SOMETHING REALLY STUPID.

2075
01:17:52,035 --> 01:17:55,105
UM, UH, CAN I ROB YOU?

2076
01:17:55,138 --> 01:17:56,840
- CUP OF COFFEE.
- YOU BET.

2077
01:17:56,873 --> 01:17:59,777
AND PUT THE FRENCH SILK PIE
IN AN UNMARKED BAG.

2078
01:17:59,810 --> 01:18:01,143
EXPECTING SOMEBODY?

2079
01:18:01,177 --> 01:18:03,280
- NO.
- I DIDN'T KNOW IT WAS DRUGS!

2080
01:18:06,817 --> 01:18:08,685
UH, DO YOU HAVE ANY BULLETS?

2081
01:18:08,718 --> 01:18:10,087
HOW ABOUT A HAMBURGER?

2082
01:18:10,120 --> 01:18:11,320
IT'S WHAT'S FOR DINNER.

2083
01:18:11,353 --> 01:18:12,855
NO THANKS, I'M NOT HUNGRY.

2084
01:18:12,888 --> 01:18:14,423
IF YOU'RE BROKE,
IT'S ON THE HOUSE.

2085
01:18:14,457 --> 01:18:16,560
HEY, IT'S OFFICER TOOTIE.

2086
01:18:16,593 --> 01:18:18,528
PLENTY OF ONIONS, EH?

2087
01:18:18,562 --> 01:18:20,230
FRENCH FRIES,
AND ALL THE TRIMMINGS.

2088
01:18:20,263 --> 01:18:22,798
I'LL TRUST YOU.
YOU CAN PAY ME ANYTIME YOU WANT.

2089
01:18:22,832 --> 01:18:25,302
- OOH OOH.
- OKAY.

2090
01:18:25,335 --> 01:18:28,572
DID SOMEONE TELL YOU
IT WAS MY BIRTHDAY?

2091
01:18:28,605 --> 01:18:32,208
YOU LIKE MY HAT? I MADE IT.

2092
01:18:32,242 --> 01:18:34,143
GIVE AND TAKE,
THAT'S MY SYSTEM.

2093
01:18:34,177 --> 01:18:36,045
- YEP.
- SHARE WHAT YOU'VE GOT,

2094
01:18:36,078 --> 01:18:37,947
AND YOU'LL NEVER WANT.

2095
01:18:37,980 --> 01:18:40,350
I'VE HAD A LOT OF GUYS
COME IN HERE BROKE.

2096
01:18:40,383 --> 01:18:41,852
NEVER SENT 'EM AWAY HUNGRY.

2097
01:18:41,885 --> 01:18:43,220
GOT 'EM PILED OUT BACK.

2098
01:18:43,253 --> 01:18:45,222
AND I DON'T LOSE
BY IT EITHER.

2099
01:18:45,255 --> 01:18:47,323
THEY ALWAYS
COME BACK AND PAY.

2100
01:18:47,357 --> 01:18:48,792
MOST PEOPLE ARE OKAY.

2101
01:18:48,825 --> 01:18:50,993
EXCEPT FOR YOU, OF COURSE.

2102
01:18:51,027 --> 01:18:53,630
HERE, STAB THIS
INTO YOUR THIGH.

2103
01:18:53,663 --> 01:18:56,633
YOU'RE NOT GONNA
HUG ME, ARE YOU?

2104
01:18:56,667 --> 01:18:58,100
BETTER GIVE ME
THAT GUN, SON.

2105
01:18:58,133 --> 01:18:59,668
YOU CAN'T EAT WITH ONE HAND.

2106
01:18:59,702 --> 01:19:02,172
ACTUALLY, YOU CAN, BUT I'LL
GIVE YOU THE GUN ANYWAY.

2107
01:19:04,507 --> 01:19:06,843
WAIT A MINUTE,
THIS IS AN EPISODE OF INSIGHT.

2108
01:19:06,877 --> 01:19:08,145
YEP.

2109
01:19:08,178 --> 01:19:10,447
I SAW IT ON YOUR FACE
WHEN YOU FIRST CAME IN HERE.

2110
01:19:10,480 --> 01:19:11,982
I CAN READ YOUR
CHAKRAS, TOO.

2111
01:19:12,015 --> 01:19:13,350
--BEEN AROUND.

2112
01:19:13,383 --> 01:19:16,052
- SEEN ALL SORTS IN MY TIME.
- BUT THEY DON'T SEE ME.

2113
01:19:16,085 --> 01:19:18,155
YOU LEARN THINGS ABOUT PEOPLE
IN THIS BUSINESS.

2114
01:19:18,188 --> 01:19:20,290
FOR INSTANCE,
THEY'RE BIPEDS.

2115
01:19:20,323 --> 01:19:22,892
MMM, LOADED TOO.

2116
01:19:22,925 --> 01:19:25,062
THAT'S DANGEROUS.

2117
01:19:25,095 --> 01:19:27,030
LOOK, CAN I HAVE
MY HAMBURGER?

2118
01:19:27,063 --> 01:19:28,965
YOU KNOW, SOME GUYS GET SORE

2119
01:19:28,998 --> 01:19:30,567
WHEN YOU PULL A GUN ON 'EM.

2120
01:19:30,600 --> 01:19:33,002
AND THEY DON'T
STOP TO THINK.

2121
01:19:33,035 --> 01:19:34,537
WHY, YOU MIGHT'VE
EVEN KILLED ME.

2122
01:19:34,570 --> 01:19:36,607
NOT MEANING IT, EITHER.

2123
01:19:36,640 --> 01:19:39,208
- SUCH THINGS HAPPEN.
- I KNOW.

2124
01:19:39,242 --> 01:19:42,645
BETTER PUT THIS AWAY BEFORE
SOMEBODY COMES IN AND SEES IT.

2125
01:19:43,780 --> 01:19:45,182
WOULD YOU GET ME
MY HAMBURGER?

2126
01:19:45,215 --> 01:19:46,983
OKAY, I'LL KEEP IT FOR YOU.

2127
01:19:47,017 --> 01:19:48,418
YOU CAN HAVE IT
ANYTIME YOU WANT.

2128
01:19:48,452 --> 01:19:50,353
[ALL] AT ALICE'S RESTAURANT.

2129
01:19:57,227 --> 01:19:58,728
FUNNY THING, YOU DROPPING
IN HERE THIS WAY.

2130
01:19:58,762 --> 01:20:01,632
- WHY?
- I'VE DREAMT OF YOUR
SOFT FEATURES.

2131
01:20:01,665 --> 01:20:04,100
--I'D LIKE TO HAVE A BOY
LIKE YOU TO HELP OUT HERE.

2132
01:20:04,133 --> 01:20:06,002
- WANT A JOB?
- SURE, I WANT A JOB.

2133
01:20:06,035 --> 01:20:07,903
YOU EVER WORKED
AS A BOY BEFORE?

2134
01:20:07,937 --> 01:20:09,705
--YOUR FOOD AND LODGINGS.

2135
01:20:09,738 --> 01:20:12,008
I GOT A SHACK HERE
IN BACK OF THE RESTAURANT.

2136
01:20:12,042 --> 01:20:13,877
- TAIN'T MUCH--
- IN FACT, IT SUCKS.

2137
01:20:13,910 --> 01:20:15,145
--COMFORTABLE ENOUGH.

2138
01:20:15,178 --> 01:20:18,282
RADIO, SOME FLOWERS
IN THE GARDEN, AND THE DOG.

2139
01:20:18,315 --> 01:20:20,250
- AND ME.
- WHAT DO YOU SAY?

2140
01:20:20,283 --> 01:20:21,450
GIVE ME MY GUN BACK.

2141
01:20:21,483 --> 01:20:22,852
--AN AWFUL CHANCE,
AREN'T YOU?

2142
01:20:22,885 --> 01:20:24,487
I MEAN, OFFERING ME
A JOB THIS WAY.

2143
01:20:24,520 --> 01:20:26,155
WITHOUT KNOWING
ANYTHING ABOUT ME?

2144
01:20:26,188 --> 01:20:27,990
YOU SEE, BEFORE I--

2145
01:20:28,023 --> 01:20:29,192
I GOTTA TELL YOU, THOUGH,

2146
01:20:29,225 --> 01:20:30,860
THERE'S ONE CONDITION
ATTACHED TO IT.

2147
01:20:30,893 --> 01:20:33,463
YOU HAVE TO GO TO CHURCH
WITH ME EVERY SUNDAY MORNING.

2148
01:20:33,497 --> 01:20:34,965
CHURCH?

2149
01:20:34,998 --> 01:20:37,100
- THAT'S RIGHT.
- FORGET IT!

2150
01:20:37,133 --> 01:20:38,735
--WEEK, I WORK FOR MYSELF.

2151
01:20:38,768 --> 01:20:42,272
ON THE SEVENTH,
I WORK FOR THE CHURCH.

2152
01:20:42,305 --> 01:20:43,573
I'M AN USHER.

2153
01:20:43,607 --> 01:20:45,608
IT WOULDN'T LOOK RIGHT,
YOU LIVING IN MY HOUSE

2154
01:20:45,642 --> 01:20:47,143
AND NOT GOING TO CHURCH.

2155
01:20:47,177 --> 01:20:49,980
OF COURSE, THAT'S ONLY
AN HOUR ON SUNDAY MORNINGS.

2156
01:20:50,013 --> 01:20:52,182
IN THE AFTERNOONS,
ON FINE DAYS,

2157
01:20:52,215 --> 01:20:53,783
- WE COULD GO FISHING.
- [ALL] AHH.

2158
01:20:53,817 --> 01:20:55,918
GEE, THAT SOUNDS SWELL.

2159
01:20:55,952 --> 01:20:57,587
OH, AND NO MOB TIES.

2160
01:20:57,620 --> 01:20:59,222
YOU'RE LEARNING FAST.

2161
01:20:59,255 --> 01:21:02,692
I'VE ENTERED
THE TWILIGHT ZONE.

2162
01:21:02,725 --> 01:21:05,062
HOW DO YOU LIKE
MY SWINGIN' CHURCH, SON?

2163
01:21:07,797 --> 01:21:11,602
♪ I'VE GOT A GOOFY HAT
ON MY HEAD ♪

2164
01:21:11,635 --> 01:21:13,370
♪ --I NEED YOU ♪

2165
01:21:13,403 --> 01:21:16,607
MICHELLE PFEIFFER
IN THE FABULOUS BAKER BOYS.

2166
01:21:16,640 --> 01:21:17,940
♪ WHERE CAN YOU BE? ♪

2167
01:21:17,973 --> 01:21:19,742
HE'S IN KANSAS,
FLIPPING BURGERS.

2168
01:21:19,775 --> 01:21:22,078
♪ I MISS YOU SO ♪

2169
01:21:22,112 --> 01:21:23,513
IT'S AN AIR FILTER PIANO.

2170
01:21:23,547 --> 01:21:25,982
♪ HOW I CRIED ♪

2171
01:21:26,015 --> 01:21:27,750
- ♪ AND TRIED ♪
- [SERVO BEAT-BOXES]

2172
01:21:27,783 --> 01:21:29,852
♪ LOOKING DOWN
THE LONELY STREET ♪

2173
01:21:29,885 --> 01:21:33,055
OH, SHE'S A REGULAR
KOKO TAYLOR. CHA-CHA.

2174
01:21:33,088 --> 01:21:34,423
OR IRREGULAR.

2175
01:21:34,457 --> 01:21:36,358
AND NOW SHE'S GOT A TABLE
CENTERPIECE ON HER HEAD.

2176
01:21:36,392 --> 01:21:38,060
♪ --RETURN HERE ♪

2177
01:21:38,093 --> 01:21:40,163
♪ HOW I LEARNED HERE-- ♪

2178
01:21:40,197 --> 01:21:41,430
NOW, LET'S SEE,
I'VE ORDERED THE DEATH

2179
01:21:41,463 --> 01:21:42,898
OF TEN, NO,
TWELVE PEOPLE TODAY.

2180
01:21:42,932 --> 01:21:44,067
PRETTY GOOD DAY.

2181
01:21:44,100 --> 01:21:45,735
♪ WHY DID YOU LEAVE ME-- ♪

2182
01:21:45,768 --> 01:21:48,738
♪ YOU TOLD HIM TO ♪

2183
01:21:48,772 --> 01:21:51,775
♪ DIDN'T YOU KNOW ♪

2184
01:21:51,808 --> 01:21:54,243
♪ I'D BE FORLORN-- ♪

2185
01:21:54,277 --> 01:21:55,912
♪ AND GREEN ♪

2186
01:21:55,945 --> 01:21:58,180
♪ NOW I HOPE ♪

2187
01:21:58,213 --> 01:22:00,250
♪ AND PRAY ♪

2188
01:22:00,283 --> 01:22:02,452
♪ THAT MAYBE SOMEDAY ♪

2189
01:22:02,485 --> 01:22:04,653
♪ I CAN SAY THAT I'M SORRY ♪

2190
01:22:04,687 --> 01:22:06,622
♪ PLEASE HEAR MY PLEA-- ♪

2191
01:22:06,655 --> 01:22:08,392
♪ NOT GUILTY! ♪

2192
01:22:08,425 --> 01:22:09,925
♪ WHERE CAN YOU BE? ♪

2193
01:22:09,958 --> 01:22:12,028
THE AUDIENCE
IS FRANKLY STUNNED.

2194
01:22:12,062 --> 01:22:14,430
♪ WHERE CAN YOU BE? ♪

2195
01:22:14,463 --> 01:22:17,967
[SERVO HARMONIZES]
♪ WHERE CAN YOU BE? ♪

2196
01:22:20,437 --> 01:22:22,038
"WHERE CAN YOU BE."

2197
01:22:22,072 --> 01:22:23,573
LAST CALL,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.

2198
01:22:23,607 --> 01:22:27,210
LAST CALL.

2199
01:22:27,243 --> 01:22:28,612
YOU WERE SWELL
IN THAT, KITTEN.

2200
01:22:28,645 --> 01:22:30,913
- [SERVO MEOWS]
- THANKS.

2201
01:22:30,947 --> 01:22:33,115
STILL THINKING
ABOUT JIMMY, HUH?

2202
01:22:33,148 --> 01:22:34,417
WHAT MAKES YOU THINK THAT?

2203
01:22:34,450 --> 01:22:36,352
OH, MAYBE THE WAY
YOU SANG THAT SONG.

2204
01:22:36,385 --> 01:22:38,020
OH, NOW, LOOK, KITTEN,
I KNOW YOU'VE BEEN--

2205
01:22:38,053 --> 01:22:39,388
- MEOW.
- --SEARCHING FOR THAT KID
FOR TWO MONTHS.

2206
01:22:39,422 --> 01:22:40,657
WHY DON'T YOU GIVE IT UP?

2207
01:22:40,690 --> 01:22:42,558
HE'S PROBABLY
A THOUSAND MILES FROM HERE.

2208
01:22:42,592 --> 01:22:43,827
I'LL TELL YOU WHAT WE'LL DO.

2209
01:22:43,860 --> 01:22:45,062
WHEN YOU GET THROUGH TONIGHT,
WE'LL GO OUT

2210
01:22:45,095 --> 01:22:46,997
AND PAINT THE TOWN.
YOU NEED SOME RECREATION.

2211
01:22:47,030 --> 01:22:48,732
I'LL KILL SOMEBODY FOR YOU.
WHO DO YOU WANT KILLED?

2212
01:22:48,765 --> 01:22:50,200
OKAY, CHARLIE.

2213
01:22:52,902 --> 01:22:54,937
HO, WHAT A CABOOSE. HOO-HAH.

2214
01:22:57,773 --> 01:22:59,875
SON, IT'S BEEN TWO MONTHS,

2215
01:22:59,908 --> 01:23:02,445
AND YOU HAVEN'T TOUCHED
YOUR HAMBURGER.

2216
01:23:02,478 --> 01:23:04,780
SIR, I JUST DON'T
UNDERSTAND THE HOLY SPIRIT.

2217
01:23:04,813 --> 01:23:06,148
IS IT A BIRD?

2218
01:23:06,182 --> 01:23:08,317
WHAT'S THE MATTER?
NOT HUNGRY?

2219
01:23:08,350 --> 01:23:10,220
HOW COME I'M
THE ONLY CUSTOMER?

2220
01:23:10,253 --> 01:23:12,288
SOMETHING'S BOTHERING YOU.

2221
01:23:12,322 --> 01:23:14,190
- WHAT IS IT? HOMESICK?
- UHH.

2222
01:23:14,223 --> 01:23:16,625
- NO.
- I FOUND A TOENAIL
IN MY HAMBURGER.

2223
01:23:16,658 --> 01:23:18,227
I THOUGHT YOU LIKED IT HERE
PRETTY WELL.

2224
01:23:18,260 --> 01:23:19,395
SEEM TO BE SETTLING DOWN.

2225
01:23:19,428 --> 01:23:21,230
I DO LIKE IT, AL.
IT'S NOT THAT.

2226
01:23:21,263 --> 01:23:23,298
IN FACT, IT'S THE ONLY TIME
I'VE EVER REALLY BEEN HAPPY.

2227
01:23:23,332 --> 01:23:25,302
BUT I WANT A SALAD.
IS THAT ASKING TOO MUCH?

2228
01:23:25,335 --> 01:23:28,170
SPILL IT, SON,
YOU CAN TELL ME.

2229
01:23:28,203 --> 01:23:29,572
WELL, IT'S-- IT'S JUST
THAT I'VE BEEN

2230
01:23:29,605 --> 01:23:30,973
THINKING THINGS OVER,
THAT'S ALL.

2231
01:23:31,007 --> 01:23:32,308
- AND I WANT NEW CURTAINS.
- YOU WANNA GO BACK

2232
01:23:32,342 --> 01:23:34,243
AND STRAIGHTEN YOURSELF OUT?

2233
01:23:34,277 --> 01:23:36,880
SQUARE ACCOUNTS?
TAKE THE LOAD OFF YOUR MIND?

2234
01:23:36,913 --> 01:23:38,147
YEAH, I GUESS THAT'S IT.

2235
01:23:38,180 --> 01:23:39,948
BRING YOUR TROUSERS
IN FOR DRY-CLEANING?

2236
01:23:39,982 --> 01:23:41,250
FIND THE COURAGE TO DO IT.

2237
01:23:41,283 --> 01:23:42,418
CHANGE THAT OLD UNDERWEAR?

2238
01:23:42,452 --> 01:23:43,687
WOULD YOU HELP ME, AL?

2239
01:23:43,720 --> 01:23:45,020
AND DON'T MENTION GOD.

2240
01:23:45,053 --> 01:23:47,023
I'VE BEEN WAITING
TO HEAR YOU SAY THAT, SON.

2241
01:23:47,057 --> 01:23:49,058
SO I PREPARED A SONG.

2242
01:23:49,092 --> 01:23:51,293
WE'LL GO BACK
AND FACE IT TOGETHER.

2243
01:23:51,327 --> 01:23:52,762
AFTER THEY HEAR YOUR STORY,

2244
01:23:52,795 --> 01:23:54,963
I'M POSITIVE THEY'LL
GIVE YOU A BREAK.

2245
01:23:54,997 --> 01:23:56,398
DON'T WORRY.

2246
01:23:56,432 --> 01:23:57,600
AH, GEE, THAT'S SWELL.

2247
01:23:57,633 --> 01:23:59,068
WELL, I FEEL BETTER ALREADY.

2248
01:23:59,102 --> 01:24:01,772
NOW TUCK IN TO THAT BEEF.

2249
01:24:01,805 --> 01:24:04,107
YOU SEE, MISS REED, I COULDN'T
LET JIMMY GIVE HIMSELF UP

2250
01:24:04,140 --> 01:24:06,375
UNLESS HE'D SEEN YOU FIRST.

2251
01:24:06,408 --> 01:24:08,678
- OKAY. LET'S GO.
- AND I WANTED TO SEE
YOU TOO, JIMMY.

2252
01:24:08,712 --> 01:24:10,247
TO EXPLAIN
AND TELL YOU THE TRUTH--

2253
01:24:10,280 --> 01:24:11,848
- I NEVER WORE THE SHOES.
- BLAKE WAS IN

2254
01:24:11,882 --> 01:24:13,382
THE OTHER ROOM THAT NIGHT,
LISTENING.

2255
01:24:13,415 --> 01:24:15,285
I HAD TO SAY WHAT I DID,
OR HE'D'VE KILLED YOU.

2256
01:24:15,318 --> 01:24:18,220
- HUH.
- THEY TRIED TO THE NIGHT
THEY BEAT YOU UP.

2257
01:24:18,253 --> 01:24:20,490
AND, THEN, THE THINGS
YOU SAID WEREN'T TRUE.

2258
01:24:20,523 --> 01:24:22,025
OF COURSE THEY WEREN'T TRUE.

2259
01:24:22,058 --> 01:24:24,560
EXCEPT FOR ABOUT
YOUR LOUSY SHOE CAREER.

2260
01:24:24,593 --> 01:24:25,962
OH, JIMMY, BLAKE'S THE CAUSE

2261
01:24:25,995 --> 01:24:27,530
OF ALL YOUR TROUBLE
AND MINE, TOO.

2262
01:24:27,563 --> 01:24:29,965
IF HE FINDS OUT YOU'RE HERE,
HE'LL KILL US BOTH.

2263
01:24:29,998 --> 01:24:32,002
NO, HE WON'T, BECAUSE HE'S GOING
TO THE POLICE STATION WITH ME.

2264
01:24:32,035 --> 01:24:33,603
YOU AND AL CAN CALL THE COPS
AND FOLLOW US.

2265
01:24:33,637 --> 01:24:34,937
JIMMY, WAIT! JIMMY!

2266
01:24:34,970 --> 01:24:36,038
QUACK, QUACK, QUACK QUACK.

2267
01:24:36,072 --> 01:24:38,942
AGAIN, PROVING
JUST HOW STUPID HE IS.

2268
01:24:38,975 --> 01:24:42,245
SO, HOW ABOUT A LITTLE SUGAR
FOR HAPPY CHEF OVER HERE?

2269
01:24:42,278 --> 01:24:43,580
ORGANIZED CRIME,
PLEASE HOLD.

2270
01:24:43,613 --> 01:24:45,248
ORGANIZED CRIME,
PLEASE HOLD-- SIR?

2271
01:24:48,117 --> 01:24:50,687
LET ME GUESS.
IT'S YOUR BIRTHDAY.

2272
01:24:50,720 --> 01:24:52,722
- HELLO, JIMMY.
- HOW'S YOUR HAT? [CHUCKLES]

2273
01:24:52,755 --> 01:24:54,523
WHAT BRINGS YOU TO SEE ME?

2274
01:24:54,557 --> 01:24:56,192
NOT IN TROUBLE AGAIN, ARE YOU?

2275
01:24:56,225 --> 01:24:57,593
NO, BUT YOU ARE.

2276
01:24:57,627 --> 01:24:58,962
I'M GIVING MYSELF UP
TO THE POLICE,

2277
01:24:58,995 --> 01:25:00,563
AND YOU'RE COMING WITH ME.

2278
01:25:00,597 --> 01:25:01,898
YOU'RE TAKING A LOT
FOR GRANTED, AREN'T YOU?

2279
01:25:01,932 --> 01:25:03,432
MAYBE I AM.

2280
01:25:03,465 --> 01:25:06,202
BUT YOU'RE GONNA TELL EVERYTHING
THAT'S HAPPENED BETWEEN US.

2281
01:25:06,235 --> 01:25:07,937
- AND IF I DON'T?
- YOU'LL KILL ME?

2282
01:25:07,970 --> 01:25:09,972
THE POLICE ARE ON THEIR WAY
HERE TO SEE THAT YOU DO.

2283
01:25:10,005 --> 01:25:11,773
NOW, LET'S SEE,
DID I CALL THEM?... RIGHT.

2284
01:25:11,807 --> 01:25:14,677
OKAY, JIMMY.

2285
01:25:14,710 --> 01:25:18,047
ABOUT TIME I WENT ON THE
STRAIGHT AND NARR-- HI-KEEBA!

2286
01:25:18,080 --> 01:25:21,885
WELL, THAT'S
A WEIRD POSITION.

2287
01:25:21,918 --> 01:25:25,688
THEY'RE REALLY
GOING TO TOWN IN THERE.

2288
01:25:25,722 --> 01:25:28,023
HEY, DOES ANYONE
HAVE AN APPOINTMENT?

2289
01:25:31,293 --> 01:25:32,428
[GUNSHOT]

2290
01:25:32,462 --> 01:25:35,030
HIS HEART JUST EXPLODED.

2291
01:25:35,063 --> 01:25:36,765
WELL, SO MUCH FOR THE WHOLE

2292
01:25:36,798 --> 01:25:38,635
"HE'S COMING WITH ME"
SCENARIO.

2293
01:25:41,337 --> 01:25:43,472
UH, I ACCUSE MY PARENTS.

2294
01:25:45,375 --> 01:25:47,277
I TRIED TO TAKE THE GUN
AWAY FROM HIM.

2295
01:25:47,310 --> 01:25:50,178
- BUT IT WENT OFF.
- HUH?

2296
01:25:50,212 --> 01:25:52,348
OH, I KNOW I'VE LIED.
I'VE CHEATED.

2297
01:25:52,382 --> 01:25:55,318
- I'VE DONE A LOT OF THINGS
THAT I SHOULDN'T HAVE DONE.
- AND MORE.

2298
01:25:55,352 --> 01:25:57,887
BUT MAYBE I WOULDN'T HAVE
STARTED LYING TO MY SCHOOLMATES

2299
01:25:57,920 --> 01:26:00,423
IF I HADN'T BEEN ASHAMED
OF MY HOME LIFE.

2300
01:26:00,457 --> 01:26:03,358
IF I HADN'T BEEN ASHAMED
THAT MY PARENTS WERE--

2301
01:26:03,392 --> 01:26:06,628
- WERE DENYING--
- THIS IS WILD.

2302
01:26:06,662 --> 01:26:10,433
--THE LOVE AND PROTECTION
THAT A BOY NEEDS.

2303
01:26:10,467 --> 01:26:11,902
THE GUIDANCE
THAT SETS HIM STRAIGHT.

2304
01:26:11,935 --> 01:26:15,170
MAYBE THEY SHOULD'VE
SWORN HIM IN.

2305
01:26:15,203 --> 01:26:17,073
AND THAT'S WHY...

2306
01:26:17,107 --> 01:26:18,742
I ACCUSE MY PARENTS.

2307
01:26:18,775 --> 01:26:21,143
[ALL] AAH. OH.

2308
01:26:21,177 --> 01:26:22,978
IS YOUR HAT FLASK EMPTY YET?

2309
01:26:23,012 --> 01:26:24,880
THAT COURT REPORTER
IS DREAMY.

2310
01:26:27,017 --> 01:26:29,018
SEEING AS IT'S YOUR BIRTHDAY,
WE'LL LET YOU GO.

2311
01:26:29,052 --> 01:26:30,953
- JAMES WILSON--
- YOU DUMMY.

2312
01:26:30,987 --> 01:26:33,823
YOUR STORY IS SUPPORTED BY MUCH
OF THE EVIDENCE IN THIS CASE.

2313
01:26:33,857 --> 01:26:36,525
AND I THINK INDICATES CLEARLY
THAT YOU ARE NOT GUILTY

2314
01:26:36,558 --> 01:26:38,027
OF THE KILLING
OF CHARLES BLAKE.

2315
01:26:38,060 --> 01:26:39,362
THANKS! WELL, BYE.

2316
01:26:39,395 --> 01:26:40,797
--COUNT I FIND YOU
NOT GUILTY.

2317
01:26:40,830 --> 01:26:42,798
[CROWD MURMURS]

2318
01:26:42,832 --> 01:26:44,767
HUH-- OH. OH, "NOT" GUILTY!

2319
01:26:44,800 --> 01:26:47,170
- OH.
- ON THE REMAINING COUNTS

2320
01:26:47,203 --> 01:26:48,872
OF HAVING AIDED AND ABETTED

2321
01:26:48,905 --> 01:26:50,507
IN THE TRANSPORTATION
AND CONCEALMENT

2322
01:26:50,540 --> 01:26:51,607
OF STOLEN PROPERTY,

2323
01:26:51,640 --> 01:26:53,308
- UH-OH.
- I FIND YOU GUILTY

2324
01:26:53,342 --> 01:26:55,545
AND SENTENCE YOU
TO FIVE YEARS IN STATE PRISON.

2325
01:26:55,578 --> 01:26:56,912
HEY, MY DAD WENT THERE.

2326
01:26:56,945 --> 01:26:58,513
THAT SENTENCE
IS HEREBY SUSPENDED.

2327
01:26:58,547 --> 01:27:00,650
AND YOU ARE PLACED
ON PROBATION FOR TWO YEARS.

2328
01:27:00,683 --> 01:27:02,452
- THANK GOD I'M WHITE!
- YOU ARE TO REMAIN IN

2329
01:27:02,485 --> 01:27:05,020
THE CUSTODY OF YOUR PARENTS
UNTIL YOU ARE 21.

2330
01:27:05,053 --> 01:27:06,322
DURING WHICH TIME I HOPE

2331
01:27:06,355 --> 01:27:07,823
THAT YOU WILL
JUSTIFY THE CONFIDENCE

2332
01:27:07,857 --> 01:27:09,158
- I AM PLACING IN YOU.
- HAH!

2333
01:27:09,192 --> 01:27:10,493
I WILL, YOUR HONOR.

2334
01:27:10,527 --> 01:27:13,595
OH, LET'S GO TO JACK TAYLOR'S
AND CELEBRATE.

2335
01:27:13,628 --> 01:27:15,063
- JIMMY!
- WAIT, WAIT,

2336
01:27:15,097 --> 01:27:17,433
HE HAS TO TALK
TO DOUG LLEWELYN FIRST.

2337
01:27:23,172 --> 01:27:24,707
HE ACCUSED US.

2338
01:27:24,740 --> 01:27:27,577
WHY DON'T YOU JUST
DO IT ON THE BENCH?

2339
01:27:27,610 --> 01:27:29,612
AS FOR YOU,
MR. AND MRS. WILSON.

2340
01:27:29,645 --> 01:27:31,380
YOU ARE NOT ON TRIAL HERE.

2341
01:27:31,413 --> 01:27:33,548
BUT YOU HAVE SEEN
THE TRAGEDY BROUGHT ABOUT

2342
01:27:33,582 --> 01:27:35,318
BY THE NEGLECT
YOUR BOY SUFFERED.

2343
01:27:35,352 --> 01:27:36,785
YOU WILL ROAST IN HELL.

2344
01:27:36,818 --> 01:27:38,788
--THE ONLY PARENTS
GUILTY OF SUCH NEGLECT.

2345
01:27:38,822 --> 01:27:41,323
- I SPEAK
TO PARENTS EVERYWHERE--
- MESSAGE COMING IN!

2346
01:27:41,357 --> 01:27:43,025
- THERE IT IS.
- IN THE PURSUIT
OF YOUR OWN

2347
01:27:43,058 --> 01:27:44,760
--OWN PLEASURES
AND OCCUPATIONS,

2348
01:27:44,793 --> 01:27:46,428
YOU NEGLECT YOUR CHILDREN.

2349
01:27:46,462 --> 01:27:48,530
REALIZE NOW
BEFORE IT IS TOO LATE.

2350
01:27:48,563 --> 01:27:50,633
- BUY BONDS.
- THIS MIGHT HAVE BEEN YOUR BOY.

2351
01:27:50,667 --> 01:27:51,767
NOT THAT YOUR BOY WOULD BE

2352
01:27:51,800 --> 01:27:53,670
QUITE SO THICK-HEADED
AS JIMMY.

2353
01:27:53,703 --> 01:27:55,372
I ACCUSE MY PARENTS

2354
01:27:55,405 --> 01:27:58,607
BROUGHT TO YOU
BY BOONE'S FARM.

2355
01:27:58,640 --> 01:28:01,277
THE MAKERS OF THIS FILM
ALSO ACCUSE HITLER

2356
01:28:01,310 --> 01:28:03,112
AND TOJO AND MUSSOLINI!

2357
01:28:03,145 --> 01:28:05,280
WE ACCUSE THEM ALL.
SOON WE'LL ACCUSE STALIN.

2358
01:28:05,313 --> 01:28:06,915
SERIOUSLY, JOEL,
WHO WOULD YOU ACCUSE?

2359
01:28:06,948 --> 01:28:09,985
OH, I DON'T REALLY...

2360
01:28:21,730 --> 01:28:24,400
OKAY, AS WE MOVE
INTO THE HOME STRETCH,

2361
01:28:24,433 --> 01:28:26,202
I THOUGHT IT'D BE NICE
TO READ A LETTER.

2362
01:28:26,235 --> 01:28:28,303
SO...

2363
01:28:28,337 --> 01:28:29,972
UH, HI, TOM. HI, CROW.

2364
01:28:30,005 --> 01:28:31,373
JUST GETTING READY
TO READ A LETTER.

2365
01:28:31,407 --> 01:28:33,075
OH, NO THANK YOU, THAT'S OKAY.

2366
01:28:33,108 --> 01:28:35,512
ALL WE'D LIKE IS
JUST A CUP OF COFFEE.

2367
01:28:35,545 --> 01:28:37,813
[COUGH] HAMBURGERS. [COUGH]

2368
01:28:37,847 --> 01:28:39,515
WELL, I'LL JUST GET GOING
ON THIS LETTER, THEN.

2369
01:28:39,548 --> 01:28:40,683
HAMBURGERS. [COUGH]

2370
01:28:40,717 --> 01:28:43,252
NO, NO THANKS.
WE'RE... NOT HUNGRY?

2371
01:28:43,285 --> 01:28:45,622
OH, I GET IT.
IT'S LIKE IN THE MOVIE.

2372
01:28:45,655 --> 01:28:48,257
HOW WOULD YOU BOYS
LIKE A HAMBURGER?

2373
01:28:48,290 --> 01:28:49,492
LIKE THAT?

2374
01:28:49,525 --> 01:28:51,627
FINALLY, WHAT
TOOK YOU SO LONG?

2375
01:28:51,660 --> 01:28:53,195
WHAT A MAROON.

2376
01:28:53,228 --> 01:28:54,830
NOW.

2377
01:28:54,863 --> 01:28:56,598
NOW WHAT?

2378
01:28:56,632 --> 01:28:58,067
- [BOTS SIGH]
- NO, NO, NO.

2379
01:28:58,100 --> 01:28:59,902
YOU STUPID, STUPID MAN.

2380
01:28:59,935 --> 01:29:01,203
NOW, YOU PRESENT US

2381
01:29:01,237 --> 01:29:03,538
WITH A BIG, BEEFY CHAR-BROILED
HAMBURGER "SAMMICH"

2382
01:29:03,572 --> 01:29:06,175
AND A FRENCH-FRIED POTATOES
GARNISH LIKE IN THE MOVIE.

2383
01:29:06,208 --> 01:29:08,443
UH, ALL I GOT
IS THIS POSTCARD.

2384
01:29:08,477 --> 01:29:10,312
D'OH. CROW, YOU TALK TO HIM.

2385
01:29:10,345 --> 01:29:12,815
YOU WERE SUPPOSED TO GET US

2386
01:29:12,848 --> 01:29:14,817
A CHAR-BROILED
HAMBURGER SANDWICH

2387
01:29:14,850 --> 01:29:16,018
LIKE IN THE MOVIE.

2388
01:29:16,052 --> 01:29:19,555
[SOBS] WHAT IS HAPPENING
TO THIS FAMILY?

2389
01:29:19,588 --> 01:29:21,057
COME ON, HONEY.
HONEY, HONEY.

2390
01:29:21,090 --> 01:29:22,858
THERE MUST BE A PIE COOLING
IN THE SHIP SOMEPLACE.

2391
01:29:22,892 --> 01:29:25,160
- A PIE?
- IT'S JUST A MOVIE, GUYS.

2392
01:29:25,193 --> 01:29:27,197
JEEZ.

2393
01:29:29,832 --> 01:29:31,133
ANYWAY.

2394
01:29:31,167 --> 01:29:33,202
THOUGHT WE COULD
READ THIS LETTER NOW.

2395
01:29:33,235 --> 01:29:34,903
UM, THIS SAYS,

2396
01:29:34,937 --> 01:29:37,038
"FOR RENT,
THE BARCO RAMMER."

2397
01:29:37,072 --> 01:29:38,842
AND IT'S FROM PETER SPEARS.

2398
01:29:38,875 --> 01:29:40,075
AND ON THE BACK HERE--

2399
01:29:40,108 --> 01:29:41,910
LET'S PUT THAT ON STILL STORE
IN THE BACK.

2400
01:29:41,943 --> 01:29:43,847
IT SAYS, "THE BARCO RAMMER.

2401
01:29:43,880 --> 01:29:45,548
"INDISPUTABLY THE FINEST.

2402
01:29:45,582 --> 01:29:48,317
"IT WILL RAM, IT WILL POUND,
IT WILL PRESS.

2403
01:29:48,350 --> 01:29:50,285
IT WILL DO WHAT
YOU WANT IT TO DO."

2404
01:29:50,318 --> 01:29:51,853
AND THEN
HE HUMOROUSLY WRITES,

2405
01:29:51,887 --> 01:29:53,857
"THE PERFECT DATE
FOR CROW AND TOM."

2406
01:29:53,890 --> 01:29:56,925
WHICH I THOUGHT
WAS PRETTY... FUNNY?

2407
01:29:56,958 --> 01:29:59,795
[TANK RATCHETS, CLANKS]

2408
01:30:02,632 --> 01:30:04,833
I ACCUSE YOU, JOEL.

2409
01:30:04,867 --> 01:30:07,035
NOW, CAREFULLY.

2410
01:30:07,068 --> 01:30:09,972
HAND OVER
THE HAMBURGER SANDWICH.

2411
01:30:12,040 --> 01:30:13,408
AHH.

2412
01:30:13,442 --> 01:30:14,610
DON'T LET HIM FORGET
THE FRENCH-FRIED

2413
01:30:14,643 --> 01:30:16,312
- POTATOES GARNISH.
- RIGHT.

2414
01:30:16,345 --> 01:30:19,015
JOEL, YOU MAGNIFICENT BASTARD!
I READ YOUR MENU!

2415
01:30:19,048 --> 01:30:21,150
COME ON, WE GOTTA BEAT
MIGHTY MESSINA, MAGGOT!

2416
01:30:21,183 --> 01:30:22,785
AAH.

2417
01:30:26,455 --> 01:30:28,090
UH, WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

2418
01:30:28,123 --> 01:30:30,660
[GLASS BREAKS]

2419
01:30:30,693 --> 01:30:33,395
[STRIPPER COUGHS]

2420
01:30:35,732 --> 01:30:37,633
UH, SORRY, JOEL.
DIDN'T CATCH THAT.

2421
01:30:37,667 --> 01:30:39,868
WE, UH, CAME THIS CLOSE
TO LOSING...

2422
01:30:39,902 --> 01:30:41,703
- RODNEY.
- RIGHT, RIGHT.

2423
01:30:41,737 --> 01:30:43,372
ALMOST LOST RODNEY.

2424
01:30:43,405 --> 01:30:44,907
IS THIS ENOUGH, DOCTOR F?

2425
01:30:44,940 --> 01:30:47,477
NO WAY, FRANK. THERE'S PLENTY
MORE FROSTING TO SHOVEL.

2426
01:30:47,510 --> 01:30:51,013
OH, JUST GO PUSH THE BUTTON,
YOU FREAKED-OUT MANIAC.

2427
01:30:51,047 --> 01:30:52,548
UH, LOOK, RODNEY.

2428
01:30:52,582 --> 01:30:54,883
I'M SORRY THIS WHOLE THING
GOT OUT OF HAND.

2429
01:30:54,917 --> 01:30:57,453
I'D LIKE TO MAKE IT
WORTH YOUR WHILE.

2430
01:30:57,487 --> 01:30:59,288
OH, NO, THAT'S--
THAT'S ALL RIGHT.

2431
01:30:59,322 --> 01:31:01,057
THAT-- YOU'VE DONE ENOUGH.

2432
01:32:04,287 --> 01:32:07,088
[DAD LAUGHS]

2433
01:32:08,223 --> 01:32:10,560
WELL, WHAT'S SO FUNNY?

2434
01:32:13,728 --> 01:32:15,397
THIS HAS BEEN
A PRESENTATION

2435
01:32:15,430 --> 01:32:16,998
FROM COMEDY CENTRAL.
